{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_427","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"GAME='Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- Task deliverables ---'; rg -n '(\"'^#|exit-interview|sourceInformation|testingFeedback|engineFeedback|promptFeedback|aiHub|400|standalone)'\"' TASK.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- Engine / networking specifications ---'; rg -n '(my-3dge|AI Hub|harness|hub-client|client 1\\\\.4|https?://|Animation|animation|noise|ghost|Dev Mode)' PLAN.md | head -100; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- Game source sizes ---'; wc -l \\\"\"'$GAME\"/*.{ts,css} \"$GAME\"/tools/* 2>/dev/null; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- App controller ---'; cat \\\"\"'$GAME/main.ts\"'","aggregated_output":"--- Task deliverables ---\n32:## This computer\n48:### What this computer doesn't have\n59:### Sharing this computer\n66:## Goal\n82:## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\n89:## Done\n92:## Source Information\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n111:  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n112:  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n113:  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n114:  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n115:  \"aiHub\": {\n--- Engine / networking specifications ---\n7:**[tested]** marks what was actually run on this machine on 2026-11-04, against my-3dge at commit e7a1243. **[source]**\n12:8 Screens · 9 Multiplayer · 10 Art · 11 Animation · 12 Audio · 13 Writing · 14 Tech · 15 Engine traps · 16 Testing ·\n34:2. **Your thumb is the exercise.** The character's limbs follow the input directly, by scrubbing animation (section 11).\n120:accel   = gain × (target − cob) + instability × cob + noise(t) × (1 − calmEffect × calm) + disturbance\n129:| `game.wobble.noise` | 3.5 /s² | 0–8 | Sway strength |\n130:| `game.wobble.noiseRate` | 0.15 Hz | 0.05–0.4 | Sway speed: a slow push you lean against |\n139:noise(t) = ( sin(2π·rate·m1·t + p1) + 0.6·sin(2π·rate·1.7·m2·t + p2) + 0.3·sin(2π·rate·3.1·m3·t + p3) ) / 1.3      // mi in 0.8–1.25\n415:gap in the rim. Score: share sunk × 800, plus time left. No Wobble noise here: this one is about touch.\n516:  Resume, Restart Activity, Back to the Island, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About / Credits, Quit to Title.\n523:**Dev Mode** (from the pause menu; absent in hub sessions; a clear panel that works with pad, keyboard and mouse):\n564:### In AI Hub: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, mode **ghost**\n566:Read the protocol once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Fetch by raw URL, into\n567:`labs/game/hub/`: `session.js` (save it as `session-client.txt`), and for tests `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same\n570:Why ghost: every copy runs its own seeded round, nothing depends on a host, and each player sees the others on the neighbouring mats,\n578:<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n587:**Startup** **[tested: this shape, on the starter's one scene, passed the harness at 2, 3 (host leaving) and 4 players with the engine running in every frame]**:\n594:const info = AIHub?.active ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\n596:const watchdog = info ? setTimeout(() => AIHub.ready(), 14000) : 0;   // the harness allows 20 s after hello\n602:unknown query key as a setting and fails with `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, **and the harness still reports PASS**, because the client keeps\n611:  `keydown` on `window`: the harness sends a synthetic one. The card has no menus or choices, and draws numbers only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n614:  `AIHub.progress({ score: 0, label: 'Breathing in' })` and one ghost message, so a slow copy still passes the harness.\n618:  `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:ghosts', […])` to actors on the other mats, tinted with `info.players[i].color`, leans scrubbed by their CoB,\n629:**Boot deadline, the one place performance matters.** The harness gives every copy 20 s to call `ready()`. **[tested on SwiftShader]** the starter\n683:## 11. Animation\n723:**New animations to write:** the eight poses; lean strips; `DeepKnee`, `SideLunge`; `StepUpL`, `StepUpR`, `SideStep`, `Jump`; `HipCircle` (a looped key ring scrubbed by angle); `Somersault` (`body` lean running to 720°, since values keep counting past 360°) and\n754:- A **syllable bank** per speaker: 16 entries (`defineSfx`), each a short consonant noise then a saw through two bandpass filters at a vowel's formants. **[tested: this renders, and vowels differ measurably; nobody can listen here, so judge by numbers]**\n758:    { wave: 'noise', dur: 0.015, vol: 0.12, attack: 0.001, filter: { type: 'bandpass', freq: 3200 } },\n778:**Effects** (`defineSfx`, plus built-ins `sfx:select`, `sfx:confirm`, `sfx:cancel`, `sfx:coin`, `sfx:step*`): wobble creak with pitch by `r`; breath in and out (filtered noise); mat squeak; stamp thump; pebble clack; small and huge splashes; gull squawk; frog ribbit; rope creak; marble roll, a loop with level by speed; hoop whoosh; clap, kick, hat; whistle; ferry horn; thunder; the island's deep groan, pitched by tilt; polite crowd \"ooh\". **Ambience:** sea, birds, wind, rain, as loops with `loop` passes.\n833:**Stack:** my-3dge full workspace (TypeScript, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, Vitest, Playwright, HTML/CSS UI). No new npm dependencies. The engine stays read-only: `npm run check` compares every engine file with `engine-lock.json`. Workarounds go in the game; what you needed goes in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\n838:src=$(mktemp -d) && git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge \"$src\" && node \"$src/tools/game/new-game.mjs\" . --name <short-lowercase-name>\n882:**Key components** (plain data): `flow` (mode: front, roam, event, cutscene, results; event, phase, tick; day), `wobble` (per seat), `seat` (input per seat), `island` (tilt), `round`, `pebble`, `plaque`, `ghost`, plus one per activity. Time in whole steps, randomness from named streams, loops in `w.query` order, `Math.pow` not `**`.\n926:| Hub's `?aihub=…` in the query | `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, engine dead, harness still passes | Strip them; assert `__engine.ready` in every frame |\n948:| Fast sway | Doing nothing beats a human thumb **[tested]** | Keep `game.wobble.noiseRate` slow; judge with the delayed-thumb bot |\n976:- **Pause and dev:** pause menu reaches Dev Mode; a slider changes behaviour; Reset restores defaults; jumps work; not present in a session.\n981:- **Hub harness:** serve the built file beside `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` (Node `http` server or `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is your game, stop only that PID: never `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`). Run `harness.html?game=<file>&players=N&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000` for N = 2, 3, 4, then `players=3&…&scenario=host-leave`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass`, with `body[data-complete=\"true\"]` at the end. **Also assert in each frame** `__engine.ready === true`, zero engine errors, a `ghost` entity at 2 players; no console line starting `[AIHub]`; and that the pasted client's SHA-256 from banner to last line matches `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0; compare what you fetched first, the hub may have moved on).\n982:- **By hand in the harness:** run it once without `auto` at 2 players: its frames are your players on this computer, and clicking a frame gives it the keyboard. New round, Time up, Remove player. Drive it by script and read the state to see the card, ghosts and results; one screenshot.\n984:**Screenshots, at the end, by eye, 1920 × 1080:** title, island, Pose Class HUD, Still Pond with a lure, The Line, Great Tilt wide shot, results, pause, Dev Mode, About. `node x shot labs/game --png` or a Playwright screenshot: both worked here.\n992:1. **Skeleton (first hour's job).** Workspace, one-file build, hub client and tags, `game:round` with one mat, harness passing with the engine truly running, `verify.mjs` skeleton.\n1000:9. **Together.** Group Class; hub ghosts, own card, full round.\n1001:10. **The shell.** Attract, full Dev Mode, Settings, Controls, About, touch-only, no-WebGPU page.\n1005:**Cut line, if and only if you run out of budget.** Cut whole things and re-flow `days.ts`, leaving no trace (no greyed-out rows, no mentions), in this order: Great Tilt step 3 → Expert variants and outfits → Hoop Patrol → Reps Hall → Island Jog's race (keep the walk) → Cliff Plunge → Step Class. Never cut: Morning Check, Pose Class, Still Pond, The Line, Sand Garden, Paddle Glide, Great Tilt steps 1, 2, 4 and 5, Group Class, hub ghost round, attract, Dev Mode, About.\n1025:Answers already decided: Plan: the name this file has in your folder. Genre and Perspective as in section 1. Tech: my-3dge at its pinned commit, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, TypeScript. Art: the engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets. Animation: the engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim. Audio: tracker songs, `defineSfx` effects, gibberish syllable voices, all code, music at 10%. Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost; same-screen Group Class on its own. Environment and Model as your TASK.md gives them. Usage: \"added on import\".\n1029:**Credits must include:** my-3dge (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), @stdlib (Apache-2.0); the AI Hub session client. Animation clips by what you actually copied: Mesh2Motion and Quaternius Universal Animation Library (CC0; credit anyway); **100STYLE dataset, Mason, Starke and Komura, 2022, CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), converted to key poses: required credit with a link and a note of changes** if you use any `STYLE100*` clip; CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database if you use any `CMU` clip (terms in `data/anim/LICENSES/CMU.txt`).\n1045:| Animation: engine's system base; new animations | 11 |\n--- Game source sizes ---\n   35 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/art.ts\n   20 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/audio.ts\n   22 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/best.test.ts\n   33 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/best.ts\n   90 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/bot.ts\n  201 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts\n   49 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/programme.ts\n   43 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts\n   95 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/wobble.ts\n    2 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/styles.css\n   22 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/tools/bundle.mjs\n  612 total\n--- App controller ---\n/** @file Runs the retreat's menus, input, and balance sessions. */\nimport './styles.css';\nimport { DAYS, rankFor, type Activity } from './programme';\nimport { DEFAULT_BALANCE, action, createSession, stepSession, targetFor, type Session } from './wobble';\nimport { Soundscape } from './audio';\nimport { welcomeView, hubView, gameView, resultView, modalView } from './view';\n\ntype Screen = 'welcome' | 'hub' | 'playing' | 'result';\ntype Modal = 'settings' | 'about' | 'pause' | 'touch' | null;\ntype Preferences = { sound: boolean; motion: boolean; contrast: boolean; assist: boolean };\ntype Save = { unlocked: number; scores: Record<string, number>; preferences: Preferences };\n\nconst root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#app')!;\nconst storageKey = 'wee-fit-retreat-save-v1';\nconst defaults: Save = { unlocked: 0, scores: {}, preferences: { sound: true, motion: false, contrast: false, assist: false } };\nfunction load(): Save {\n  try {\n    const saved = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(storageKey) || '{}') as Partial<Save>;\n    return { ...defaults, ...saved, scores: saved.scores || {}, preferences: { ...defaults.preferences, ...saved.preferences } };\n  } catch { return structuredClone(defaults); }\n}\nlet save = load();\nlet screen: Screen = 'welcome';\nlet modal: Modal = null;\nlet dayIndex = 0;\nlet activityIndex = 0;\nlet session: Session | null = null;\nlet attract = false;\nlet lastInput = performance.now();\nlet lastFrame = 0;\nlet accumulator = 0;\nlet lastPadButtons: boolean[] = [];\nlet lastInputType: 'keyboard' | 'controller' = 'keyboard';\nconst keys = new Set<string>();\nconst sounds = new Soundscape();\nsounds.enabled = save.preferences.sound;\n\nfunction persist(): void {\n  try { localStorage.setItem(storageKey, JSON.stringify(save)); } catch { /* storage can be unavailable */ }\n}\nfunction flatIndex(day: number, activity: number): number {\n  return DAYS.slice(0, day).reduce((total, item) => total + item.activities.length, 0) + activity;\n}\nfunction selected(): Activity { return DAYS[dayIndex].activities[activityIndex]; }\nfunction selectFlat(index: number): void {\n  let remaining = index;\n  for (let day = 0; day < DAYS.length; day++) {\n    if (remaining < DAYS[day].activities.length) { dayIndex = day; activityIndex = remaining; return; }\n    remaining -= DAYS[day].activities.length;\n  }\n}\nfunction totalActivities(): number { return DAYS.reduce((total, day) => total + day.activities.length, 0); }\nfunction playSound(name: 'click' | 'hit' | 'finish' | 'miss'): void { try { sounds.play(name); } catch { /* audio is optional */ } }\nfunction isTouchOnly(): boolean {\n  return matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)').matches && !Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.() || []).some(Boolean);\n}\nfunction render(): void {\n  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('reduced-motion', save.preferences.motion);\n  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('high-contrast', save.preferences.contrast);\n  const content = screen === 'welcome' ? welcomeView(isTouchOnly()) : screen === 'hub' ? hubView(dayIndex, activityIndex, save.unlocked, save.scores) : screen === 'playing' && session ? gameView(session, attract, lastInputType) : session ? resultView(session) : '';\n  root.innerHTML = content + (modal ? modalView(modal, save.preferences) : '');\n  if (screen === 'playing') updateGame();\n  if (modal) root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.modal button, .modal input')?.focus();\n}\nfunction openGame(preview = false): void {\n  if (!preview && isTouchOnly()) { modal = 'touch'; render(); return; }\n  session = createSession(selected(), 13 + flatIndex(dayIndex, activityIndex));\n  attract = preview; screen = 'playing'; modal = null; lastFrame = 0; accumulator = 0;\n  keys.clear(); render();\n}\nfunction finish(): void {\n  if (!session) return;\n  if (attract) { screen = 'welcome'; attract = false; session = null; lastInput = performance.now(); render(); return; }\n  const index = flatIndex(dayIndex, activityIndex);\n  save.scores[session.activity.id] = Math.max(save.scores[session.activity.id] || 0, session.score);\n  save.unlocked = Math.min(totalActivities() - 1, Math.max(save.unlocked, index + 1));\n  persist(); playSound('finish'); screen = 'result'; render();\n}\nfunction updateGame(): void {\n  if (!session) return;\n  const balance = session.balance;\n  const target = targetFor(session);\n  const ball = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#balance-ball');\n  const marker = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#balance-target');\n  if (ball) { ball.style.left = `${50 + balance.x * 40}%`; ball.style.top = `${50 + balance.y * 40}%`; }\n  if (marker) { marker.style.left = `${50 + target.x * 40}%`; marker.style.top = `${50 + target.y * 40}%`; }\n  const timer = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-time');\n  if (timer) { const remaining = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(session.activity.duration - session.time)); timer.textContent = `${Math.floor(remaining / 60)}:${String(remaining % 60).padStart(2, '0')}`; }\n  const cue = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-cue');\n  if (cue) cue.textContent = balance.recovering > 0 ? 'Take a breath. Find your footing.' : target.label || session.cue || 'Find your centre';\n  const score = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-score');\n  if (score) score.textContent = `${Math.round(session.samples ? session.scoreSum / session.samples : 0)}`;\n  const falls = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-falls');\n  if (falls) falls.textContent = String(balance.falls);\n  const progress = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-progress');\n  if (progress) progress.style.width = `${Math.min(100, session.time / session.activity.duration * 100)}%`;\n  const person = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.guest-art');\n  if (person) person.style.setProperty('--lean', `${Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, balance.x)) * 11}deg`);\n}\nfunction moveFocus(direction: number): void {\n  const scope = modal ? root.querySelector('.modal') : root;\n  const focusables = Array.from(scope?.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('button:not(:disabled), input:not(:disabled)') || []);\n  if (!focusables.length) return;\n  const current = focusables.indexOf(document.activeElement as HTMLElement);\n  focusables[(current + direction + focusables.length) % focusables.length].focus();\n}\nfunction doFoot(foot: 'left' | 'right' | 'both'): void {\n  if (!session || screen !== 'playing' || modal || attract) return;\n  playSound(action(session, foot) ? 'hit' : 'miss');\n}\nfunction wake(): void {\n  lastInput = performance.now();\n  if (attract) { attract = false; session = null; screen = 'welcome'; render(); }\n}\nroot.addEventListener('click', (event) => {\n  const button = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLElement>('[data-action]');\n  if (!button) return;\n  if (attract) { wake(); return; }\n  wake(); const command = button.dataset.action; playSound('click');\n  if (command === 'begin') { screen = 'hub'; selectFlat(save.unlocked); }\n  else if (command === 'home') { screen = 'welcome'; session = null; }\n  else if (command === 'settings' || command === 'about') modal = command;\n  else if (command === 'close') modal = null;\n  else if (command === 'pause') modal = 'pause';\n  else if (command === 'resume') { modal = null; lastFrame = 0; }\n  else if (command === 'quit') { modal = null; session = null; screen = 'hub'; }\n  else if (command === 'reset') {\n    if (window.confirm('Reset all retreat progress and scores?')) { save = structuredClone(defaults); sounds.enabled = save.preferences.sound; persist(); dayIndex = 0; activityIndex = 0; }\n  } else if (command === 'day') { dayIndex = Number(button.dataset.day); activityIndex = 0; }\n  else if (command === 'activity') activityIndex = Number(button.dataset.index);\n  else if (command === 'start' || command === 'retry') { openGame(); return; }\n  else if (command === 'continue') { screen = 'hub'; session = null; selectFlat(save.unlocked); }\n  render();\n});\nroot.addEventListener('change', (event) => {\n  const input = event.target as HTMLInputElement;\n  const key = input.dataset.preference as keyof Preferences | undefined;\n  if (!key) return;\n  save.preferences[key] = input.checked; sounds.enabled = save.preferences.sound; persist(); render();\n});\nwindow.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n  const key = event.key.toLowerCase();\n  if (attract) { event.preventDefault(); wake(); return; }\n  lastInput = performance.now(); lastInputType = 'keyboard';\n  if (key === 'escape') { event.preventDefault(); if (modal) modal = null; else if (screen === 'playing') modal = 'pause'; render(); return; }\n  if (screen === 'playing' && !modal) {\n    if (['arrowup','arrowdown','arrowleft','arrowright',' ','q','e'].includes(key)) event.preventDefault();\n    keys.add(key);\n    if (!event.repeat && key === 'q') doFoot('left');\n    if (!event.repeat && key === 'e') doFoot('right');\n    if (!event.repeat && key === ' ') doFoot('both');\n  } else if (['arrowup','arrowdown','arrowleft','arrowright'].includes(key)) {\n    event.preventDefault(); moveFocus(key === 'arrowup' || key === 'arrowleft' ? -1 : 1);\n  }\n});\nwindow.addEventListener('keyup', (event) => keys.delete(event.key.toLowerCase()));\nwindow.addEventListener('blur', () => keys.clear());\ndocument.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => { lastFrame = 0; });\nwindow.addEventListener('pointerdown', () => { if (attract) wake(); else lastInput = performance.now(); });\n\nfunction frame(now: number): void {\n  const pad = Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.() || []).find(Boolean);\n  let stickX = 0; let stickY = 0; let gentle = false;\n  if (pad) {\n    stickX = Math.abs(pad.axes[0] || 0) > .13 ? pad.axes[0] : 0;\n    stickY = Math.abs(pad.axes[1] || 0) > .13 ? pad.axes[1] : 0;\n    gentle = !!pad.buttons[7]?.pressed;\n    const buttons = pad.buttons.map((button) => button.pressed);\n    const pressed = (index: number) => buttons[index] && !lastPadButtons[index];\n    if (buttons.some((button, index) => button && !lastPadButtons[index]) || stickX || stickY) {\n      if (attract) wake();\n      lastInput = now; lastInputType = 'controller';\n    }\n    if (pressed(9) || pressed(3)) { if (screen === 'playing') { modal = modal ? null : 'pause'; render(); } }\n    if (screen === 'playing' && !modal) {\n      if (pressed(4)) doFoot('left'); if (pressed(5)) doFoot('right'); if (pressed(0)) doFoot('both');\n    } else {\n      if (pressed(12) || pressed(14)) moveFocus(-1);\n      if (pressed(13) || pressed(15)) moveFocus(1);\n      if (pressed(0)) (document.activeElement as HTMLElement | null)?.click();\n      if (pressed(1) && modal) { modal = null; render(); }\n    }\n    lastPadButtons = buttons;\n  } else lastPadButtons = [];\n  if (screen === 'welcome' && !modal && now - lastInput > 60000) { dayIndex = 0; activityIndex = 0; openGame(true); }\n  if (screen === 'playing' && session && !modal && !document.hidden) {\n    const elapsed = lastFrame ? Math.min((now - lastFrame) / 1000, .1) : 0;\n    accumulator += elapsed;\n    const input = attract ? { x: Math.sin(now / 1800) * .25, y: Math.cos(now / 2400) * .2, gentle: true } : {\n      x: Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, stickX + Number(keys.has('d') || keys.has('arrowright')) - Number(keys.has('a') || keys.has('arrowleft')))),\n      y: Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, stickY + Number(keys.has('s') || keys.has('arrowdown')) - Number(keys.has('w') || keys.has('arrowup')))),\n      gentle: gentle || keys.has('shift'),\n    };\n    const settings = save.preferences.assist ? { ...DEFAULT_BALANCE, gain: DEFAULT_BALANCE.gain * .7, instability: DEFAULT_BALANCE.instability * .7, damping: DEFAULT_BALANCE.damping * 1.3 } : DEFAULT_BALANCE;\n    while (accumulator >= 1 / 60 && !session.finished) { stepSession(session, input, settings, 1 / 60); accumulator -= 1 / 60; }\n    updateGame();\n    if (session.finished) finish();\n  }\n  lastFrame = now; requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\nrender(); requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
