{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_429","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"GAME='Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game'; echo '--- specs ---'; rg -n 'https?://|my-3dge|AI Hub|hub-client|harness|Animation|animation|noise|ghost|Dev Mode' PLAN.md | head -85; echo '--- files ---'; wc -l \\\"\"'$GAME\"/*.{ts,css} \"$GAME\"/tools/* 2>/dev/null; echo '\"'--- entry and scene ---'; sed -n '1,180p' \\\"\"'$GAME/scenes/play.ts\"; echo '\"'--- engine exports ---'; rg -n 'class (Engine|Game|World|Character|Animation)|export .*Animation|export .*Character' 'Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine' | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_429","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"GAME='Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game'; echo '--- specs ---'; rg -n 'https?://|my-3dge|AI Hub|hub-client|harness|Animation|animation|noise|ghost|Dev Mode' PLAN.md | head -85; echo '--- files ---'; wc -l \\\"\"'$GAME\"/*.{ts,css} \"$GAME\"/tools/* 2>/dev/null; echo '\"'--- entry and scene ---'; sed -n '1,180p' \\\"\"'$GAME/scenes/play.ts\"; echo '\"'--- engine exports ---'; rg -n 'class (Engine|Game|World|Character|Animation)|export .*Animation|export .*Character' 'Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine' | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"--- specs ---\n7:**[tested]** marks what was actually run on this machine on 2026-11-04, against my-3dge at commit e7a1243. **[source]**\n12:8 Screens · 9 Multiplayer · 10 Art · 11 Animation · 12 Audio · 13 Writing · 14 Tech · 15 Engine traps · 16 Testing ·\n34:2. **Your thumb is the exercise.** The character's limbs follow the input directly, by scrubbing animation (section 11).\n120:accel   = gain × (target − cob) + instability × cob + noise(t) × (1 − calmEffect × calm) + disturbance\n129:| `game.wobble.noise` | 3.5 /s² | 0–8 | Sway strength |\n130:| `game.wobble.noiseRate` | 0.15 Hz | 0.05–0.4 | Sway speed: a slow push you lean against |\n139:noise(t) = ( sin(2π·rate·m1·t + p1) + 0.6·sin(2π·rate·1.7·m2·t + p2) + 0.3·sin(2π·rate·3.1·m3·t + p3) ) / 1.3      // mi in 0.8–1.25\n415:gap in the rim. Score: share sunk × 800, plus time left. No Wobble noise here: this one is about touch.\n516:  Resume, Restart Activity, Back to the Island, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About / Credits, Quit to Title.\n523:**Dev Mode** (from the pause menu; absent in hub sessions; a clear panel that works with pad, keyboard and mouse):\n564:### In AI Hub: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, mode **ghost**\n566:Read the protocol once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Fetch by raw URL, into\n567:`labs/game/hub/`: `session.js` (save it as `session-client.txt`), and for tests `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same\n570:Why ghost: every copy runs its own seeded round, nothing depends on a host, and each player sees the others on the neighbouring mats,\n578:<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n587:**Startup** **[tested: this shape, on the starter's one scene, passed the harness at 2, 3 (host leaving) and 4 players with the engine running in every frame]**:\n594:const info = AIHub?.active ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\n596:const watchdog = info ? setTimeout(() => AIHub.ready(), 14000) : 0;   // the harness allows 20 s after hello\n602:unknown query key as a setting and fails with `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, **and the harness still reports PASS**, because the client keeps\n611:  `keydown` on `window`: the harness sends a synthetic one. The card has no menus or choices, and draws numbers only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n614:  `AIHub.progress({ score: 0, label: 'Breathing in' })` and one ghost message, so a slow copy still passes the harness.\n618:  `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:ghosts', […])` to actors on the other mats, tinted with `info.players[i].color`, leans scrubbed by their CoB,\n629:**Boot deadline, the one place performance matters.** The harness gives every copy 20 s to call `ready()`. **[tested on SwiftShader]** the starter\n683:## 11. Animation\n723:**New animations to write:** the eight poses; lean strips; `DeepKnee`, `SideLunge`; `StepUpL`, `StepUpR`, `SideStep`, `Jump`; `HipCircle` (a looped key ring scrubbed by angle); `Somersault` (`body` lean running to 720°, since values keep counting past 360°) and\n754:- A **syllable bank** per speaker: 16 entries (`defineSfx`), each a short consonant noise then a saw through two bandpass filters at a vowel's formants. **[tested: this renders, and vowels differ measurably; nobody can listen here, so judge by numbers]**\n758:    { wave: 'noise', dur: 0.015, vol: 0.12, attack: 0.001, filter: { type: 'bandpass', freq: 3200 } },\n778:**Effects** (`defineSfx`, plus built-ins `sfx:select`, `sfx:confirm`, `sfx:cancel`, `sfx:coin`, `sfx:step*`): wobble creak with pitch by `r`; breath in and out (filtered noise); mat squeak; stamp thump; pebble clack; small and huge splashes; gull squawk; frog ribbit; rope creak; marble roll, a loop with level by speed; hoop whoosh; clap, kick, hat; whistle; ferry horn; thunder; the island's deep groan, pitched by tilt; polite crowd \"ooh\". **Ambience:** sea, birds, wind, rain, as loops with `loop` passes.\n833:**Stack:** my-3dge full workspace (TypeScript, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, Vitest, Playwright, HTML/CSS UI). No new npm dependencies. The engine stays read-only: `npm run check` compares every engine file with `engine-lock.json`. Workarounds go in the game; what you needed goes in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\n838:src=$(mktemp -d) && git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge \"$src\" && node \"$src/tools/game/new-game.mjs\" . --name <short-lowercase-name>\n882:**Key components** (plain data): `flow` (mode: front, roam, event, cutscene, results; event, phase, tick; day), `wobble` (per seat), `seat` (input per seat), `island` (tilt), `round`, `pebble`, `plaque`, `ghost`, plus one per activity. Time in whole steps, randomness from named streams, loops in `w.query` order, `Math.pow` not `**`.\n926:| Hub's `?aihub=…` in the query | `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, engine dead, harness still passes | Strip them; assert `__engine.ready` in every frame |\n948:| Fast sway | Doing nothing beats a human thumb **[tested]** | Keep `game.wobble.noiseRate` slow; judge with the delayed-thumb bot |\n976:- **Pause and dev:** pause menu reaches Dev Mode; a slider changes behaviour; Reset restores defaults; jumps work; not present in a session.\n981:- **Hub harness:** serve the built file beside `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` (Node `http` server or `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is your game, stop only that PID: never `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`). Run `harness.html?game=<file>&players=N&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000` for N = 2, 3, 4, then `players=3&…&scenario=host-leave`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass`, with `body[data-complete=\"true\"]` at the end. **Also assert in each frame** `__engine.ready === true`, zero engine errors, a `ghost` entity at 2 players; no console line starting `[AIHub]`; and that the pasted client's SHA-256 from banner to last line matches `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0; compare what you fetched first, the hub may have moved on).\n982:- **By hand in the harness:** run it once without `auto` at 2 players: its frames are your players on this computer, and clicking a frame gives it the keyboard. New round, Time up, Remove player. Drive it by script and read the state to see the card, ghosts and results; one screenshot.\n984:**Screenshots, at the end, by eye, 1920 × 1080:** title, island, Pose Class HUD, Still Pond with a lure, The Line, Great Tilt wide shot, results, pause, Dev Mode, About. `node x shot labs/game --png` or a Playwright screenshot: both worked here.\n992:1. **Skeleton (first hour's job).** Workspace, one-file build, hub client and tags, `game:round` with one mat, harness passing with the engine truly running, `verify.mjs` skeleton.\n1000:9. **Together.** Group Class; hub ghosts, own card, full round.\n1001:10. **The shell.** Attract, full Dev Mode, Settings, Controls, About, touch-only, no-WebGPU page.\n1005:**Cut line, if and only if you run out of budget.** Cut whole things and re-flow `days.ts`, leaving no trace (no greyed-out rows, no mentions), in this order: Great Tilt step 3 → Expert variants and outfits → Hoop Patrol → Reps Hall → Island Jog's race (keep the walk) → Cliff Plunge → Step Class. Never cut: Morning Check, Pose Class, Still Pond, The Line, Sand Garden, Paddle Glide, Great Tilt steps 1, 2, 4 and 5, Group Class, hub ghost round, attract, Dev Mode, About.\n1025:Answers already decided: Plan: the name this file has in your folder. Genre and Perspective as in section 1. Tech: my-3dge at its pinned commit, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, TypeScript. Art: the engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets. Animation: the engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim. Audio: tracker songs, `defineSfx` effects, gibberish syllable voices, all code, music at 10%. Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost; same-screen Group Class on its own. Environment and Model as your TASK.md gives them. Usage: \"added on import\".\n1029:**Credits must include:** my-3dge (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), @stdlib (Apache-2.0); the AI Hub session client. Animation clips by what you actually copied: Mesh2Motion and Quaternius Universal Animation Library (CC0; credit anyway); **100STYLE dataset, Mason, Starke and Komura, 2022, CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), converted to key poses: required credit with a link and a note of changes** if you use any `STYLE100*` clip; CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database if you use any `CMU` clip (terms in `data/anim/LICENSES/CMU.txt`).\n1045:| Animation: engine's system base; new animations | 11 |\n--- files ---\n   35 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/art.ts\n   20 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/audio.ts\n   22 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/best.test.ts\n   33 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/best.ts\n   90 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/bot.ts\n  201 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts\n   49 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/programme.ts\n   43 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts\n   95 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/wobble.ts\n    2 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/styles.css\n   22 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/tools/bundle.mjs\n  612 total\n--- entry and scene ---\n/**\n * @file The starter game's scene `game:play`: every new game begins as this one (tools/game/new-game.mjs copies\n * labs/game/ into it), so it is small, plays, and shows the parts a game is made of. The player, a humanoid on the\n * character controller, runs round the arena (`ARENA_TEXT` below: walls, two pillars, two low walls to jump) collecting\n * the gems the seed scatters, before the clock runs out. All the gems: won; the clock at 0: lost.\n *\n * The parts: a level as text, compiled for its physics bodies; settings (`game.*`, read when the scene starts, so they\n * change play and go in replays); components (`gem`, drawn as a small glowing box because it declares `x` and `z` in\n * metres; `round`, the score and the clock); the player (labs/game/cast/player.ts, an actor that reads the step's\n * intents: `move`, `jump`, `dash`); systems in the phase `rules`, after the actors' feet are read back; a named random\n * stream (`gems`); events (`gem`, `won`, `lost`) that pages, sounds and tests hear. The page is labs/game/main.ts, the\n * bot labs/game/bot.ts.\n *\n * The level's text lives here, not in a .txt file, since sim-side code reads no files; the page registers the same\n * text for the view (labs/game/main.ts).\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts, so `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts` runs it in Node.\n *\n * @example\n * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --steps 600\n * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --set game.gems=3 --seed 7\n * ARENA.spawns.find((spawn) => spawn.name === 'hero')?.position; // [3.5, 0, 2.5]\n * @see labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\n */\nimport {\n  addLevelBodies,\n  compileLevel,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineScene,\n  defineSettings,\n  physicsOf,\n  type ActorComponent,\n  type World,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { spawnPlayer } from '../cast/player';\n\n/** The arena: 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls (0.75 m) to jump, the spawn `@`. */\nexport const ARENA_TEXT = `---\ndescription: The starter game's arena. 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls 0.75 m high that the player jumps, and the player's spawn.\n---\n##################\n#................#\n#..@.............#\n#.......PP.......#\n#.......PP.......#\n#................#\n#....w......w....#\n#....w......w....#\n#................#\n#.......PP.......#\n#.......PP.......#\n#................#\n#................#\n##################\n`;\n\n/** The arena, compiled: its colliders for physics, its tiles for the gems and the bot's paths. */\nexport const ARENA = compileLevel(ARENA_TEXT, { file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts', name: 'arena' });\n\n/** The game's settings: each is reachable through `x set`, URL parameters (`?game.gems=3`) and `__engine.set`. */\nexport const GAME_SETTINGS = defineSettings({\n  'game.gems': {\n    type: 'integer',\n    default: 10,\n    minimum: 1,\n    maximum: 40,\n    when: 'scene',\n    description: 'How many gems the seed scatters.',\n  },\n  'game.seconds': {\n    type: 'number',\n    default: 30,\n    minimum: 5,\n    maximum: 600,\n    unit: 's',\n    when: 'scene',\n    description: 'How long the player has to collect them all.',\n  },\n  'game.speed': {\n    type: 'number',\n    default: 6,\n    minimum: 1,\n    maximum: 20,\n    unit: 'm/s',\n    when: 'scene',\n    description: 'How fast the player runs.',\n  },\n});\n\n/** A gem: where it floats and how it looks (the page draws a component that declares x and z in metres). */\nexport const GEM = defineComponent('gem', {\n  description: 'A gem to collect: where it floats, its spin and how it is drawn.',\n  fields: {\n    x: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm', description: 'East.' },\n    y: { type: 'number', default: 0.5, unit: 'm', description: 'Up: the bottom of its box.' },\n    z: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm', description: 'South.' },\n    yaw: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'rad', description: 'Its spin.' },\n    size: { type: 'number', default: 0.4, unit: 'm', description: 'The side of its box.' },\n    material: { type: 'string', default: 'material:glow', description: 'What it is drawn with.' },\n  },\n});\n\n/** The round: the score, the clock and how it ended. One entity holds it. */\nexport const ROUND = defineComponent('round', {\n  description:\n    'The round: gems collected of the total, the steps left on the clock, and whether it is playing, won or lost.',\n  fields: {\n    gems: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many gems the round scattered.' },\n    collected: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many the player has collected.' },\n    left: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'The sim steps left on the clock (60 a second).' },\n    state: { type: 'string', default: 'playing', description: \"'playing', 'won' or 'lost'.\" },\n  },\n});\n\n/** The round, as the component holds it. */\nexport type Round = { gems: number; collected: number; left: number; state: 'playing' | 'won' | 'lost' };\n\n/** The scene's components, typed. */\nexport type GameComponents = {\n  gem: { x: number; y: number; z: number; yaw: number; size: number; material: string };\n  round: Round;\n  actor: ActorComponent;\n};\n\n/** How close the player's feet come to a gem to collect it, m (on the ground plane). */\nexport const REACH = 0.8;\n\n/** How far from the spawn the gems keep, m, so the first one is never collected without moving. */\nconst CLEAR = 3;\n\n/** Where the player starts: the level's spawn `@`. */\nconst START = ARENA.spawns.find((spawn) => spawn.name === 'hero')!.position;\n\n/** The floor tiles a gem may float over: open floor (`.`), at least `CLEAR` metres from the spawn, in reading order. */\nfunction gemTiles(): number[] {\n  const tiles: number[] = [];\n  ARENA.tiles.forEach((char, i) => {\n    const x = ((i % ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    const z = (Math.floor(i / ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    if (char === '.' && Math.hypot(x - START[0], z - START[2]) >= CLEAR) tiles.push(i);\n  });\n  return tiles;\n}\n\n/** Scatters `count` gems over distinct floor tiles drawn from the stream `gems`: each seed lays them its own way. */\nfunction scatterGems(w: World<GameComponents>, count: number): void {\n  const tiles = gemTiles();\n  const rng = w.rng('gems');\n  for (let k = 0; k < count && tiles.length > 0; k++) {\n    const [tile] = tiles.splice(rng.int(0, tiles.length - 1), 1);\n    const x = ((tile % ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    const z = (Math.floor(tile / ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    w.spawn({ gem: { x, z, yaw: rng.range(0, Math.PI) } });\n  }\n}\n\n/** Ends the round: the player stops reading intents (and so stands still), and the event says how it ended. */\nfunction endRound(w: World<GameComponents>, round: Round, state: 'won' | 'lost'): void {\n  round.state = state;\n  for (const e of w.query('actor')) {\n    e.actor.player = false;\n    e.actor.intents = {};\n  }\n  w.emit(state, { collected: round.collected, gems: round.gems, left: round.left });\n}\n\n/**\n * Spins the gems, collects those an actor's feet reach, and ends the round when the last one goes. A despawn waits for\n * the end of the step, so a gem taken this step is remembered: two actors never count it twice.\n */\nfunction collect(w: World<GameComponents>): void {\n  const [{ round }] = w.query('round');\n  for (const gem of w.query('gem')) gem.gem.yaw += 2 * w.dt;\n  if (round.state !== 'playing') return;\n  const taken = new Set<number>();\n  for (const { actor } of w.query('actor')) {\n    for (const gem of w.query('gem')) {\n      if (taken.has(gem.id) || Math.hypot(gem.gem.x - actor.x, gem.gem.z - actor.z) > REACH) continue;\n      taken.add(gem.id);\n      w.despawn(gem.id);\n--- engine exports ---\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/index.ts:301:export { AnimationClip } from 'three/webgpu';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/index.ts:303:export { AnimationMixer } from 'three/webgpu';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/sim-api.ts:171:export { createCharacter } from './physics/character';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/sim-api.ts:172:export type { Character } from './physics/character';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/sim-api.ts:175:export type { CharacterState } from './physics/character';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/sim/actors.ts:88:export interface ActorComponent extends CharacterState {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/room.ts:48:export function roomOf(physics: Physics, body: number, character: Character, oneWay?: ReadonlySet<number>): Room {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/room.ts:67:export function fitHull(physics: Physics, body: number, character: Character, motion: MotionState, air: boolean, oneWay?: ReadonlySet<number>): void { // prettier-ignore\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/ledge.ts:86:export function findWall(physics: Physics, body: number, character: Character, dir: readonly [number, number], probe: number): Wall | null { // prettier-ignore\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/sim/feelCourse.ts:95:export function measureFeel(character: Character, options: FeelOptions = {}): FeelReport {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/sim/movementApi.ts:36:export { tuneCharacter } from '../physics/movement/settings';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/movement/settings.ts:59:export function tuneCharacter(character: Character, overrides: readonly MovementOverride[]): Character {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/movement/mantle.ts:67:export const crouchPressed = (input: CharacterInput, motion: MotionState) =>\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/movement/mantle.ts:143:export function startMantle(character: Character, state: CharacterState, motion: MotionState, input: CharacterInput, ledge: Ledge, feet: Point, dt: number): void { // prettier-ignore\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/anim/clip/retarget.ts:302:export interface AnimationClipJSON {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/anim/clip/retarget.ts:316:export function clipJSON(baked: BakedClip, skeleton: Skeleton, options: { travel?: boolean } = {}): AnimationClipJSON {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/anim/api.ts:191:export type { AnimationClipJSON } from './clip/retarget';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/movement/ride.ts:95:export const spent = (character: Character, dt: number) => Math.round(character.feel.coyote / dt) + 1;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/anim/traversal/contacts.ts:88:export function hullOf(character: CharacterView | null | undefined, rung: number): HullView {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/movement/crouch.ts:44:export function hullFor(character: Character, motion: MotionState): number {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/feel.ts:236:export function steer(character: Character, state: CharacterState, input: CharacterInput, dt: number, g: number) {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/characterBody.ts:27:export function bodyAt(character: Character, feet: Vec3Like, where = 'bodyAt(feet)'): [number, number, number] {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/characterBody.ts:34:export function addCharacter(physics: Physics, character: Character, feet: Vec3Like): number {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/characterBody.ts:48:export function feetOf(physics: Physics, body: number, character: Character): Vector3 {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/core/log.ts:113:export class EngineError extends Error {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/hull.ts:37:export function hullHeight(physics: Physics, body: number, character: Character): number {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/hull.ts:78:export function setHull(physics: Physics, body: number, character: Character, height: number, keep: HullKeep): void {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/character.ts:59:export { addCharacter, bodyAt, feetOf } from './characterBody';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/character.ts:134:export type Character = EntryOf<typeof CHARACTER_FIELDS>;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/character.ts:153:export function createCharacter(spec: Record<string, unknown> = {}, registry?: Registry): Character {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/character.ts:181:export type CharacterState = {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/character.ts:186:export function createCharacterState(): CharacterState {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/character.ts:191:export interface CharacterInput {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/character.ts:238:export interface CharacterStep {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/character.ts:279:export function stepCharacter(\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/move.ts:48:export interface CharacterHit {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/move.ts:55:export interface CharacterMove {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/move.ts:115:export function halfHeightOf(collider: RAPIER.Collider, character: Character): number {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/move.ts:151:export function isWall(character: Character, normal: Vector3): boolean {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/move.ts:156:export function queryGroups(collider: RAPIER.Collider, character: Character): number {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/move.ts:162:export function isWalkable(character: Character, normal: Vector3): boolean {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/physics/move.ts:177:export function moveCharacter(\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
