{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_572","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"P=Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- task deliverables ---'; rg -n -C 2 'my-3dge|exit-interview|feedback|session\\\\.js|AIHub|sourceInformation' TASK.md | head -n 120; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- engine exports ---'; ls \\\"\"'$P/engine\"; cat \"$P/engine/index.ts\" 2>/dev/null | head -n 150; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- source structure ---'; find \\\"\"'$P/labs/game\" -maxdepth 2 -type f | sort; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- main control flow ---'; rg -n '\"'^function |''^const |''^let |''^type |''^import'\"' \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/main.ts\"; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- plan engine and hub ---'; rg -n -C 2 'AIHub\\\\.connect|Hub round|harness|session\\\\.js|render3D|3D|pebble|music' PLAN.md | head -n 150\"","aggregated_output":"--- task deliverables ---\n11-Package: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\n12-\n13:Tech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge#make-a-game-with-my-3dge, in the engine's full workspace. The engine stays read-only, as the AGENTS.md it gives your game says: add whatever systems, art assets and animations the game needs on top of it. The rest of the tech stack is your choice.\n14-\n15-Art Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic props.\n--\n107-- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n108-\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n110-{\n111:  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n112-  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n113-  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n--- engine exports ---\nLICENSE\nanim\napp\naudio\ncore\ndev\ngfx\nindex.ts\ninput\nphysics\nsim\nsim-api.ts\nui\nworld\n/**\n * @file The engine's front page: the public API for pages and tools (PLAN.md §6.1, §6.9, WP 1.6; doctrine: Quality\n * under the hood). A game's pages import only this module, its sim-side code only engine/sim-api.ts, which this module\n * re-exports whole (ESLint's public-API rule enforces both), so game agents never read the internals. docs/API.md is\n * the manual: every public name with its doc comment; docs/ERRORS.md gives every error and advice code with its fix.\n *\n * What is here, beyond the sim API: `createHeadless`, the engine without a page (Node, tests, `x sim`), whose object\n * is the inspector a page publishes as `window.__engine` (`help()` lists its members); `createEngine`, the engine in\n * a page, arrives with WP 2.7.\n *\n * Invariants: a flat list of `export … from` lines, one name per line, grouped by area, and append-only: each WP adds\n * its public names at the end of their area, so parallel lanes merge cleanly (§11.3). Each name is documented where\n * it is declared (`x docs --check` fails one without). No engine module imports this file or engine/sim-api.ts\n * (ESLint's layer rules): the barrels are for game code.\n *\n * @example\n * // labs/box/main.ts\n * // import { createEngine, defineScene } from '../../engine';\n * @see engine/sim-api.ts\n */\n\n// The sim API: everything sim-side game code uses.\nexport * from './sim-api';\n\n// Headless: the engine without a page, and its inspector (window.__engine in a page).\nexport { createHeadless } from './app/headless';\nexport type { Headless } from './app/headless';\nexport type { HeadlessOptions } from './app/headless';\nexport type { Inspector } from './dev/inspector';\nexport type { EngineInfo } from './dev/inspector';\nexport type { EntitySummary } from './dev/inspector';\n\n// Materials and procedural textures (WP 2.3): materials as data with three.js's classic parameters, seeded tiling\n// texture generators and their helpers, the CPU bake, and the page's material library.\nexport { defineMaterial } from './gfx/materials/material';\nexport { getMaterial } from './gfx/materials/material';\nexport type { MaterialEntry } from './gfx/materials/material';\nexport type { MaterialSpec } from './gfx/materials/material';\nexport { createMaterialLibrary } from './gfx/materials/library';\nexport type { MaterialLibrary } from './gfx/materials/library';\nexport { defineTexture } from './gfx/textures/texture';\nexport type { TextureEntry } from './gfx/textures/texture';\nexport type { Texel } from './gfx/textures/types';\nexport type { TextureContext } from './gfx/textures/types';\nexport type { TextureSpec } from './gfx/textures/types';\nexport type { TextureLook } from './gfx/textures/types';\nexport { bakeTexture } from './gfx/textures/bake';\nexport type { TextureBake } from './gfx/textures/bake';\nexport type { TextureRef } from './gfx/textures/bake';\nexport { cellHash } from './gfx/textures/tile';\nexport { wrapIndex } from './gfx/textures/tile';\nexport { palette } from './gfx/textures/tile';\nexport { pickTone } from './gfx/textures/tile';\nexport { runningBond } from './gfx/textures/tile';\nexport { tileNoise } from './gfx/textures/tile';\n\n// Input (WP 3.3, WP 13.9): the devices sampled into intents, action maps, bindings, aiming and the look settings.\nexport * from './input/api';\n// Geometry kit and level meshes (WP 2.4): shapes standing on the ground with UVs in metres, the geometry registry\n// (props and levels name geometry by id), their QA measures, and a compiled level drawn as meshes.\nexport { boxGeometry } from './gfx/geometry/box';\nexport type { BoxOptions } from './gfx/geometry/box';\nexport { roundedBoxGeometry } from './gfx/geometry/roundedBox';\nexport type { RoundedBoxOptions } from './gfx/geometry/roundedBox';\nexport { limbGeometry } from './gfx/geometry/limb';\nexport type { LimbOptions } from './gfx/geometry/limb';\nexport { rampGeometry } from './gfx/geometry/ramp';\nexport type { RampOptions } from './gfx/geometry/ramp';\nexport { frustumGeometry } from './gfx/geometry/frustum';\nexport type { FrustumOptions } from './gfx/geometry/frustum';\nexport { pillarGeometry } from './gfx/geometry/pillar';\nexport { pillarParts } from './gfx/geometry/pillar';\nexport type { PillarOptions } from './gfx/geometry/pillar';\nexport type { PillarPart } from './gfx/geometry/pillar';\nexport { ringGeometry } from './gfx/geometry/ring';\nexport type { RingOptions } from './gfx/geometry/ring';\nexport { sidesThenTops } from './gfx/geometry/groups';\nexport { mergeGeometries } from './gfx/geometry/groups';\nexport { defineGeometry } from './gfx/geometry/geometry';\nexport { getGeometry } from './gfx/geometry/geometry';\nexport { buildGeometry } from './gfx/geometry/geometry';\nexport type { GeometryEntry } from './gfx/geometry/geometry';\nexport type { GeometrySpec } from './gfx/geometry/geometry';\nexport type { GeometryRef } from './gfx/geometry/geometry';\nexport { inspectGeometry } from './gfx/geometry/inspect';\nexport type { GeometryReport } from './gfx/geometry/inspect';\nexport { createLevelMeshes } from './gfx/level/meshes';\nexport type { LevelMeshes } from './gfx/level/meshes';\nexport type { LevelMeshesOptions } from './gfx/level/meshes';\nexport type { LevelMeshPart } from './gfx/level/meshes';\nexport type { LevelCell } from './gfx/level/cells';\nexport { LEVEL_RECIPES } from './gfx/level/recipes';\nexport type { LevelRecipe } from './gfx/level/recipes';\nexport type { LevelShape } from './gfx/level/recipes';\nexport { createTerrainMeshes } from './gfx/terrain';\nexport type { TerrainMeshes } from './gfx/terrain';\nexport type { TerrainMeshesOptions } from './gfx/terrain';\n// Sound (WP 9.2, WP 9.3, WP 13.22): effects and songs as data, the audio runtime, rooms and walls: engine/audio/api.ts.\nexport * from './audio/api';\n// The engine in a page (WP 2.7): createEngine reads the routes, starts the scene with its view, publishes\n// window.__engine, warms up and runs the frame loop; createHeadless({ view: true }) builds the same view in Node.\nexport { createEngine } from './app/engine';\nexport type { Engine } from './app/engine';\nexport type { EngineOptions } from './app/engine';\nexport { parseRoutes } from './app/routes';\nexport { routeQuery } from './app/routes';\nexport type { Routes } from './app/routes';\nexport type { CameraInfo } from './app/view';\nexport type { PlayResult } from './app/playback';\nexport type { PlayIntoOptions } from './app/playback';\nexport type { ViewChange } from './app/playback';\n// A page's own presentation (WP 9.5): createEngine's onFrame, once per drawn frame, with the run to read and the camera.\nexport type { EngineFrame } from './app/engine';\nexport type { FrameWorld } from './app/engine';\nexport type { CameraPose } from './gfx/cameras/pose';\n// Touch controls (WP 3.12; built, not tested, ADR-0021): a page's touch layout (the corner fan's buttons and the menu\n// button) for createEngine's touchLayout and onMenu, the touch device on input.touch, and the touch codes it writes.\nexport { defineTouchLayout } from './ui/touch';\nexport { getTouchLayout } from './ui/touch';\nexport type { TouchLayout } from './ui/touch';\nexport type { TouchLayoutSpec } from './ui/touch';\nexport type { TouchButtonSpec } from './ui/touch';\nexport type { TouchDevice } from './input/devices/touch';\nexport type { StickView } from './input/devices/touch';\nexport type { TouchSetting } from './input/devices/touch';\nexport { touchCode } from './input/codes';\n// Level meshes v2 and the cutaway (WP 4.4): galleries, stairs, the dais, pillars with plinths and capitals and\n// brazier stands as recipe shapes; walls facing an outside camera cut low and pillars before the hero as stumps.\nexport { createCutaway } from './gfx/cutaway';\nexport { planCutaway } from './gfx/cutaway';\nexport type { Cutaway } from './gfx/cutaway';\nexport type { CutawayReport } from './gfx/cutaway';\nexport type { CutTarget } from './gfx/cutaway';\nexport type { LevelCut } from './gfx/level/recipes';\nexport type { CutWhen } from './gfx/level/recipes';\nexport type { PartCut } from './gfx/level/shapes';\n// Instancing and puppets (WP 3.8): batches of instanced copies in pages above r182's 1,000-slot uniform path; puppet\n// bodies as data (one line per part on the humanoid skeleton's bones, mirrored parts, material slots), compiled per\n// build and drawn as one rigid-skinned mesh per character or as instanced parts for crowds; blob shadows.\nexport { createInstancedBatch } from './gfx/instancing';\nexport type { InstancedBatch } from './gfx/instancing';\nexport type { InstancedBatchOptions } from './gfx/instancing';\nexport type { InstancedBatchStats } from './gfx/instancing';\nexport type { InstanceColor } from './gfx/instancing';\nexport { defineBody } from './gfx/puppets/grammar';\nexport { getBody } from './gfx/puppets/grammar';\nexport type { Body } from './gfx/puppets/grammar';\nexport type { BodySpec } from './gfx/puppets/grammar';\nexport type { BodyPart } from './gfx/puppets/grammar';\nexport type { BodyPoint } from './gfx/puppets/grammar';\n--- source structure ---\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/README.md\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/art.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/audio.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/best.test.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/best.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/bot.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/cast/player.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/index.html\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/programme.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/scenes/play.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/styles.css\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/tools/bundle.mjs\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/wobble.ts\n--- main control flow ---\n2:import './styles.css';\n3:import { DAYS, rankFor, type Activity } from './programme';\n4:import { DEFAULT_BALANCE, action, createSession, stepSession, targetFor, type Session } from './wobble';\n5:import { Soundscape } from './audio';\n6:import { welcomeView, hubView, gameView, resultView, modalView } from './view';\n8:type Screen = 'welcome' | 'hub' | 'playing' | 'result';\n9:type Modal = 'settings' | 'about' | 'pause' | 'touch' | null;\n10:type Preferences = { sound: boolean; motion: boolean; contrast: boolean; assist: boolean };\n11:type Save = { unlocked: number; scores: Record<string, number>; preferences: Preferences };\n13:const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#app')!;\n14:const storageKey = 'wee-fit-retreat-save-v1';\n15:const defaults: Save = { unlocked: 0, scores: {}, preferences: { sound: true, motion: false, contrast: false, assist: false } };\n16:function load(): Save {\n22:let save = load();\n23:let screen: Screen = 'welcome';\n24:let modal: Modal = null;\n25:let dayIndex = 0;\n26:let activityIndex = 0;\n27:let session: Session | null = null;\n28:let attract = false;\n29:let lastInput = performance.now();\n30:let lastFrame = 0;\n31:let accumulator = 0;\n32:let lastPadButtons: boolean[] = [];\n33:let lastInputType: 'keyboard' | 'controller' = 'keyboard';\n34:const keys = new Set<string>();\n35:const sounds = new Soundscape();\n38:function persist(): void {\n41:function flatIndex(day: number, activity: number): number {\n44:function selected(): Activity { return DAYS[dayIndex].activities[activityIndex]; }\n45:function selectFlat(index: number): void {\n52:function totalActivities(): number { return DAYS.reduce((total, day) => total + day.activities.length, 0); }\n53:function playSound(name: 'click' | 'hit' | 'finish' | 'miss'): void { try { sounds.play(name); } catch { /* audio is optional */ } }\n54:function isTouchOnly(): boolean {\n57:function render(): void {\n65:function openGame(preview = false): void {\n71:function finish(): void {\n79:function updateGame(): void {\n100:function moveFocus(direction: number): void {\n107:function doFoot(foot: 'left' | 'right' | 'both'): void {\n111:function wake(): void {\n161:function frame(now: number): void {\n--- plan engine and hub ---\n24-rock. On the last night the storm comes, the island tips, and in the finale your thumb's balance *is* the island's.\n25-\n26:**Genre:** a 3D sports and wellness anthology of balance activities around a small walkable island, with a daily-ritual\n27-meta game and a comedy story. **Perspective:** third person throughout: a chase camera on the island, and a purpose-built\n28-camera for each activity (the table in section 6). **Hub genre:** Sports.\n--\n36-3. **Deadpan kindness.** Nobody shouts, nothing is a game over. The game is polite, slightly invasive, and proud of you\n37-   in a way that worries you.\n38:4. **The daily ritual.** A morning check, one big number, a stamp, a growing stack of pebbles. Coming back is the game.\n39-5. **A small joke grows into the world.** The tilt starts as a sign that says \"Please keep to the centre\". It ends with\n40-   a storm and a whole island on your thumb.\n--\n274-10 Expert variants (a smaller ring, more sway), 20 and 30 tracksuit colours and a headband, 40 the \"Unsettling\" stamp set.\n275-\n276:**Exploration.** 20 pebbles, 12 \"Did you know?\" plaques, and each cast member has 3–5 new lines each day. Sit on a bench\n277-to watch the view with the Meditate clip. Wave at Gerald. Plaques visibly creep downhill across the days.\n278-\n--\n280-loose props drift and the sea sits fractionally wrong at the horizon. Only the Great Tilt gives it weight in play.\n281-\n282:**Saves** go in the page store (`createStore`, prefix unique to your game): day, done list, ages, pebbles, finds,\n283-outfits, bests, settings. The sim never reads them: the page hands the sim its starting state through a scene action\n284-(`game.begin`, section 14). Settings has Erase with an in-game confirmation, never `confirm()`.\n--\n365-follow your combo: lose it and they fall out of time, one by one, politely.\n366-\n367:**Beat audio goes on the effects bus, not the music bus.** Music defaults to 10%, so the song is only a bed. Sim `beat`\n368-events fire claps and kicks at full level. The bed has no drums, so nothing flams against it. Timing is in sim steps,\n369-never audio time.\n--\n463-   the East Terrace (a sensor): each one delivered takes off 0.5°. Loungers slide through. Nan walks up on her own and is\n464-   already there.\n465:3. **Counterweights (45 s).** Two pebble carts on rails, cranked by alternating feet while you lean into the slope with the\n466-   Wobble Model: your whole Cairn is on one of them. (First part to cut if the budget runs short.)\n467-4. **The Centre Stone (60 s).** You climb to the summit and stand on the plate that says \"Do not\". The camera pulls back to the\n--\n484-one word, one number, one sentence, one small graph. The dev panel is the only busy screen, and only developers open it.\n485-\n486:**UI look:** pebble-shaped rounded panels in warm off-white with soft shadows, not the source's look. A rounded system stack\n487-(`ui-rounded, \"SF Pro Rounded\", \"Segoe UI Rounded\", system-ui`); fonts are allowed but not needed. Screens are HTML/CSS under\n488-`engine.ui.root`, with `createMenu` for lists (hover already moves its focus, click picks **[source]**) and a small\n--\n511-- **Programme:** today's list as up to four cards with stamps, each with \"Go\". **Noticeboard:** a 3 × 2 page of activity cards with\n512-  best rank; L1, R1 or Q, E page through them.\n513:- **Results:** rank word, score, pebbles falling onto a little cairn, a line from Plumb or Tare; \"Again\" or \"Carry on\".\n514-- **Evening:** calendar stamp, the age graph, a closing remark, \"Sleep\".\n515-- **Pause** (Options or Esc, in play and on the island; pauses the sim with `inspector.pause()`, `modal` keeps keys out of play):\n--\n523-**Dev Mode** (from the pause menu; absent in hub sessions; a clear panel that works with pad, keyboard and mouse):\n524-\n525:- **Live sliders with Reset**, per group and for all: every numeric `game.*` setting in this plan, plus `game.pebbles.mult`. They are\n526-  sim settings with `when: 'now'`, changed by `inspector.set(path, value)`, so they apply at once and replays hold them. Defaults come\n527-  from `inspector.describe('setting', path)` **[tested]**.\n528-- **Jumps:** to any day, any activity, any finale step. Finish activity now at a chosen rank.\n529:- **Cheats:** bot plays for me, no topple, unlock all, give pebbles, reset save, a throwaway save mode (`createStore` `sandbox`).\n530-- **Tools:** time scale (0.25, 1, 4), pause and frame step, free camera (`cam3=fly`), state overlay (CoB, calm, sync, tilt, event,\n531-  phase, tick, hash), seed and new seed, copy tuned settings as JSON.\n--\n565-\n566-Read the protocol once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Fetch by raw URL, into\n567:`labs/game/hub/`: `session.js` (save it as `session-client.txt`), and for tests `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same\n568-folder. **Do not clone the ai-hub repository: it is 5.3 GB.**\n569-\n--\n585-Goal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80. Also `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit.\n586-\n587:**Startup** **[tested: this shape, on the starter's one scene, passed the harness at 2, 3 (host leaving) and 4 players with the engine running in every frame]**:\n588-\n589-```ts\n--\n592-search.set('touch', 'off');\n593-const AIHub = window.AIHub;\n594:const info = AIHub?.active ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\n595-if (info) { search.set('scene', 'game:round'); search.set('seed', String(info.seed)); }\n596:const watchdog = info ? setTimeout(() => AIHub.ready(), 14000) : 0;   // the harness allows 20 s after hello\n597-engine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['game:island', 'game:round'], search: `?${search}`, /* … */ });\n598-if (info) { clearTimeout(watchdog); AIHub.ready(); }\n--\n600-\n601-**The biggest trap in this whole plan [tested]:** the hub opens the page with `?aihub=1&aihub-seed=N`. `createEngine` treats every\n602:unknown query key as a setting and fails with `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, **and the harness still reports PASS**, because the client keeps\n603-answering while the game is dead. Strip those keys, and make your test assert, inside every frame, `__engine.ready === true` and\n604-`__engine.errors.length === 0`.\n--\n609-  mat. It shows the game's title, players in colour with who is ready, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left (from the `card` event).\n610-  Keys: Enter or Cross answers `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T answers `'more'`, a tap or click works too. Listen for Enter with your own\n611:  `keydown` on `window`: the harness sends a synthetic one. The card has no menus or choices, and draws numbers only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n612-  Make it HTML over whatever is drawn, because the watchdog may call `ready()` while the view is still warming up.\n613-- `start` arrives; play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`. Send the sim `round.go` then (scene action). On `start` also send one\n614:  `AIHub.progress({ score: 0, label: 'Breathing in' })` and one ghost message, so a slow copy still passes the harness.\n615-- During play: `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` whenever it changes (label at most 24 characters, \"Class 2 · 640\"), and every 100 ms\n616-  `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', e: classIndex, x, y, p: poseId, s: score }, { reliable: false })`. Never above 20 a second.\n--\n627-- Outside a session (`connect` gives `null`, or no client at all in the dev server) the game must behave exactly as it does alone.\n628-\n629:**Boot deadline, the one place performance matters.** The harness gives every copy 20 s to call `ready()`. **[tested on SwiftShader]** the starter\n630-game alone needed 8–16 s per copy at four copies; the engine's playground needed 52–73 s. So `game:round` is a small separate scene with just the\n631-pavilion, the mats and the cast. The island's cost never reaches a session, and the watchdog covers the rest. Performance is out of scope everywhere else.\n--\n665-a few centimetres to make the water live. Keep walkers out of deep water with a sim clamp; shallows get a splash emitter.\n666-\n667:**Make these as props** (`node x new prop labs/game/props/<name>`; parts are geometry by id and material by id, with `tint`): mats, Tare's Platform, Noticeboard, plaques, Cairn pebbles (squashed rounded\n668-boxes in varied tints), Pavilion (pillars, frustum roof, curtains), Annex with mirror wall, huts, ferry and pier, benches and loungers, parasols, palms (limb trunk, flattened boxes), rocks, lighthouse,\n669-buoys, paddleboard, slackline posts and line, tray with ridges and holes (ring), marbles (a rounded box with maximum radius), hoops (ring), step platforms and floor tiles, counterweight carts and rails,\n--\n676-screen Tare's dial is a large CSS dial with a live needle. The Gull and the Frog are engine **blob rigs** (with wings for the Gull) as crowd bodies: `addAgent`, `crowdBody`, cheap and very funny; `labs/box/cast/` has worked examples.\n677-\n678:**Effects** (`defineEmitter`): ripple rings, splashes small and huge, pebble clack dust, calm wave, sparkle on stamps, seagull feathers, confetti on Unsettling, rain and spray in the storm. Built-ins worth using:\n679-`emitter:confetti`, `bubbles`, `dust`, `rain`, `fountain`, `glints`, `fireflies`.\n680-\n--\n735-All sound is code and data. No audio files. Test: the built HTML holds no `data:audio`, `.mp3`, `.wav` or `.ogg`.\n736-\n737:**Music, original, tracker notation** (`defineSong`; `node x new song`; test with `node x audio song:<id>`): light, slightly over-pleasant lobby music with plucks and soft marimba, never a melody from the source.\n738-\n739-| Song | Use | Character |\n--\n748-| `song:stamp` | Results | A short jingle, played once |\n749-\n750:**Music is 10% by default:** right after `createAudio()`, call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)`. The engine's default is 0.5 **[source]**. Settings shows it as 10%. Test `audio.volume('music') === 0.1` on a fresh save. Mix each song so it is fine at 100% and a whisper at 10%; nothing the player needs may live only in music.\n751-\n752-**Voices: Animalese-style gibberish, written in code.** The engine has no speech. Build it from sound data:\n--\n776-- **`say(speaker, text)`** in `labs/game/audio/voice.ts`: one syllable per two letters, hashed from the letters so the same line always babbles the same way; `audio.play(id, { pitch, when, vol, bus: 'ui', duck: true })`; pitch contour rises on \"?\" and falls on \".\"; text types in sync. Voices slider scales `vol`. Silence on spaces, longer on punctuation.\n777-\n778:**Effects** (`defineSfx`, plus built-ins `sfx:select`, `sfx:confirm`, `sfx:cancel`, `sfx:coin`, `sfx:step*`): wobble creak with pitch by `r`; breath in and out (filtered noise); mat squeak; stamp thump; pebble clack; small and huge splashes; gull squawk; frog ribbit; rope creak; marble roll, a loop with level by speed; hoop whoosh; clap, kick, hat; whistle; ferry horn; thunder; the island's deep groan, pitched by tilt; polite crowd \"ooh\". **Ambience:** sea, birds, wind, rain, as loops with `loop` passes.\n779-\n780-In `onFrame`: `audio.update(frame.camera, frame.queries ?? undefined)`, then play each new sim event by `seq` from `frame.world.events.trace()`. Reset your `seq` when `frame.world` changes (after a restart).\n781-\n782:**Checks:** `node x qa audio`, and in the browser read levels with an `AnalyserNode` or render through an `OfflineAudioContext` (`createAudio({ context })`). Nobody can listen here, so prove each voice and song makes sound, and that music sits at 10%.\n783-\n784----\n--\n880-```\n881-\n882:**Key components** (plain data): `flow` (mode: front, roam, event, cutscene, results; event, phase, tick; day), `wobble` (per seat), `seat` (input per seat), `island` (tilt), `round`, `pebble`, `plaque`, `ghost`, plus one per activity. Time in whole steps, randomness from named streams, loops in `w.query` order, `Math.pow` not `**`.\n883-\n884-**The single HTML [tested: 6.7 MB, 4 s, opens from file://, client stays byte-identical].** `node x html` is engine-only, so the game carries this. The session client goes in as text, so no formatter ever touches it: the hub rejects an edited copy by SHA-256.\n--\n924-| Trap | What happens | Do this |\n925-|---|---|---|\n926:| Hub's `?aihub=…` in the query | `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, engine dead, harness still passes | Strip them; assert `__engine.ready` in every frame |\n927-| No `CHROMIUM_PATH` | `x shot` and friends crash on `/opt/pw-browsers/chromium` | Export the headless shell path (section 14) |\n928-| A crashed `x` browser launch | The process hangs after printing the crash | Wrap browser commands in `timeout` |\n--\n938-| `input.prompt()` **[source]** | Xbox labels for unknown pads | Own glyph table (section 4) |\n939-| Engine touch stick **[source]** | Appears on touch screens | `touch=off` in the query |\n940:| Bus defaults **[source]** | Music 0.5 | `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` |\n941-| Hub client through a formatter **[source]** | Hub rejects it | Keep it as `.txt`, inject at build |\n942-| `git` in the dev folder | It belongs to the larger repository around it | Do not `git init`, commit or restore there, despite `AGENTS.md`'s \"commit as you go\", unless your TASK.md asks |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
