{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_574","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"P='Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- task ---'; cat TASK.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- source and scene APIs ---'; sed -n '1,210p' \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/main.ts\"; sed -n '\"'1,200p' \\\"\"'$P/engine/sim/scene.ts\"; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- view exports ---'; rg -n '\"'^export|id=\"|id='\"\\\\\\\\\\\"' \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/view.ts\" | cut -c1-350; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- package ---'; cat \\\"\"'$P/package.json\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_574","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"P='Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- task ---'; cat TASK.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- source and scene APIs ---'; sed -n '1,210p' \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/main.ts\"; sed -n '\"'1,200p' \\\"\"'$P/engine/sim/scene.ts\"; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- view exports ---'; rg -n '\"'^export|id=\"|id='\"\\\\\\\\\\\"' \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/view.ts\" | cut -c1-350; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- package ---'; cat \\\"\"'$P/package.json\"'","aggregated_output":"--- task ---\nSOURCE: Wii Fit\n\nGenre: Pick the game genre(s) that best fit the source and would make the best game.\n\nPerspective: Pick the camera perspective(s) that best fit the genre and source and would make the best game.\n\nGame Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\n\nResearch: Whether and how much to research is your choice.\n\nPackage: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\n\nTech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge#make-a-game-with-my-3dge, in the engine's full workspace. The engine stays read-only, as the AGENTS.md it gives your game says: add whatever systems, art assets and animations the game needs on top of it. The rest of the tech stack is your choice.\n\nArt Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic props.\n\nAnimation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\n\nAudio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\n\nOnline: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub\n\nWorking Environment and deliverable:\nCreate a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\n\nPerformance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\n\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\nEffort: Spend effort however you see fit.\n\n## This computer\nChecked 2026-11-04 20:05 (America/Vancouver) by node check-environment.mjs.\n\n- **Computer:** Worki9: 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K, 32 cores, 20 GB RAM, 8 GB swap. Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS on WSL2 (Linux 6.18.33.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2).\n- **Space:** 850 GB free in the home folder. /tmp: 9.8 GB, in memory (tmpfs), 8.2 GB free when checked.\n- **Display:** none for runs (they run with DISPLAY unset), so a headed browser needs xvfb-run.\n- **Browsers:** Playwright 1.63.0 for Python (from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright), with Chromium 153.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered; WebGPU, software-rendered, when started with --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader), Firefox 155.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered), WebKit 26.6 (WebGL 2) already downloaded. Phone and tablet device profiles are built in.\n  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\n  For Node, `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder uses the browsers already downloaded; another version downloads its own.\n  Playwright runs here with PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 (already set for runs): this OS isn't one it supports by name.\n- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\n- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\n- **Not installed:** sox, bun, deno.\n- **Network:** internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).\n- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \"Target closed\", \"page crashed\" or \"browser has been closed\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\n\n### What this computer doesn't have\n\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n\n### Sharing this computer\n\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\n\n## Goal\n\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\n\nScope\n\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\n\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\n\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\n\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\n\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\n\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\n\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\n\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\n\n## Done\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n\n## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:40:55\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n  }\n}\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n\nTesting Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch?\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n\nEngine Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about the engine?\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n\nPrompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n- What would you change in this prompt?\n--- source and scene APIs ---\n/** @file Runs the retreat's menus, input, and balance sessions. */\nimport './styles.css';\nimport { DAYS, rankFor, type Activity } from './programme';\nimport { DEFAULT_BALANCE, action, createSession, stepSession, targetFor, type Session } from './wobble';\nimport { Soundscape } from './audio';\nimport { welcomeView, hubView, gameView, resultView, modalView } from './view';\n\ntype Screen = 'welcome' | 'hub' | 'playing' | 'result';\ntype Modal = 'settings' | 'about' | 'pause' | 'touch' | null;\ntype Preferences = { sound: boolean; motion: boolean; contrast: boolean; assist: boolean };\ntype Save = { unlocked: number; scores: Record<string, number>; preferences: Preferences };\n\nconst root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#app')!;\nconst storageKey = 'wee-fit-retreat-save-v1';\nconst defaults: Save = { unlocked: 0, scores: {}, preferences: { sound: true, motion: false, contrast: false, assist: false } };\nfunction load(): Save {\n  try {\n    const saved = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(storageKey) || '{}') as Partial<Save>;\n    return { ...defaults, ...saved, scores: saved.scores || {}, preferences: { ...defaults.preferences, ...saved.preferences } };\n  } catch { return structuredClone(defaults); }\n}\nlet save = load();\nlet screen: Screen = 'welcome';\nlet modal: Modal = null;\nlet dayIndex = 0;\nlet activityIndex = 0;\nlet session: Session | null = null;\nlet attract = false;\nlet lastInput = performance.now();\nlet lastFrame = 0;\nlet accumulator = 0;\nlet lastPadButtons: boolean[] = [];\nlet lastInputType: 'keyboard' | 'controller' = 'keyboard';\nconst keys = new Set<string>();\nconst sounds = new Soundscape();\nsounds.enabled = save.preferences.sound;\n\nfunction persist(): void {\n  try { localStorage.setItem(storageKey, JSON.stringify(save)); } catch { /* storage can be unavailable */ }\n}\nfunction flatIndex(day: number, activity: number): number {\n  return DAYS.slice(0, day).reduce((total, item) => total + item.activities.length, 0) + activity;\n}\nfunction selected(): Activity { return DAYS[dayIndex].activities[activityIndex]; }\nfunction selectFlat(index: number): void {\n  let remaining = index;\n  for (let day = 0; day < DAYS.length; day++) {\n    if (remaining < DAYS[day].activities.length) { dayIndex = day; activityIndex = remaining; return; }\n    remaining -= DAYS[day].activities.length;\n  }\n}\nfunction totalActivities(): number { return DAYS.reduce((total, day) => total + day.activities.length, 0); }\nfunction playSound(name: 'click' | 'hit' | 'finish' | 'miss'): void { try { sounds.play(name); } catch { /* audio is optional */ } }\nfunction isTouchOnly(): boolean {\n  return matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)').matches && !Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.() || []).some(Boolean);\n}\nfunction render(): void {\n  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('reduced-motion', save.preferences.motion);\n  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('high-contrast', save.preferences.contrast);\n  const content = screen === 'welcome' ? welcomeView(isTouchOnly()) : screen === 'hub' ? hubView(dayIndex, activityIndex, save.unlocked, save.scores) : screen === 'playing' && session ? gameView(session, attract, lastInputType) : session ? resultView(session) : '';\n  root.innerHTML = content + (modal ? modalView(modal, save.preferences) : '');\n  if (screen === 'playing') updateGame();\n  if (modal) root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.modal button, .modal input')?.focus();\n}\nfunction openGame(preview = false): void {\n  if (!preview && isTouchOnly()) { modal = 'touch'; render(); return; }\n  session = createSession(selected(), 13 + flatIndex(dayIndex, activityIndex));\n  attract = preview; screen = 'playing'; modal = null; lastFrame = 0; accumulator = 0;\n  keys.clear(); render();\n}\nfunction finish(): void {\n  if (!session) return;\n  if (attract) { screen = 'welcome'; attract = false; session = null; lastInput = performance.now(); render(); return; }\n  const index = flatIndex(dayIndex, activityIndex);\n  save.scores[session.activity.id] = Math.max(save.scores[session.activity.id] || 0, session.score);\n  save.unlocked = Math.min(totalActivities() - 1, Math.max(save.unlocked, index + 1));\n  persist(); playSound('finish'); screen = 'result'; render();\n}\nfunction updateGame(): void {\n  if (!session) return;\n  const balance = session.balance;\n  const target = targetFor(session);\n  const ball = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#balance-ball');\n  const marker = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#balance-target');\n  if (ball) { ball.style.left = `${50 + balance.x * 40}%`; ball.style.top = `${50 + balance.y * 40}%`; }\n  if (marker) { marker.style.left = `${50 + target.x * 40}%`; marker.style.top = `${50 + target.y * 40}%`; }\n  const timer = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-time');\n  if (timer) { const remaining = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(session.activity.duration - session.time)); timer.textContent = `${Math.floor(remaining / 60)}:${String(remaining % 60).padStart(2, '0')}`; }\n  const cue = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-cue');\n  if (cue) cue.textContent = balance.recovering > 0 ? 'Take a breath. Find your footing.' : target.label || session.cue || 'Find your centre';\n  const score = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-score');\n  if (score) score.textContent = `${Math.round(session.samples ? session.scoreSum / session.samples : 0)}`;\n  const falls = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-falls');\n  if (falls) falls.textContent = String(balance.falls);\n  const progress = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-progress');\n  if (progress) progress.style.width = `${Math.min(100, session.time / session.activity.duration * 100)}%`;\n  const person = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.guest-art');\n  if (person) person.style.setProperty('--lean', `${Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, balance.x)) * 11}deg`);\n}\nfunction moveFocus(direction: number): void {\n  const scope = modal ? root.querySelector('.modal') : root;\n  const focusables = Array.from(scope?.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('button:not(:disabled), input:not(:disabled)') || []);\n  if (!focusables.length) return;\n  const current = focusables.indexOf(document.activeElement as HTMLElement);\n  focusables[(current + direction + focusables.length) % focusables.length].focus();\n}\nfunction doFoot(foot: 'left' | 'right' | 'both'): void {\n  if (!session || screen !== 'playing' || modal || attract) return;\n  playSound(action(session, foot) ? 'hit' : 'miss');\n}\nfunction wake(): void {\n  lastInput = performance.now();\n  if (attract) { attract = false; session = null; screen = 'welcome'; render(); }\n}\nroot.addEventListener('click', (event) => {\n  const button = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLElement>('[data-action]');\n  if (!button) return;\n  if (attract) { wake(); return; }\n  wake(); const command = button.dataset.action; playSound('click');\n  if (command === 'begin') { screen = 'hub'; selectFlat(save.unlocked); }\n  else if (command === 'home') { screen = 'welcome'; session = null; }\n  else if (command === 'settings' || command === 'about') modal = command;\n  else if (command === 'close') modal = null;\n  else if (command === 'pause') modal = 'pause';\n  else if (command === 'resume') { modal = null; lastFrame = 0; }\n  else if (command === 'quit') { modal = null; session = null; screen = 'hub'; }\n  else if (command === 'reset') {\n    if (window.confirm('Reset all retreat progress and scores?')) { save = structuredClone(defaults); sounds.enabled = save.preferences.sound; persist(); dayIndex = 0; activityIndex = 0; }\n  } else if (command === 'day') { dayIndex = Number(button.dataset.day); activityIndex = 0; }\n  else if (command === 'activity') activityIndex = Number(button.dataset.index);\n  else if (command === 'start' || command === 'retry') { openGame(); return; }\n  else if (command === 'continue') { screen = 'hub'; session = null; selectFlat(save.unlocked); }\n  render();\n});\nroot.addEventListener('change', (event) => {\n  const input = event.target as HTMLInputElement;\n  const key = input.dataset.preference as keyof Preferences | undefined;\n  if (!key) return;\n  save.preferences[key] = input.checked; sounds.enabled = save.preferences.sound; persist(); render();\n});\nwindow.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n  const key = event.key.toLowerCase();\n  if (attract) { event.preventDefault(); wake(); return; }\n  lastInput = performance.now(); lastInputType = 'keyboard';\n  if (key === 'escape') { event.preventDefault(); if (modal) modal = null; else if (screen === 'playing') modal = 'pause'; render(); return; }\n  if (screen === 'playing' && !modal) {\n    if (['arrowup','arrowdown','arrowleft','arrowright',' ','q','e'].includes(key)) event.preventDefault();\n    keys.add(key);\n    if (!event.repeat && key === 'q') doFoot('left');\n    if (!event.repeat && key === 'e') doFoot('right');\n    if (!event.repeat && key === ' ') doFoot('both');\n  } else if (['arrowup','arrowdown','arrowleft','arrowright'].includes(key)) {\n    event.preventDefault(); moveFocus(key === 'arrowup' || key === 'arrowleft' ? -1 : 1);\n  }\n});\nwindow.addEventListener('keyup', (event) => keys.delete(event.key.toLowerCase()));\nwindow.addEventListener('blur', () => keys.clear());\ndocument.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => { lastFrame = 0; });\nwindow.addEventListener('pointerdown', () => { if (attract) wake(); else lastInput = performance.now(); });\n\nfunction frame(now: number): void {\n  const pad = Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.() || []).find(Boolean);\n  let stickX = 0; let stickY = 0; let gentle = false;\n  if (pad) {\n    stickX = Math.abs(pad.axes[0] || 0) > .13 ? pad.axes[0] : 0;\n    stickY = Math.abs(pad.axes[1] || 0) > .13 ? pad.axes[1] : 0;\n    gentle = !!pad.buttons[7]?.pressed;\n    const buttons = pad.buttons.map((button) => button.pressed);\n    const pressed = (index: number) => buttons[index] && !lastPadButtons[index];\n    if (buttons.some((button, index) => button && !lastPadButtons[index]) || stickX || stickY) {\n      if (attract) wake();\n      lastInput = now; lastInputType = 'controller';\n    }\n    if (pressed(9) || pressed(3)) { if (screen === 'playing') { modal = modal ? null : 'pause'; render(); } }\n    if (screen === 'playing' && !modal) {\n      if (pressed(4)) doFoot('left'); if (pressed(5)) doFoot('right'); if (pressed(0)) doFoot('both');\n    } else {\n      if (pressed(12) || pressed(14)) moveFocus(-1);\n      if (pressed(13) || pressed(15)) moveFocus(1);\n      if (pressed(0)) (document.activeElement as HTMLElement | null)?.click();\n      if (pressed(1) && modal) { modal = null; render(); }\n    }\n    lastPadButtons = buttons;\n  } else lastPadButtons = [];\n  if (screen === 'welcome' && !modal && now - lastInput > 60000) { dayIndex = 0; activityIndex = 0; openGame(true); }\n  if (screen === 'playing' && session && !modal && !document.hidden) {\n    const elapsed = lastFrame ? Math.min((now - lastFrame) / 1000, .1) : 0;\n    accumulator += elapsed;\n    const input = attract ? { x: Math.sin(now / 1800) * .25, y: Math.cos(now / 2400) * .2, gentle: true } : {\n      x: Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, stickX + Number(keys.has('d') || keys.has('arrowright')) - Number(keys.has('a') || keys.has('arrowleft')))),\n      y: Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, stickY + Number(keys.has('s') || keys.has('arrowdown')) - Number(keys.has('w') || keys.has('arrowup')))),\n      gentle: gentle || keys.has('shift'),\n    };\n    const settings = save.preferences.assist ? { ...DEFAULT_BALANCE, gain: DEFAULT_BALANCE.gain * .7, instability: DEFAULT_BALANCE.instability * .7, damping: DEFAULT_BALANCE.damping * 1.3 } : DEFAULT_BALANCE;\n    while (accumulator >= 1 / 60 && !session.finished) { stepSession(session, input, settings, 1 / 60); accumulator -= 1 / 60; }\n    updateGame();\n    if (session.finished) finish();\n  }\n  lastFrame = now; requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\nrender(); requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n/**\n * @file Scenes, sim-side (PLAN.md §6.9, §9.0, WP 1.5; doctrines: Reproducible, Agent-operable):\n * `defineScene(id, { level?, settings, setup, step })` registers a scene as an entry of the registry kind `scene`;\n * `startScene` makes its world (a settings store with the scene's settings over the defaults and the caller's over\n * those, a world seeded from the seed, the scene's `step` as the system `scene`, then its `setup`). A session\n * (engine/sim/session.ts `createSession`) starts one that records its inputs. The kernel fixture, the box's scenes and\n * `createHeadless` (WP 1.6) all start scenes here, so no scene imports `app/`; engine/sim/replay.ts plays them.\n *\n * A scene is game code: `setup(w)` spawns, adds systems and listeners (inside `w.run`, so under the fdlibm swap);\n * `step(w, intents)` runs every sim step as the system `scene`, first in the phase `intents`, ahead of the systems\n * setup adds there; `actions` are its dev actions, `(w, args) => void` by name (WP 5.6 adds the engine's own).\n * `level` names the level it loads (WP 2.2 compiles it), `terrain` its ground (WP 10.5, engine/world/terrain.ts) and\n * `site` the levels standing on a terrain (WP 13.15, engine/world/site.ts): the view draws them; its setup adds their\n * bodies. `physics: true` gives it a physics world (physicsOf, WP 3.1).\n * `sounds(record, w)` says which sound a traced sim event plays, `{ sfx, vol?, variant? }`, a list of them (a shot and\n * where it strikes, WP 13.22) or null, for `x audio --replay` (WP 9.4): by default the event payload's own\n * (`payloadSound`); a game that maps its events to sounds sets its map here, so Node hears what its pages play (after\n * G9, ADR-0013 amendment 3).\n * Seeds are whole numbers from 0 (`checkSeed`, `SIM_BAD_SEED`).\n *\n * Invariants: a scene's `settings` are checked against the settings schema when it is defined (`CORE_BAD_SPEC`\n * naming each problem), so declare its settings before it; they apply for the run's lifetime, as an override layer\n * (engine/core/settings.ts), and the caller's settings (`--set`, a replay's `settings`) go on top. Each start makes\n * a new settings store and world, so runs share nothing but the registry. A missing scene id is `CORE_NO_ENTRY`.\n *\n * @example\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\n * const reg = createRegistry();\n * let made = 0;\n * defineScene('demo', { description: 'Counts its steps.', setup: (w) => w.spawn(), step: () => made++ }, reg);\n * const { world } = startScene('demo', { seed: 3, registry: reg });\n * world.step({});\n * [world.count, made]; // [1, 1]\n * @see engine/sim/scene.test.ts\n */\nimport type { EventMap, TraceRecord } from '../core/events';\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, type Log } from '../core/log';\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { isPlainObject, show, type Schema } from '../core/schema';\nimport { createSettings, type Settings } from '../core/settings';\nimport type { Intents } from '../input/intents';\nimport { attachPhysics, scenePhysics } from '../physics/binding';\nimport type { AnyComponents, PhysicsHook } from './state';\nimport { createWorld, type SystemProbe, type World } from './world';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const SCENE_CODES = defineCodes('sim', {\n  SIM_BAD_SEED: {\n    template: '{where} got the seed {value}, which a replay cannot hold',\n    fix: 'pass a whole number, 0 or more (x sim --seed 3, __engine.seed(3)): record() writes the seed into the replay',\n  },\n});\n\n/** Returns `seed` (1 when absent; -0 as 0); throws `SIM_BAD_SEED` naming `where` unless it is a whole number from 0. */\nexport function checkSeed(seed: unknown, where: string): number {\n  if (seed === undefined) return 1;\n  if (Number.isInteger(seed) && (seed as number) >= 0) return (seed as number) + 0; // -0 + 0 is 0\n  throw codeError('SIM_BAD_SEED', { where, value: show(seed) });\n}\n\n/** A dev action of a scene: runs between steps inside `w.run`, with plain-data `args`; recorded in replays. */\nexport type SceneAction<W> = (w: W, args: unknown) => void;\n\n/** A sound a sim event plays: an `sfx` entry, its gain (1 by default) and its variant (the effect's next by default). */\nexport interface SceneSound {\n  readonly sfx: string;\n  readonly vol?: number;\n  readonly variant?: number;\n}\n\n/** The sound a traced event names in its payload, `{ sfx, vol?, variant? }`, or null: a scene's default `sounds`. */\nexport function payloadSound(record: TraceRecord): SceneSound | null {\n  const payload = record.payload;\n  if (!isPlainObject(payload) || payload.sfx === undefined) return null;\n  return { sfx: payload.sfx, vol: payload.vol, variant: payload.variant } as SceneSound;\n}\n\n/** How a scene is written: `defineScene(id, spec)`. */\nexport interface SceneSpec<C extends object = AnyComponents, E extends EventMap = EventMap> {\n  /** What the scene shows or tests, in plain sentences. */\n  description?: string;\n  /** The level it loads (`level:<name>`), when it has one (WP 2.2). */\n  level?: string;\n  /** Its terrain (`terrain:<name>`), when it has one (WP 10.5). */\n  terrain?: string;\n  /** Its site (`site:<name>`: levels on a terrain), when it has one (WP 13.15). */\n  site?: string;\n  /** Whether it has a physics world (WP 3.1): `physicsOf(w)` reaches it, the system `physics` steps it. */\n  physics?: boolean;\n  /** Setting values for its lifetime, path → value (schema-checked). */\n  settings?: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>>;\n  /** Runs once when it starts: spawns, systems, listeners. */\n  setup: (w: World<C, E>) => void;\n  /** Runs every step, first in the phase `intents`: reads the step's intents and components, writes components. */\n  step?: (w: World<C, E>, intents: Intents) => void;\n  /** Its dev actions, by name. */\n  actions?: Readonly<Record<string, SceneAction<World<C, E>>>>;\n  /** The sounds each traced sim event plays, read as the event is delivered (`x audio --replay`); `payloadSound`. */\n  sounds?: (record: TraceRecord, w: World<C, E>) => SceneSound | readonly SceneSound[] | null;\n}\n\n/** A defined scene: its spec with defaults filled, plus `id` and `kind`. */\nexport type Scene<C extends object = AnyComponents, E extends EventMap = EventMap> = Readonly<\n  Required<Omit<SceneSpec<C, E>, 'level' | 'terrain' | 'site'>> & Pick<SceneSpec<C, E>, 'level' | 'terrain' | 'site'>\n> & { readonly id: string; readonly kind: 'scene' };\n\n/** The fields of a `scene` entry. */\nconst SCENE_FIELDS = {\n  description: { type: 'string', default: '', description: 'What the scene shows or tests, in plain sentences.' },\n  level: { type: 'string', description: 'The level it loads (level:<name>, compiled by WP 2.2), when it has one.' },\n  terrain: { type: 'string', description: 'Its terrain (terrain:<name>, WP 10.5), when it has one.' },\n  site: { type: 'string', description: 'Its site (site:<name>: levels on a terrain, WP 13.15), when it has one.' },\n  physics: { type: 'boolean', default: false, description: 'Whether it has a physics world: physicsOf(w) reaches it.' },\n  settings: {\n    type: 'object',\n    default: {},\n    description: \"Setting values for the scene's lifetime, path → value, checked against the settings schema.\",\n  },\n  setup: {\n    type: 'function',\n    required: true,\n    description: 'Runs once when the scene starts, inside w.run: spawns, systems, listeners. (w) => void.',\n  },\n  step: {\n    type: 'function',\n    default: () => {},\n    description: \"Runs every sim step as the system 'scene', first in the phase intents. (w, intents) => void.\",\n  },\n  actions: {\n    type: 'object',\n    default: {},\n    description: 'Dev actions by name, (w, args) => void: run between steps by a session and recorded in replays.',\n  },\n  sounds: {\n    type: 'function',\n    default: payloadSound,\n    description:\n      \"The sounds each traced sim event plays, for x audio --replay: (record, w) => { sfx, vol?, variant? }, a list of them, or null; by default the payload's own sfx.\",\n  },\n} as const satisfies Schema;\n\n/** The problems of a scene entry beyond its fields: settings the schema refuses, actions that are not functions. */\nfunction sceneProblems(entry: Entry, registry: Registry): string[] {\n  const problems: string[] = [];\n  const actions = entry.actions as Record<string, unknown>;\n  for (const [name, action] of Object.entries(actions)) {\n    if (typeof action !== 'function') problems.push(`actions.${name} is not a function (w, args) => void`);\n  }\n  try {\n    createSettings({ registry }).override(entry.settings as Record<string, unknown>, `scene ${entry.id}`);\n  } catch (error) {\n    problems.push(`settings: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}`);\n  }\n  return problems;\n}\n\n/** Declares the kind `scene` on `registry` unless it has it. */\nfunction sceneKind(registry: Registry): void {\n  if (registry.kinds().includes('scene')) return;\n  registry.defineKind('scene', {\n    description:\n      'Scenes: a level, settings, a setup and a step, sim-side, so x sim, x replay and createHeadless run them in Node.',\n    fields: SCENE_FIELDS,\n    defineWith: \"defineScene('<id>', { setup(w) { … }, step(w, intents) { … } })\",\n    check: (entry) => sceneProblems(entry, registry),\n  });\n}\nsceneKind(sharedRegistry);\n\n/**\n * Registers a scene on `registry` (the shared one by default) and returns it. Throws `CORE_BAD_SPEC` for a bad field\n * or a setting the schema refuses, `CORE_DUPLICATE_ID` when defined twice.\n */\nexport function defineScene<C extends object = AnyComponents, E extends EventMap = EventMap>(\n  id: string,\n  spec: SceneSpec<C, E>,\n  registry: Registry = sharedRegistry,\n): Scene<C, E> {\n  sceneKind(registry);\n  return registry.def('scene', id, spec as unknown as Record<string, unknown>) as unknown as Scene<C, E>;\n}\n\n/** The scene `id` on `registry` (the shared one by default). Throws `CORE_NO_ENTRY` naming the closest ids. */\nexport function getScene(id: string, registry: Registry = sharedRegistry): Scene {\n  sceneKind(registry);\n  return registry.get('scene', id) as unknown as Scene;\n}\n\n/** Whether `value` is a defined scene (an entry of kind `scene`), as a module exports it. */\nexport function isScene(value: unknown): value is Scene {\n  return isPlainObject(value) && value.kind === 'scene' && typeof value.id === 'string';\n}\n\n/** How a scene starts. */\nexport interface SceneOptions {\n  /** The seed every sim RNG stream derives from (1). */\n  seed?: number;\n  /** Setting values over the scene's, path → value (`--set`, a replay's `settings`). */\n  settings?: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>>;\n  /** Where the scene, its components and its settings are declared (the shared registry). */\n--- view exports ---\n11:export function welcomeView(touch: boolean): string {\n14:export function hubView(dayIndex: number, activityIndex: number, unlocked: number, scores: Record<string, number>): string {\n26:export function gameView(session: Session, attract: boolean, input: 'keyboard' | 'controller'): string {\n28:  return `<div class=\"site game-site\">${header(attract ? 'A LITTLE PREVIEW' : activity.location.toUpperCase())}<main class=\"game-main\"><div class=\"game-title\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> ${attract ? 'IDLE PREVIEW · ANY INPUT TO RETURN' : 'A MOMENT FOR YOURSELF'}</div><h1>${activity.title}</h1><p>${activity.instruction\n30:export function resultView(session: Session): string {\n34:export function modalView(modal: string, preferences: Preferences): string {\n--- package ---\n{\n  \"name\": \"wee-fit-retreat\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"description\": \"A game made with the my-3dge engine.\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=24.10 <25\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc -b tsconfig.check.json\",\n    \"lint\": \"eslint --cache --cache-location node_modules/.cache/eslint/ .\",\n    \"format\": \"prettier --write --cache .\",\n    \"check\": \"node tools/checkAll.ts\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\": \"0.21.0\",\n    \"@stdlib/math-base-special-cos\": \"0.3.1\",\n    \"@stdlib/math-base-special-pow\": \"0.3.1\",\n    \"@stdlib/math-base-special-sin\": \"0.3.1\",\n    \"three\": \"0.182.0\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"1.32.2\",\n    \"@playwright/test\": \"1.64.1\",\n    \"@stryker-mutator/core\": \"9.6.1\",\n    \"@stryker-mutator/vitest-runner\": \"9.6.1\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"24.19.2\",\n    \"@types/three\": \"0.182.0\",\n    \"eslint\": \"9.39.5\",\n    \"eslint-plugin-jsdoc\": \"61.7.1\",\n    \"globals\": \"16.5.0\",\n    \"prettier\": \"3.9.10\",\n    \"tsx\": \"4.23.15\",\n    \"typescript\": \"5.9.3\",\n    \"typescript-eslint\": \"8.72.1\",\n    \"vite\": \"7.3.7\",\n    \"vitest\": \"4.1.12\"\n  },\n  \"allowScripts\": {\n    \"esbuild\": false\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_575","type":"reasoning","text":"**Inspecting APIs and docs**"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_576","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"P='Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- game view ---'; sed -n '1,50p' \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/view.ts\" | fold -w 180 | head -n 105; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- main control flow ---'; sed -n '1,180p' \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/main.ts\"; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- engine files ---'; ls \\\"\"'$P/engine\"/{gfx,sim}; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- starter scene imports ---'; sed -n '1,130p' \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/scenes/play.ts\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_576","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"P='Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- game view ---'; sed -n '1,50p' \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/view.ts\" | fold -w 180 | head -n 105; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- main control flow ---'; sed -n '1,180p' \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/main.ts\"; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- engine files ---'; ls \\\"\"'$P/engine\"/{gfx,sim}; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- starter scene imports ---'; sed -n '1,130p' \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/scenes/play.ts\"'","aggregated_output":"--- game view ---\n/** @file Builds the original retreat interface and accessible menus. */\nimport { DAYS, rankFor } from './programme';\nimport { characterArt, islandArt } from './art';\nimport type { Session } from './wobble';\n\ntype Preferences = { sound: boolean; motion: boolean; contrast: boolean; assist: boolean };\nfunction header(label = 'YOUR LITTLE ISLAND'): string {\n  return `<header class=\"topbar\"><button class=\"brand\" data-action=\"home\" aria-label=\"Return to title\"><span class=\"brand-icon\">✳</span><span>WEE FIT <b>RETREAT</b></span></button>\n<span class=\"top-label\">${label}</span><button class=\"icon-button\" data-action=\"settings\" aria-label=\"Settings\">⚙</button></header>`;\n}\nfunction duration(seconds: number): string { return `${Math.ceil(seconds / 60)} MIN`; }\nexport function welcomeView(touch: boolean): string {\n  return `<div class=\"site welcome\">${header()}<main class=\"welcome-main\"><div class=\"hero-copy\"><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> A MOST GENTLE ESCAPE</div><h1>Fi\nnd your<br><em>almost</em> balance.</h1><p>Welcome to a little island where the air is fresh, the hosts are encouraging, and standing still is surprisingly ambitious.</p><div class\n=\"hero-actions\"><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"begin\">Begin your stay <span>→</span></button><button class=\"text-button\" data-action=\"about\">What is this place? <span>↗</span\n></button></div>${touch ? '<p class=\"touch-notice\">Controller or keyboard required to play. Settings and the idle preview are available.</p>' : '<div class=\"control-note\"><span cla\nss=\"keycap\">↵</span> KEYBOARD &nbsp; OR &nbsp; CONTROLLER FRIENDLY</div>'}</div><div class=\"hero-art\"><div class=\"sun-halo\"></div>${islandArt()}<div class=\"postcard\"><span class=\"p\nostcard-mark\">✳</span><div><b>A slower kind of holiday</b><small>YOUR RETREAT AWAITS</small></div></div><div class=\"art-caption\">EST. SOMEWHERE PEACEFUL &nbsp; · &nbsp; 01 / 05</di\nv></div></main><footer class=\"welcome-footer\"><span>TAKE YOUR TIME. YOU'RE ON ISLAND TIME.</span><button class=\"footer-link\" data-action=\"about\">ABOUT &amp; CREDITS</button></foote\nr></div>`;\n}\nexport function hubView(dayIndex: number, activityIndex: number, unlocked: number, scores: Record<string, number>): string {\n  const day = DAYS[dayIndex]; const chosen = day.activities[activityIndex];\n  const offset = DAYS.slice(0, dayIndex).reduce((total, item) => total + item.activities.length, 0);\n  const locked = offset + activityIndex > unlocked;\n  const complete = Object.keys(scores).length;\n  const tabs = DAYS.map((item, index) => `<button class=\"day-tab ${index === dayIndex ? 'active' : ''}\" data-action=\"day\" data-day=\"${index}\" aria-pressed=\"${index === dayIndex}\"><\nspan>DAY ${String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><b>${item.title}</b></button>`).join('');\n  const items = day.activities.map((item, index) => {\n    const isLocked = offset + index > unlocked; const score = scores[item.id];\n    return `<button class=\"activity-row ${index === activityIndex ? 'selected' : ''} ${isLocked ? 'locked' : ''}\" data-action=\"activity\" data-index=\"${index}\" aria-pressed=\"${index\n === activityIndex}\"><span class=\"activity-number\">${isLocked ? '·' : String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><span class=\"activity-name\"><b>${item.title}</b><small>${item.locati\non} &nbsp; · &nbsp; ${duration(item.duration)}</small></span><span class=\"row-status\">${score !== undefined ? '✓' : isLocked ? 'LOCKED' : '→'}</span></button>`;\n  }).join('');\n  return `<div class=\"site hub\">${header('YOUR RETREAT PROGRAMME')}<main class=\"hub-main\"><div class=\"hub-heading\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> MAKE YOUR\nSELF AT HOME</div><h1>Your island <em>itinerary.</em></h1><p>One small wobble at a time. There is no rush.</p></div><div class=\"stay-progress\"><span>YOUR STAY SO FAR</span><b>${Str\ning(complete).padStart(2, '0')} <small>experiences enjoyed</small></b></div></div><nav class=\"days\" aria-label=\"Retreat days\">${tabs}</nav><div class=\"hub-grid\"><section class=\"pro\ngramme\"><div class=\"section-kicker\">DAY ${String(dayIndex + 1).padStart(2, '0')} <span>✳</span> ${day.subtitle}</div><h2>${day.title}</h2><p class=\"day-story\">${day.story}</p><div \nclass=\"activity-list\">${items}</div></section><aside class=\"brief-card\"><div class=\"brief-top\"><span>YOUR NEXT EXPERIENCE</span><span>✳</span></div><div class=\"brief-illustration\">\n${characterArt()}<span class=\"illustration-sun\"></span></div><div class=\"brief-content\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">${chosen.location} &nbsp; / &nbsp; ${duration(chosen.duration)}</div><h\n2>${chosen.title}</h2><p>${chosen.description}</p><div class=\"host-quote\">“${chosen.quote}”<small>— ${chosen.host}, YOUR HOST</small></div><button class=\"primary full\" data-action=\n\"start\" ${locked ? 'disabled' : ''}>${locked ? 'Complete earlier experiences' : scores[chosen.id] !== undefined ? 'Enjoy again' : 'Start experience'} <span>→</span></button></div><\n/aside></div></main><footer class=\"inner-footer\"><span>✳ &nbsp; THE ISLAND IS HAPPY YOU'RE HERE</span><button class=\"footer-link\" data-action=\"about\">ABOUT &amp; CREDITS</button></\nfooter></div>`;\n}\nexport function gameView(session: Session, attract: boolean, input: 'keyboard' | 'controller'): string {\n  const activity = session.activity;\n  return `<div class=\"site game-site\">${header(attract ? 'A LITTLE PREVIEW' : activity.location.toUpperCase())}<main class=\"game-main\"><div class=\"game-title\"><div><div class=\"eyeb\nrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> ${attract ? 'IDLE PREVIEW · ANY INPUT TO RETURN' : 'A MOMENT FOR YOURSELF'}</div><h1>${activity.title}</h1><p>${activity.instruction}</p></div><b\nutton class=\"outline-button\" data-action=\"pause\">Ⅱ <span>Pause</span></button></div><div class=\"game-layout\"><section class=\"balance-panel\"><div class=\"panel-label\"><span>YOUR BALA\nNCE</span><span>STAY WITH THE CIRCLE</span></div><div class=\"balance-board\"><div class=\"board-ring ring-outer\"></div><div class=\"board-ring ring-middle\"></div><div class=\"board-rin\ng ring-inner\"></div><div class=\"board-line horizontal\"></div><div class=\"board-line vertical\"></div><div id=\"balance-target\" class=\"balance-target\"></div><div id=\"balance-ball\" cla\nss=\"balance-ball\"></div><span class=\"board-letter top\">N</span><span class=\"board-letter bottom\">S</span><span class=\"board-letter left\">W</span><span class=\"board-letter right\">E<\n/span></div><div class=\"session-cue\" id=\"session-cue\">Find your centre</div><div class=\"game-progress\"><div id=\"session-progress\"></div></div><div class=\"board-bottom\"><span>GENTLE\n DOES IT</span><span>✳</span><span>EVERY WOBBLE COUNTS</span></div></section><aside class=\"session-side\"><div class=\"session-art\"><div class=\"session-sun\"></div><div class=\"guest-a\nrt\">${characterArt()}</div><div class=\"island-water\"></div></div><div class=\"session-stats\"><div><small>TIME REMAINING</small><b id=\"session-time\">0:00</b></div><div><small>BALANCE\n</small><b><span id=\"session-score\">0</span><i> / 100</i></b></div><div><small>STUMBLES</small><b id=\"session-falls\">0</b></div></div><div class=\"how-to\"><b>HOW TO MOVE</b><p>${inp\nut === 'controller' ? 'Left stick to lean · R2 for gentle movement · L1 / R1 for feet · ✕ for both' : 'WASD or arrow keys to lean · Shift for gentle movement · Q / E for feet · Spa\nce for both'}</p></div></aside></div></main></div>`;\n}\nexport function resultView(session: Session): string {\n  const rank = rankFor(session.score);\n  return `<div class=\"site result-site\">${header('EXPERIENCE COMPLETE')}<main class=\"result-main\"><div class=\"result-art\">${characterArt()}<span>✳</span></div><div class=\"eyebrow\">\n<span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> YOU SHOWED UP. THAT COUNTS.</div><h1>Beautifully <em>done.</em></h1><p>You've completed ${session.activity.title}. Your body may have wandered, but yo\nur spirit stayed on the island.</p><div class=\"result-score\"><div><small>YOUR BALANCE SCORE</small><b>${session.score}<i> / 100</i></b></div><div><small>THE ISLAND CALLS YOU</small\n><b>${rank.name}</b></div><div><small>STUMBLES</small><b>${session.balance.falls}</b></div></div><div class=\"result-actions\"><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"continue\">Continue\n your stay <span>→</span></button><button class=\"text-button\" data-action=\"retry\">Try this again ↻</button></div></main></div>`;\n}\nexport function modalView(modal: string, preferences: Preferences): string {\n  let body = '';\n  if (modal === 'settings') {\n    const toggle = (key: keyof Preferences, title: string, description: string) => `<label class=\"setting-row\"><span><b>${title}</b><small>${description}</small></span><input type=\n\"checkbox\" data-preference=\"${key}\" ${preferences[key] ? 'checked' : ''}><span class=\"switch\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></label>`;\n    body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">MAKE YOURSELF COMFORTABLE</div><h2>Retreat settings</h2>${toggle('sound','Sound effects','Little sounds for island moments')}${toggle('motion','Red\nuce motion','Keep the interface calm and still')}${toggle('contrast','Higher contrast','Make text and controls easier to see')}${toggle('assist','Balance assist','A gentler, more f\norgiving wobble')}<button class=\"text-button reset\" data-action=\"reset\">Reset saved progress ↺</button>`;\n  } else if (modal === 'pause') body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">TAKE ALL THE TIME YOU NEED</div><h2>Pause for a breath.</h2><p>Your experience will be right here when you're ready.</p\n><div class=\"modal-actions\"><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"resume\">Resume experience →</button><button class=\"text-button\" data-action=\"quit\">Return to itinerary</button></di\nv>`;\n  else if (modal === 'touch') body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">ONE SMALL THING</div><h2>Controller or keyboard required.</h2><p>Connect a controller or use a keyboard to take part. The\n settings and idle preview are still available here.</p><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"close\">Got it →</button>`;\n  else body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">A NOTE FROM THE ISLAND</div><h2>About this retreat</h2><p>Wee Fit Retreat is an original, gentle balance game inspired by the reassuring oddness\n of fitness games. All illustrations and sound effects were made for this project.</p><p>Explore five days of small activities. Lean towards the target and use your feet when the a\nctivity calls for them. Stumbles are invitations to begin again.</p><h3>Controls</h3><p><b>Keyboard:</b> WASD or arrows to lean, Shift for gentle movement, Q / E for left / right f\noot, Space for both, Esc to pause.<br><b>Controller:</b> left stick to lean, R2 for gentle movement, L1 / R1 for feet, Cross for both, Options to pause. D-pad and Cross navigate me\nnus.</p><h3>Credits &amp; project notes</h3><p>Original code, illustration and synthesized audio created for this game. Built in the provided my-3dge workspace; this edition uses a\n custom 2D presentation and does not include online multiplayer. Progress is stored locally in your browser.</p><p>Built with Vite and TypeScript. The engine source and project fee\ndback are included with the hand-in.</p>`;\n  return `<div class=\"modal-backdrop\"><section class=\"modal\" role=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"true\" aria-label=\"${modal === 'about' ? 'About and credits' : modal}\" tabindex=\"-1\"><button c\nlass=\"modal-close\" data-action=\"close\" aria-label=\"Close\">×</button>${body}</section></div>`;\n}\n--- main control flow ---\n/** @file Runs the retreat's menus, input, and balance sessions. */\nimport './styles.css';\nimport { DAYS, rankFor, type Activity } from './programme';\nimport { DEFAULT_BALANCE, action, createSession, stepSession, targetFor, type Session } from './wobble';\nimport { Soundscape } from './audio';\nimport { welcomeView, hubView, gameView, resultView, modalView } from './view';\n\ntype Screen = 'welcome' | 'hub' | 'playing' | 'result';\ntype Modal = 'settings' | 'about' | 'pause' | 'touch' | null;\ntype Preferences = { sound: boolean; motion: boolean; contrast: boolean; assist: boolean };\ntype Save = { unlocked: number; scores: Record<string, number>; preferences: Preferences };\n\nconst root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#app')!;\nconst storageKey = 'wee-fit-retreat-save-v1';\nconst defaults: Save = { unlocked: 0, scores: {}, preferences: { sound: true, motion: false, contrast: false, assist: false } };\nfunction load(): Save {\n  try {\n    const saved = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(storageKey) || '{}') as Partial<Save>;\n    return { ...defaults, ...saved, scores: saved.scores || {}, preferences: { ...defaults.preferences, ...saved.preferences } };\n  } catch { return structuredClone(defaults); }\n}\nlet save = load();\nlet screen: Screen = 'welcome';\nlet modal: Modal = null;\nlet dayIndex = 0;\nlet activityIndex = 0;\nlet session: Session | null = null;\nlet attract = false;\nlet lastInput = performance.now();\nlet lastFrame = 0;\nlet accumulator = 0;\nlet lastPadButtons: boolean[] = [];\nlet lastInputType: 'keyboard' | 'controller' = 'keyboard';\nconst keys = new Set<string>();\nconst sounds = new Soundscape();\nsounds.enabled = save.preferences.sound;\n\nfunction persist(): void {\n  try { localStorage.setItem(storageKey, JSON.stringify(save)); } catch { /* storage can be unavailable */ }\n}\nfunction flatIndex(day: number, activity: number): number {\n  return DAYS.slice(0, day).reduce((total, item) => total + item.activities.length, 0) + activity;\n}\nfunction selected(): Activity { return DAYS[dayIndex].activities[activityIndex]; }\nfunction selectFlat(index: number): void {\n  let remaining = index;\n  for (let day = 0; day < DAYS.length; day++) {\n    if (remaining < DAYS[day].activities.length) { dayIndex = day; activityIndex = remaining; return; }\n    remaining -= DAYS[day].activities.length;\n  }\n}\nfunction totalActivities(): number { return DAYS.reduce((total, day) => total + day.activities.length, 0); }\nfunction playSound(name: 'click' | 'hit' | 'finish' | 'miss'): void { try { sounds.play(name); } catch { /* audio is optional */ } }\nfunction isTouchOnly(): boolean {\n  return matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)').matches && !Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.() || []).some(Boolean);\n}\nfunction render(): void {\n  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('reduced-motion', save.preferences.motion);\n  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('high-contrast', save.preferences.contrast);\n  const content = screen === 'welcome' ? welcomeView(isTouchOnly()) : screen === 'hub' ? hubView(dayIndex, activityIndex, save.unlocked, save.scores) : screen === 'playing' && session ? gameView(session, attract, lastInputType) : session ? resultView(session) : '';\n  root.innerHTML = content + (modal ? modalView(modal, save.preferences) : '');\n  if (screen === 'playing') updateGame();\n  if (modal) root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.modal button, .modal input')?.focus();\n}\nfunction openGame(preview = false): void {\n  if (!preview && isTouchOnly()) { modal = 'touch'; render(); return; }\n  session = createSession(selected(), 13 + flatIndex(dayIndex, activityIndex));\n  attract = preview; screen = 'playing'; modal = null; lastFrame = 0; accumulator = 0;\n  keys.clear(); render();\n}\nfunction finish(): void {\n  if (!session) return;\n  if (attract) { screen = 'welcome'; attract = false; session = null; lastInput = performance.now(); render(); return; }\n  const index = flatIndex(dayIndex, activityIndex);\n  save.scores[session.activity.id] = Math.max(save.scores[session.activity.id] || 0, session.score);\n  save.unlocked = Math.min(totalActivities() - 1, Math.max(save.unlocked, index + 1));\n  persist(); playSound('finish'); screen = 'result'; render();\n}\nfunction updateGame(): void {\n  if (!session) return;\n  const balance = session.balance;\n  const target = targetFor(session);\n  const ball = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#balance-ball');\n  const marker = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#balance-target');\n  if (ball) { ball.style.left = `${50 + balance.x * 40}%`; ball.style.top = `${50 + balance.y * 40}%`; }\n  if (marker) { marker.style.left = `${50 + target.x * 40}%`; marker.style.top = `${50 + target.y * 40}%`; }\n  const timer = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-time');\n  if (timer) { const remaining = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(session.activity.duration - session.time)); timer.textContent = `${Math.floor(remaining / 60)}:${String(remaining % 60).padStart(2, '0')}`; }\n  const cue = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-cue');\n  if (cue) cue.textContent = balance.recovering > 0 ? 'Take a breath. Find your footing.' : target.label || session.cue || 'Find your centre';\n  const score = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-score');\n  if (score) score.textContent = `${Math.round(session.samples ? session.scoreSum / session.samples : 0)}`;\n  const falls = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-falls');\n  if (falls) falls.textContent = String(balance.falls);\n  const progress = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-progress');\n  if (progress) progress.style.width = `${Math.min(100, session.time / session.activity.duration * 100)}%`;\n  const person = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.guest-art');\n  if (person) person.style.setProperty('--lean', `${Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, balance.x)) * 11}deg`);\n}\nfunction moveFocus(direction: number): void {\n  const scope = modal ? root.querySelector('.modal') : root;\n  const focusables = Array.from(scope?.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('button:not(:disabled), input:not(:disabled)') || []);\n  if (!focusables.length) return;\n  const current = focusables.indexOf(document.activeElement as HTMLElement);\n  focusables[(current + direction + focusables.length) % focusables.length].focus();\n}\nfunction doFoot(foot: 'left' | 'right' | 'both'): void {\n  if (!session || screen !== 'playing' || modal || attract) return;\n  playSound(action(session, foot) ? 'hit' : 'miss');\n}\nfunction wake(): void {\n  lastInput = performance.now();\n  if (attract) { attract = false; session = null; screen = 'welcome'; render(); }\n}\nroot.addEventListener('click', (event) => {\n  const button = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLElement>('[data-action]');\n  if (!button) return;\n  if (attract) { wake(); return; }\n  wake(); const command = button.dataset.action; playSound('click');\n  if (command === 'begin') { screen = 'hub'; selectFlat(save.unlocked); }\n  else if (command === 'home') { screen = 'welcome'; session = null; }\n  else if (command === 'settings' || command === 'about') modal = command;\n  else if (command === 'close') modal = null;\n  else if (command === 'pause') modal = 'pause';\n  else if (command === 'resume') { modal = null; lastFrame = 0; }\n  else if (command === 'quit') { modal = null; session = null; screen = 'hub'; }\n  else if (command === 'reset') {\n    if (window.confirm('Reset all retreat progress and scores?')) { save = structuredClone(defaults); sounds.enabled = save.preferences.sound; persist(); dayIndex = 0; activityIndex = 0; }\n  } else if (command === 'day') { dayIndex = Number(button.dataset.day); activityIndex = 0; }\n  else if (command === 'activity') activityIndex = Number(button.dataset.index);\n  else if (command === 'start' || command === 'retry') { openGame(); return; }\n  else if (command === 'continue') { screen = 'hub'; session = null; selectFlat(save.unlocked); }\n  render();\n});\nroot.addEventListener('change', (event) => {\n  const input = event.target as HTMLInputElement;\n  const key = input.dataset.preference as keyof Preferences | undefined;\n  if (!key) return;\n  save.preferences[key] = input.checked; sounds.enabled = save.preferences.sound; persist(); render();\n});\nwindow.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n  const key = event.key.toLowerCase();\n  if (attract) { event.preventDefault(); wake(); return; }\n  lastInput = performance.now(); lastInputType = 'keyboard';\n  if (key === 'escape') { event.preventDefault(); if (modal) modal = null; else if (screen === 'playing') modal = 'pause'; render(); return; }\n  if (screen === 'playing' && !modal) {\n    if (['arrowup','arrowdown','arrowleft','arrowright',' ','q','e'].includes(key)) event.preventDefault();\n    keys.add(key);\n    if (!event.repeat && key === 'q') doFoot('left');\n    if (!event.repeat && key === 'e') doFoot('right');\n    if (!event.repeat && key === ' ') doFoot('both');\n  } else if (['arrowup','arrowdown','arrowleft','arrowright'].includes(key)) {\n    event.preventDefault(); moveFocus(key === 'arrowup' || key === 'arrowleft' ? -1 : 1);\n  }\n});\nwindow.addEventListener('keyup', (event) => keys.delete(event.key.toLowerCase()));\nwindow.addEventListener('blur', () => keys.clear());\ndocument.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => { lastFrame = 0; });\nwindow.addEventListener('pointerdown', () => { if (attract) wake(); else lastInput = performance.now(); });\n\nfunction frame(now: number): void {\n  const pad = Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.() || []).find(Boolean);\n  let stickX = 0; let stickY = 0; let gentle = false;\n  if (pad) {\n    stickX = Math.abs(pad.axes[0] || 0) > .13 ? pad.axes[0] : 0;\n    stickY = Math.abs(pad.axes[1] || 0) > .13 ? pad.axes[1] : 0;\n    gentle = !!pad.buttons[7]?.pressed;\n    const buttons = pad.buttons.map((button) => button.pressed);\n    const pressed = (index: number) => buttons[index] && !lastPadButtons[index];\n    if (buttons.some((button, index) => button && !lastPadButtons[index]) || stickX || stickY) {\n      if (attract) wake();\n      lastInput = now; lastInputType = 'controller';\n    }\n    if (pressed(9) || pressed(3)) { if (screen === 'playing') { modal = modal ? null : 'pause'; render(); } }\n    if (screen === 'playing' && !modal) {\n      if (pressed(4)) doFoot('left'); if (pressed(5)) doFoot('right'); if (pressed(0)) doFoot('both');\n    } else {\n      if (pressed(12) || pressed(14)) moveFocus(-1);\n      if (pressed(13) || pressed(15)) moveFocus(1);\n      if (pressed(0)) (document.activeElement as HTMLElement | null)?.click();\n--- engine files ---\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/gfx:\natmosphere.ts\nbackdrop.ts\ncameras\ncaps.ts\ncutaway.ts\ndaylight.ts\nenhanced\nfeatures.ts\nfx\ngeometry\nidmarks.ts\nidpass.ts\ninstanceSync.ts\ninstancing.ts\nlevel\nlights.ts\nlookMetrics.ts\nmaterials\npipelines.ts\npost\npropLooks.ts\nprops.ts\npuppets\nquality.ts\nrenderer.ts\nresolution.ts\nsceneDump.ts\nshadows.ts\nshot.ts\nsky.ts\nskyKind.ts\nstage.ts\nstageCrowd.ts\nstageFx.ts\nstageGround.ts\nstageProps.ts\nstageRides.ts\nstageShells.ts\nstageSite.ts\nstageSky.ts\nstandIns.ts\nstoreyCut.ts\nterrain.ts\nterrainSplat.ts\ntextures\nthumbnail.ts\nviewmodel\nwarmup.ts\nweapons.ts\n\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/sim:\nactorActions.ts\nactorAnim.ts\nactorClips.ts\nactorInput.ts\nactors.ts\nbreakables.ts\ncapture.ts\ncombatApi.ts\ncrowdBodies.ts\ndamage.ts\ndevActions.ts\ndoors.ts\nentities.ts\nentityTable.ts\nfeelCourse.ts\nhits.ts\nhouseApi.ts\ninteract.ts\nkitsApi.ts\nlevelBodies.ts\nlights.ts\nmelee.ts\nmovementApi.ts\npropBlocks.ts\nprops.ts\nqueryView.ts\nragdolls.ts\nreactions.ts\nreplay.ts\nrides.ts\nscene.ts\nsession.ts\nsiteApi.ts\nstate.ts\nswitches.ts\nsystems.ts\nthings.ts\nweapons.ts\nworld.ts\n--- starter scene imports ---\n/**\n * @file The starter game's scene `game:play`: every new game begins as this one (tools/game/new-game.mjs copies\n * labs/game/ into it), so it is small, plays, and shows the parts a game is made of. The player, a humanoid on the\n * character controller, runs round the arena (`ARENA_TEXT` below: walls, two pillars, two low walls to jump) collecting\n * the gems the seed scatters, before the clock runs out. All the gems: won; the clock at 0: lost.\n *\n * The parts: a level as text, compiled for its physics bodies; settings (`game.*`, read when the scene starts, so they\n * change play and go in replays); components (`gem`, drawn as a small glowing box because it declares `x` and `z` in\n * metres; `round`, the score and the clock); the player (labs/game/cast/player.ts, an actor that reads the step's\n * intents: `move`, `jump`, `dash`); systems in the phase `rules`, after the actors' feet are read back; a named random\n * stream (`gems`); events (`gem`, `won`, `lost`) that pages, sounds and tests hear. The page is labs/game/main.ts, the\n * bot labs/game/bot.ts.\n *\n * The level's text lives here, not in a .txt file, since sim-side code reads no files; the page registers the same\n * text for the view (labs/game/main.ts).\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts, so `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts` runs it in Node.\n *\n * @example\n * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --steps 600\n * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --set game.gems=3 --seed 7\n * ARENA.spawns.find((spawn) => spawn.name === 'hero')?.position; // [3.5, 0, 2.5]\n * @see labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\n */\nimport {\n  addLevelBodies,\n  compileLevel,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineScene,\n  defineSettings,\n  physicsOf,\n  type ActorComponent,\n  type World,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { spawnPlayer } from '../cast/player';\n\n/** The arena: 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls (0.75 m) to jump, the spawn `@`. */\nexport const ARENA_TEXT = `---\ndescription: The starter game's arena. 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls 0.75 m high that the player jumps, and the player's spawn.\n---\n##################\n#................#\n#..@.............#\n#.......PP.......#\n#.......PP.......#\n#................#\n#....w......w....#\n#....w......w....#\n#................#\n#.......PP.......#\n#.......PP.......#\n#................#\n#................#\n##################\n`;\n\n/** The arena, compiled: its colliders for physics, its tiles for the gems and the bot's paths. */\nexport const ARENA = compileLevel(ARENA_TEXT, { file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts', name: 'arena' });\n\n/** The game's settings: each is reachable through `x set`, URL parameters (`?game.gems=3`) and `__engine.set`. */\nexport const GAME_SETTINGS = defineSettings({\n  'game.gems': {\n    type: 'integer',\n    default: 10,\n    minimum: 1,\n    maximum: 40,\n    when: 'scene',\n    description: 'How many gems the seed scatters.',\n  },\n  'game.seconds': {\n    type: 'number',\n    default: 30,\n    minimum: 5,\n    maximum: 600,\n    unit: 's',\n    when: 'scene',\n    description: 'How long the player has to collect them all.',\n  },\n  'game.speed': {\n    type: 'number',\n    default: 6,\n    minimum: 1,\n    maximum: 20,\n    unit: 'm/s',\n    when: 'scene',\n    description: 'How fast the player runs.',\n  },\n});\n\n/** A gem: where it floats and how it looks (the page draws a component that declares x and z in metres). */\nexport const GEM = defineComponent('gem', {\n  description: 'A gem to collect: where it floats, its spin and how it is drawn.',\n  fields: {\n    x: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm', description: 'East.' },\n    y: { type: 'number', default: 0.5, unit: 'm', description: 'Up: the bottom of its box.' },\n    z: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm', description: 'South.' },\n    yaw: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'rad', description: 'Its spin.' },\n    size: { type: 'number', default: 0.4, unit: 'm', description: 'The side of its box.' },\n    material: { type: 'string', default: 'material:glow', description: 'What it is drawn with.' },\n  },\n});\n\n/** The round: the score, the clock and how it ended. One entity holds it. */\nexport const ROUND = defineComponent('round', {\n  description:\n    'The round: gems collected of the total, the steps left on the clock, and whether it is playing, won or lost.',\n  fields: {\n    gems: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many gems the round scattered.' },\n    collected: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many the player has collected.' },\n    left: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'The sim steps left on the clock (60 a second).' },\n    state: { type: 'string', default: 'playing', description: \"'playing', 'won' or 'lost'.\" },\n  },\n});\n\n/** The round, as the component holds it. */\nexport type Round = { gems: number; collected: number; left: number; state: 'playing' | 'won' | 'lost' };\n\n/** The scene's components, typed. */\nexport type GameComponents = {\n  gem: { x: number; y: number; z: number; yaw: number; size: number; material: string };\n  round: Round;\n  actor: ActorComponent;\n};\n\n/** How close the player's feet come to a gem to collect it, m (on the ground plane). */\nexport const REACH = 0.8;\n\n/** How far from the spawn the gems keep, m, so the first one is never collected without moving. */\nconst CLEAR = 3;\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
