{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_581","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"P='Wee-Fit-Rreat'; P='Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- engine renderer ---'; ls \\\"\"'$P/engine/gfx\"; sed -n '\"'1,180p' \\\"\"'$P/engine/gfx/scene.ts\" 2>/dev/null; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- package and bundle ---'; cat \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/tools/bundle.mjs\"; cat \"$P/package.json\" | head -n 65; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- 3D and multiplayer plan ---'; rg -n -C 3 '3D|three\\\\.js|Engine|AI Hub|multiplayer|session.js' PLAN.md | head -n 190; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- play view hooks ---'; rg -n 'gameView|characterArt|islandArt|data-' \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/view.ts\" | head -n 16'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_581","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"P='Wee-Fit-Rreat'; P='Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- engine renderer ---'; ls \\\"\"'$P/engine/gfx\"; sed -n '\"'1,180p' \\\"\"'$P/engine/gfx/scene.ts\" 2>/dev/null; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- package and bundle ---'; cat \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/tools/bundle.mjs\"; cat \"$P/package.json\" | head -n 65; printf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- 3D and multiplayer plan ---'; rg -n -C 3 '3D|three\\\\.js|Engine|AI Hub|multiplayer|session.js' PLAN.md | head -n 190; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- play view hooks ---'; rg -n 'gameView|characterArt|islandArt|data-' \\\"\"'$P/labs/game/view.ts\" | head -n 16'","aggregated_output":"--- engine renderer ---\natmosphere.ts\nbackdrop.ts\ncameras\ncaps.ts\ncutaway.ts\ndaylight.ts\nenhanced\nfeatures.ts\nfx\ngeometry\nidmarks.ts\nidpass.ts\ninstanceSync.ts\ninstancing.ts\nlevel\nlights.ts\nlookMetrics.ts\nmaterials\npipelines.ts\npost\npropLooks.ts\nprops.ts\npuppets\nquality.ts\nrenderer.ts\nresolution.ts\nsceneDump.ts\nshadows.ts\nshot.ts\nsky.ts\nskyKind.ts\nstage.ts\nstageCrowd.ts\nstageFx.ts\nstageGround.ts\nstageProps.ts\nstageRides.ts\nstageShells.ts\nstageSite.ts\nstageSky.ts\nstandIns.ts\nstoreyCut.ts\nterrain.ts\nterrainSplat.ts\ntextures\nthumbnail.ts\nviewmodel\nwarmup.ts\nweapons.ts\n--- package and bundle ---\n/** @file Packages the game as one portable HTML file. */\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { join, resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { build } from 'vite';\n\nconst root = process.cwd();\nconst result = await build({ root, configFile: false, logLevel: 'warn', base: './', build: { write: false, modulePreload: false, cssCodeSplit: false, rollupOptions: { input: { game: join(root, 'labs/game/index.html') }, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } } } });\nlet html = '';\nconst files = {};\nfor (const entry of (Array.isArray(result) ? result : [result]).flatMap((output) => output.output)) {\n  const text = entry.type === 'chunk' ? entry.code : typeof entry.source === 'string' ? entry.source : new TextDecoder().decode(entry.source);\n  if (entry.fileName.endsWith('.html')) html = text;\n  else files[entry.fileName] = text;\n}\nfunction contents(reference) {\n  const name = Object.keys(files).find((file) => reference.endsWith(file));\n  if (!name) throw new Error(`Missing build asset: ${reference}`);\n  return files[name];\n}\nhtml = html.replace(/<script type=\"module\" crossorigin src=\"([^\"]+)\"><\\/script>|<link rel=\"stylesheet\" crossorigin href=\"([^\"]+)\">/g, (_tag, script, style) => style ? `<style>${contents(style)}</style>` : `<script type=\"module\">${contents(script).replaceAll('</script', '<\\\\/script')}</script>`);\nif (!html || /(?:src|href)=\"\\.\\/assets\\//.test(html)) throw new Error('Build is not self-contained');\nwriteFileSync(resolve(process.argv[2]), html);\n{\n  \"name\": \"wee-fit-retreat\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"description\": \"A game made with the my-3dge engine.\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=24.10 <25\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc -b tsconfig.check.json\",\n    \"lint\": \"eslint --cache --cache-location node_modules/.cache/eslint/ .\",\n    \"format\": \"prettier --write --cache .\",\n    \"check\": \"node tools/checkAll.ts\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\": \"0.21.0\",\n    \"@stdlib/math-base-special-cos\": \"0.3.1\",\n    \"@stdlib/math-base-special-pow\": \"0.3.1\",\n    \"@stdlib/math-base-special-sin\": \"0.3.1\",\n    \"three\": \"0.182.0\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"1.32.2\",\n    \"@playwright/test\": \"1.64.1\",\n    \"@stryker-mutator/core\": \"9.6.1\",\n    \"@stryker-mutator/vitest-runner\": \"9.6.1\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"24.19.2\",\n    \"@types/three\": \"0.182.0\",\n    \"eslint\": \"9.39.5\",\n    \"eslint-plugin-jsdoc\": \"61.7.1\",\n    \"globals\": \"16.5.0\",\n    \"prettier\": \"3.9.10\",\n    \"tsx\": \"4.23.15\",\n    \"typescript\": \"5.9.3\",\n    \"typescript-eslint\": \"8.72.1\",\n    \"vite\": \"7.3.7\",\n    \"vitest\": \"4.1.12\"\n  },\n  \"allowScripts\": {\n    \"esbuild\": false\n  }\n}\n--- 3D and multiplayer plan ---\n5-rule, and the reports. Every path below is relative to your dev folder.\n6-\n7-**[tested]** marks what was actually run on this machine on 2026-11-04, against my-3dge at commit e7a1243. **[source]**\n8:marks what was read in that commit's code but not run. Trust both over your memory of three.js or the engine. Anything\n9-unmarked is design: yours to tune.\n10-\n11-Contents: 1 The game · 2 World and cast · 3 The one verb · 4 Controls · 5 Structure · 6 Activities · 7 The finale ·\n12:8 Screens · 9 Multiplayer · 10 Art · 11 Animation · 12 Audio · 13 Writing · 14 Tech · 15 Engine traps · 16 Testing ·\n13-17 Build order · 18 Done · 19 Reports · 20 Brief-to-plan map\n14-\n15----\n--\n23-Marbles roll by themselves. The staff keep asking you to stand further east. Little Fulcrum is balanced on a single\n24-rock. On the last night the storm comes, the island tips, and in the finale your thumb's balance *is* the island's.\n25-\n26:**Genre:** a 3D sports and wellness anthology of balance activities around a small walkable island, with a daily-ritual\n27-meta game and a comedy story. **Perspective:** third person throughout: a chase camera on the island, and a purpose-built\n28-camera for each activity (the table in section 6). **Hub genre:** Sports.\n29-\n--\n517-- **Settings:** Music (**10% by default**), Effects, Voices, Button icons, Mouse sensitivity, Invert look, Rumble, Steadier Hands (an\n518-  assist: halves the sway), Reduced Motion (no camera roll or shake), Fullscreen, Erase Save.\n519-- **Controls:** shows the bindings per scheme; keyboard rebinding through `input.bindingsFor`, `rebind`, `listen`.\n520:- **About / Credits:** paged, from one data file: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, credits\n521-  (section 19).\n522-\n523-**Dev Mode** (from the pause menu; absent in hub sessions; a clear panel that works with pad, keyboard and mouse):\n--\n561-The engine's gamepad device only follows one active pad, so the page reads `navigator.getGamepads()` itself in Group Class and sends\n562-each seat's input with `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:seats', […])`.\n563-\n564:### In AI Hub: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, mode **ghost**\n565-\n566-Read the protocol once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Fetch by raw URL, into\n567:`labs/game/hub/`: `session.js` (save it as `session-client.txt`), and for tests `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same\n568-folder. **Do not clone the ai-hub repository: it is 5.3 GB.**\n569-\n570-Why ghost: every copy runs its own seeded round, nothing depends on a host, and each player sees the others on the neighbouring mats,\n--\n594-const info = AIHub?.active ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\n595-if (info) { search.set('scene', 'game:round'); search.set('seed', String(info.seed)); }\n596-const watchdog = info ? setTimeout(() => AIHub.ready(), 14000) : 0;   // the harness allows 20 s after hello\n597:engine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['game:island', 'game:round'], search: `?${search}`, /* … */ });\n598-if (info) { clearTimeout(watchdog); AIHub.ready(); }\n599-```\n600-\n601:**The biggest trap in this whole plan [tested]:** the hub opens the page with `?aihub=1&aihub-seed=N`. `createEngine` treats every\n602-unknown query key as a setting and fails with `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, **and the harness still reports PASS**, because the client keeps\n603-answering while the game is dead. Strip those keys, and make your test assert, inside every frame, `__engine.ready === true` and\n604-`__engine.errors.length === 0`.\n--\n830-\n831-## 14. Tech\n832-\n833:**Stack:** my-3dge full workspace (TypeScript, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, Vitest, Playwright, HTML/CSS UI). No new npm dependencies. The engine stays read-only: `npm run check` compares every engine file with `engine-lock.json`. Workarounds go in the game; what you needed goes in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\n834-\n835-**Setup [tested], in the empty dev folder:**\n836-\n--\n849-\n850-**The one-scene rule.** A running page cannot change scene **[source]**. So: `game:island` is the whole game on one world, with activities spawned at their stations and removed afterwards; `game:round` is the small session scene. A page picks by `?scene=` at load. Never reload the page in a session.\n851-\n852:**The pilot.** Keep every character, the Guest included, at `player: false`, and let one sim system, `pilot`, write `actor.intents` each step: the step's `move` on the island, nothing in an activity, the bot's in attract, the slope added in the finale. This one rule makes roam, activities, attract and the Great Tilt the same code. Cameras follow only a `player: true` actor by themselves, so give them the Guest's feet with `createEngine({ cameraInput: () => ({ follow: feet }) })` **[tested: walks and the chase camera follows]**.\n853-\n854-**Cameras and maps** are page state: when `flow` changes, the page calls `inspector.camera.set(code, { blend: true })` and `engine.input.use(mapId)`. Your own camera modes come from `node x new camera labs/game/cameras/<name>` (one each for the mat, the line, the dive); `cam3=chase`, `cam3=fly` and `cam=topdown` are built in.\n855-\n--\n919-\n920----\n921-\n922:## 15. Engine traps (hit on this machine unless marked **[source]**)\n923-\n924-| Trap | What happens | Do this |\n925-|---|---|---|\n--\n932-| `docs/GAME-GUIDE.md` cites `labs/playground/…` | Those files are not in your workspace | Use `labs/box/`; or read the engine's GitHub repository if one is truly worth it |\n933-| `playClip` in `setup` | `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` | `clips.play` at spawn, or from the first step |\n934-| `seekClip` **[source]** | Moves only the top clip | Write `clips.state.slots[i].t` |\n935:| No public way into the three.js scene **[source]** | A page cannot add a mesh | Everything drawn is a sim entity: terrain, level, prop, actor, crowd body, telegraph, emitter, or a component with `x`, `z`. All else is HTML |\n936-| `modal()` true **[source]** | Intents dropped, virtual device too | Menu picks go through scene actions |\n937-| Importing `three` or `rapier` **[source]** | Lint error | Public API only |\n938-| `input.prompt()` **[source]** | Xbox labels for unknown pads | Own glyph table (section 4) |\n939:| Engine touch stick **[source]** | Appears on touch screens | `touch=off` in the query |\n940-| Bus defaults **[source]** | Music 0.5 | `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` |\n941-| Hub client through a formatter **[source]** | Hub rejects it | Keep it as `.txt`, inject at build |\n942-| `git` in the dev folder | It belongs to the larger repository around it | Do not `git init`, commit or restore there, despite `AGENTS.md`'s \"commit as you go\", unless your TASK.md asks |\n--\n1022-\n1023-**Keep a running tally as you go** of the issues testing catches, and which were critical: you will be asked for both, and for your most and least helpful test. Note engine surprises in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` when they happen.\n1024-\n1025:Answers already decided: Plan: the name this file has in your folder. Genre and Perspective as in section 1. Tech: my-3dge at its pinned commit, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, TypeScript. Art: the engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets. Animation: the engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim. Audio: tracker songs, `defineSfx` effects, gibberish syllable voices, all code, music at 10%. Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost; same-screen Group Class on its own. Environment and Model as your TASK.md gives them. Usage: \"added on import\".\n1026-\n1027-Hub catalogue suggestions: type `Game`; genre `Sports`; source `Wii Fit`; series empty (the source is its own franchise); players `1–4`; controls \"Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse · Feet: L2 R2, Q E or mouse buttons · Breathe: both\"; tags from `3d`, `third-person`, `comedy`, `arcade`, `sports`, `story`. Tagline idea: \"Stand still. It is harder than it looks.\"\n1028-\n1029:**Credits must include:** my-3dge (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), @stdlib (Apache-2.0); the AI Hub session client. Animation clips by what you actually copied: Mesh2Motion and Quaternius Universal Animation Library (CC0; credit anyway); **100STYLE dataset, Mason, Starke and Komura, 2022, CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), converted to key poses: required credit with a link and a note of changes** if you use any `STYLE100*` clip; CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database if you use any `CMU` clip (terms in `data/anim/LICENSES/CMU.txt`).\n1030-\n1031----\n1032-\n--\n1040-| Title: playful riff, picked by a real RNG from 50 | Yours, per TASK.md. This plan just says \"the game's title\": on the title screen, hub card, attract banner, About |\n1041-| Research: your choice | Not needed beyond this plan; report what you did |\n1042-| Single HTML; downloads optional | 14 (everything inlined) |\n1043:| Engine's full workspace, engine read-only, own systems on top | 14, 15 |\n1044-| Art: engine's native style base; new assets for the source's feel | 10 |\n1045-| Animation: engine's system base; new animations | 11 |\n1046-| Audio: all code, no files; gibberish voices; music 10% default | 12 |\n1047:| Online and multiplayer: hub integration and on its own | 9 |\n1048-| Dev folder, separate modules, bundle; shared machine rules | 14, 16 |\n1049-| Performance out of scope | 9 (one protocol deadline only) |\n1050-| Testing: headless scripts, full playthrough, one command, failures only, sparing screenshots, no review subagents | 16 |\n--- play view hooks ---\n3:import { characterArt, islandArt } from './art';\n8:  return `<header class=\"topbar\"><button class=\"brand\" data-action=\"home\" aria-label=\"Return to title\"><span class=\"brand-icon\">✳</span><span>WEE FIT <b>RETREAT</b></span></button><span class=\"top-label\">${label}</span><button class=\"icon-button\" data-action=\"settings\" aria-label=\"Settings\">⚙</button></header>`;\n12:  return `<div class=\"site welcome\">${header()}<main class=\"welcome-main\"><div class=\"hero-copy\"><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> A MOST GENTLE ESCAPE</div><h1>Find your<br><em>almost</em> balance.</h1><p>Welcome to a little island where the air is fresh, the hosts are encouraging, and standing still is surprisingly ambitious.</p><div class=\"hero-actions\"><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"begin\">Begin your stay <span>→</span></button><button class=\"text-button\" data-action=\"about\">What is this place? <span>↗</span></button></div>${touch ? '<p class=\"touch-notice\">Controller or keyboard required to play. Settings and the idle preview are available.</p>' : '<div class=\"control-note\"><span class=\"keycap\">↵</span> KEYBOARD &nbsp; OR &nbsp; CONTROLLER FRIENDLY</div>'}</div><div class=\"hero-art\"><div class=\"sun-halo\"></div>${islandArt()}<div class=\"postcard\"><span class=\"postcard-mark\">✳</span><div><b>A slower kind of holiday</b><small>YOUR RETREAT AWAITS</small></div></div><div class=\"art-caption\">EST. SOMEWHERE PEACEFUL &nbsp; · &nbsp; 01 / 05</div></div></main><footer class=\"welcome-footer\"><span>TAKE YOUR TIME. YOU'RE ON ISLAND TIME.</span><button class=\"footer-link\" data-action=\"about\">ABOUT &amp; CREDITS</button></footer></div>`;\n19:  const tabs = DAYS.map((item, index) => `<button class=\"day-tab ${index === dayIndex ? 'active' : ''}\" data-action=\"day\" data-day=\"${index}\" aria-pressed=\"${index === dayIndex}\"><span>DAY ${String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><b>${item.title}</b></button>`).join('');\n22:    return `<button class=\"activity-row ${index === activityIndex ? 'selected' : ''} ${isLocked ? 'locked' : ''}\" data-action=\"activity\" data-index=\"${index}\" aria-pressed=\"${index === activityIndex}\"><span class=\"activity-number\">${isLocked ? '·' : String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><span class=\"activity-name\"><b>${item.title}</b><small>${item.location} &nbsp; · &nbsp; ${duration(item.duration)}</small></span><span class=\"row-status\">${score !== undefined ? '✓' : isLocked ? 'LOCKED' : '→'}</span></button>`;\n24:  return `<div class=\"site hub\">${header('YOUR RETREAT PROGRAMME')}<main class=\"hub-main\"><div class=\"hub-heading\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> MAKE YOURSELF AT HOME</div><h1>Your island <em>itinerary.</em></h1><p>One small wobble at a time. There is no rush.</p></div><div class=\"stay-progress\"><span>YOUR STAY SO FAR</span><b>${String(complete).padStart(2, '0')} <small>experiences enjoyed</small></b></div></div><nav class=\"days\" aria-label=\"Retreat days\">${tabs}</nav><div class=\"hub-grid\"><section class=\"programme\"><div class=\"section-kicker\">DAY ${String(dayIndex + 1).padStart(2, '0')} <span>✳</span> ${day.subtitle}</div><h2>${day.title}</h2><p class=\"day-story\">${day.story}</p><div class=\"activity-list\">${items}</div></section><aside class=\"brief-card\"><div class=\"brief-top\"><span>YOUR NEXT EXPERIENCE</span><span>✳</span></div><div class=\"brief-illustration\">${characterArt()}<span class=\"illustration-sun\"></span></div><div class=\"brief-content\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">${chosen.location} &nbsp; / &nbsp; ${duration(chosen.duration)}</div><h2>${chosen.title}</h2><p>${chosen.description}</p><div class=\"host-quote\">“${chosen.quote}”<small>— ${chosen.host}, YOUR HOST</small></div><button class=\"primary full\" data-action=\"start\" ${locked ? 'disabled' : ''}>${locked ? 'Complete earlier experiences' : scores[chosen.id] !== undefined ? 'Enjoy again' : 'Start experience'} <span>→</span></button></div></aside></div></main><footer class=\"inner-footer\"><span>✳ &nbsp; THE ISLAND IS HAPPY YOU'RE HERE</span><button class=\"footer-link\" data-action=\"about\">ABOUT &amp; CREDITS</button></footer></div>`;\n26:export function gameView(session: Session, attract: boolean, input: 'keyboard' | 'controller'): string {\n28:  return `<div class=\"site game-site\">${header(attract ? 'A LITTLE PREVIEW' : activity.location.toUpperCase())}<main class=\"game-main\"><div class=\"game-title\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> ${attract ? 'IDLE PREVIEW · ANY INPUT TO RETURN' : 'A MOMENT FOR YOURSELF'}</div><h1>${activity.title}</h1><p>${activity.instruction}</p></div><button class=\"outline-button\" data-action=\"pause\">Ⅱ <span>Pause</span></button></div><div class=\"game-layout\"><section class=\"balance-panel\"><div class=\"panel-label\"><span>YOUR BALANCE</span><span>STAY WITH THE CIRCLE</span></div><div class=\"balance-board\"><div class=\"board-ring ring-outer\"></div><div class=\"board-ring ring-middle\"></div><div class=\"board-ring ring-inner\"></div><div class=\"board-line horizontal\"></div><div class=\"board-line vertical\"></div><div id=\"balance-target\" class=\"balance-target\"></div><div id=\"balance-ball\" class=\"balance-ball\"></div><span class=\"board-letter top\">N</span><span class=\"board-letter bottom\">S</span><span class=\"board-letter left\">W</span><span class=\"board-letter right\">E</span></div><div class=\"session-cue\" id=\"session-cue\">Find your centre</div><div class=\"game-progress\"><div id=\"session-progress\"></div></div><div class=\"board-bottom\"><span>GENTLE DOES IT</span><span>✳</span><span>EVERY WOBBLE COUNTS</span></div></section><aside class=\"session-side\"><div class=\"session-art\"><div class=\"session-sun\"></div><div class=\"guest-art\">${characterArt()}</div><div class=\"island-water\"></div></div><div class=\"session-stats\"><div><small>TIME REMAINING</small><b id=\"session-time\">0:00</b></div><div><small>BALANCE</small><b><span id=\"session-score\">0</span><i> / 100</i></b></div><div><small>STUMBLES</small><b id=\"session-falls\">0</b></div></div><div class=\"how-to\"><b>HOW TO MOVE</b><p>${input === 'controller' ? 'Left stick to lean · R2 for gentle movement · L1 / R1 for feet · ✕ for both' : 'WASD or arrow keys to lean · Shift for gentle movement · Q / E for feet · Space for both'}</p></div></aside></div></main></div>`;\n32:  return `<div class=\"site result-site\">${header('EXPERIENCE COMPLETE')}<main class=\"result-main\"><div class=\"result-art\">${characterArt()}<span>✳</span></div><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> YOU SHOWED UP. THAT COUNTS.</div><h1>Beautifully <em>done.</em></h1><p>You've completed ${session.activity.title}. Your body may have wandered, but your spirit stayed on the island.</p><div class=\"result-score\"><div><small>YOUR BALANCE SCORE</small><b>${session.score}<i> / 100</i></b></div><div><small>THE ISLAND CALLS YOU</small><b>${rank.name}</b></div><div><small>STUMBLES</small><b>${session.balance.falls}</b></div></div><div class=\"result-actions\"><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"continue\">Continue your stay <span>→</span></button><button class=\"text-button\" data-action=\"retry\">Try this again ↻</button></div></main></div>`;\n37:    const toggle = (key: keyof Preferences, title: string, description: string) => `<label class=\"setting-row\"><span><b>${title}</b><small>${description}</small></span><input type=\"checkbox\" data-preference=\"${key}\" ${preferences[key] ? 'checked' : ''}><span class=\"switch\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></label>`;\n38:    body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">MAKE YOURSELF COMFORTABLE</div><h2>Retreat settings</h2>${toggle('sound','Sound effects','Little sounds for island moments')}${toggle('motion','Reduce motion','Keep the interface calm and still')}${toggle('contrast','Higher contrast','Make text and controls easier to see')}${toggle('assist','Balance assist','A gentler, more forgiving wobble')}<button class=\"text-button reset\" data-action=\"reset\">Reset saved progress ↺</button>`;\n39:  } else if (modal === 'pause') body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">TAKE ALL THE TIME YOU NEED</div><h2>Pause for a breath.</h2><p>Your experience will be right here when you're ready.</p><div class=\"modal-actions\"><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"resume\">Resume experience →</button><button class=\"text-button\" data-action=\"quit\">Return to itinerary</button></div>`;\n40:  else if (modal === 'touch') body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">ONE SMALL THING</div><h2>Controller or keyboard required.</h2><p>Connect a controller or use a keyboard to take part. The settings and idle preview are still available here.</p><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"close\">Got it →</button>`;\n42:  return `<div class=\"modal-backdrop\"><section class=\"modal\" role=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"true\" aria-label=\"${modal === 'about' ? 'About and credits' : modal}\" tabindex=\"-1\"><button class=\"modal-close\" data-action=\"close\" aria-label=\"Close\">×</button>${body}</section></div>`;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
