ller'): string {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts:28:  return `<div class=\"site game-site\">${header(attract ? 'A LITTLE PREVIEW' : activity.location.toUpperCase())}<main class=\"game-main\"><div class=\"game-title\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> ${attract ? 'IDLE PREVIEW · ANY INPUT TO RETURN' : 'A MOMENT FOR YOURSELF'}</div><h1>${activity.title}</h1><p>${activity.instruction}</p></div><button class=\"outline-button\" data-action=\"pause\">Ⅱ <span>Pause</span></button></div><div class=\"game-layout\"><section class=\"balance-panel\"><div class=\"panel-label\"><span>YOUR BALANCE</span><span>STAY WITH THE CIRCLE</span></div><div class=\"balance-board\"><div class=\"board-ring ring-outer\"></div><div class=\"board-ring ring-middle\"></div><div class=\"board-ring ring-inner\"></div><div class=\"board-line horizontal\"></div><div class=\"board-line vertical\"></div><div id=\"balance-target\" class=\"balance-target\"></div><div id=\"balance-ball\" class=\"balance-ball\"></div><span class=\"board-letter top\">N</span><span class=\"board-letter bottom\">S</span><span class=\"board-letter left\">W</span><span class=\"board-letter right\">E</span></div><div class=\"session-cue\" id=\"session-cue\">Find your centre</div><div class=\"game-progress\"><div id=\"session-progress\"></div></div><div class=\"board-bottom\"><span>GENTLE DOES IT</span><span>✳</span><span>EVERY WOBBLE COUNTS</span></div></section><aside class=\"session-side\"><div class=\"session-art\"><div class=\"session-sun\"></div><div class=\"guest-art\">${characterArt()}</div><div class=\"island-water\"></div></div><div class=\"session-stats\"><div><small>TIME REMAINING</small><b id=\"session-time\">0:00</b></div><div><small>BALANCE</small><b><span id=\"session-score\">0</span><i> / 100</i></b></div><div><small>STUMBLES</small><b id=\"session-falls\">0</b></div></div><div class=\"how-to\"><b>HOW TO MOVE</b><p>${input === 'controller' ? 'Left stick to lean · R2 for gentle movement · L1 / R1 for feet · ✕ for both' : 'WASD or arrow keys to lean · Shift for gentle movement · Q / E for feet · Space for both'}</p></div></aside></div></main></div>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts:34:export function modalView(modal: string, preferences: Preferences): string {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:6:import { welcomeView, hubView, gameView, resultView, modalView } from './view';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:57:function render(): void {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:60:  const content = screen === 'welcome' ? welcomeView(isTouchOnly()) : screen === 'hub' ? hubView(dayIndex, activityIndex, save.unlocked, save.scores) : screen === 'playing' && session ? gameView(session, attract, lastInputType) : session ? resultView(session) : '';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:61:  root.innerHTML = content + (modal ? modalView(modal, save.preferences) : '');\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:65:function openGame(preview = false): void {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:71:function finish(): void {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:79:function updateGame(): void {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:115:root.addEventListener('click', (event) => {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:135:root.addEventListener('change', (event) => {\n--- restrictions ---\n13:Tech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge#make-a-game-with-my-3dge, in the engine's full workspace. The engine stays read-only, as the AGENTS.md it gives your game says: add whatever systems, art assets and animations the game needs on top of it. The rest of the tech stack is your choice.\n15:Art Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic props.\n17:Animation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\n19:Audio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\n24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\n38:- **Browsers:** Playwright 1.63.0 for Python (from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright), with Chromium 153.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered; WebGPU, software-rendered, when started with --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader), Firefox 155.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered), WebKit 26.6 (WebGL 2) already downloaded. Phone and tablet device profiles are built in.\n39:  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\n54:- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n72:Create a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\n93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n98:- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n99:- Art Direction: style used\n101:- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n107:- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n111:  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n113:  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n125:    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n137:Engine Feedback\n139:- What did you like most about the engine?\n142:- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n143:- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n144:- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n148:- What did you like most about this prompt?\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
