{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_610","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- workspace ---'; ls; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- game sources ---'; rg --files 'Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game' | head -80; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- requirements ---'; rg -n 'AI Hub|session.js|harness|three|3D|About|exit-interview|@file|noise|Testing|music' TASK.md PLAN.md | head -100; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- package ---'; cat Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/package.json\"","aggregated_output":"--- workspace ---\nPLAN.md\nPROGRESS.md\nTASK.md\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055.html\n--- game sources ---\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/bot.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/programme.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/wobble.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/index.html\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/README.md\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/audio.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/styles.css\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/best.test.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/art.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/best.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/scenes/play.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/cast/player.ts\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/tools/bundle.mjs\n--- requirements ---\nPLAN.md:8:marks what was read in that commit's code but not run. Trust both over your memory of three.js or the engine. Anything\nPLAN.md:12:8 Screens · 9 Multiplayer · 10 Art · 11 Animation · 12 Audio · 13 Writing · 14 Tech · 15 Engine traps · 16 Testing ·\nPLAN.md:26:**Genre:** a 3D sports and wellness anthology of balance activities around a small walkable island, with a daily-ritual\nPLAN.md:47:**Never take (this is an original game, not a recreation):** the word \"Wii\" anywhere in the game except the About\nPLAN.md:93:- **You**: \"Guest\". Pick one of three looks and a tracksuit colour at the pier. No name entry.\nPLAN.md:120:accel   = gain × (target − cob) + instability × cob + noise(t) × (1 − calmEffect × calm) + disturbance\nPLAN.md:129:| `game.wobble.noise` | 3.5 /s² | 0–8 | Sway strength |\nPLAN.md:130:| `game.wobble.noiseRate` | 0.15 Hz | 0.05–0.4 | Sway speed: a slow push you lean against |\nPLAN.md:139:noise(t) = ( sin(2π·rate·m1·t + p1) + 0.6·sin(2π·rate·1.7·m2·t + p2) + 0.3·sin(2π·rate·3.1·m3·t + p3) ) / 1.3      // mi in 0.8–1.25\nPLAN.md:249:**The Programme.** A five-day residency: a first full play takes about 45 minutes. Each day is a Morning Check plus three\nPLAN.md:302:| Reps Hall | Annex | Side three-quarter, mirror behind | Lean scrubs the body |\nPLAN.md:314:Tare's Platform. Tare asks one yes/no question for the day (it changes only the remark). Then three tests:\nPLAN.md:323:### Pose Class (about 2.5 min, three poses)\nPLAN.md:345:### Reps Hall (about 90 s, three exercises)\nPLAN.md:360:Rhythm on a step platform in the Annex, three phrases at 104, 112 and 120 BPM (`game.step.bpm` scales them), charts as\nPLAN.md:367:**Beat audio goes on the effects bus, not the music bus.** Music defaults to 10%, so the song is only a bed. Sim `beat`\nPLAN.md:396:A 40 m slackline across the lagoon with three flags. Alternate feet to step: each step moves 0.75 m and kicks you sideways\nPLAN.md:415:gap in the rim. Score: share sunk × 800, plus time left. No Wobble noise here: this one is about touch.\nPLAN.md:417:### Cliff Plunge (three dives)\nPLAN.md:502:              ├─ Group Class → join on mats → three classes → podium\nPLAN.md:504:              └─ About / Credits\nPLAN.md:516:  Resume, Restart Activity, Back to the Island, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About / Credits, Quit to Title.\nPLAN.md:520:- **About / Credits:** paged, from one data file: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, credits\nPLAN.md:551:**A Round** is three classes dealt from `w.rng('deal')` (same seed, same deal): Still Ring, then one of Heron, Hoop or Step, then Still\nPLAN.md:552:Pond, each in its `short` 45 s form with a 6 s lead-in. About 2.7 minutes. Score: the sum, 0–3000. They all play on mats, so they need\nPLAN.md:564:### In AI Hub: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, mode **ghost**\nPLAN.md:567:`labs/game/hub/`: `session.js` (save it as `session-client.txt`), and for tests `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same\nPLAN.md:580:<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Stay the steadiest across three classes\">\nPLAN.md:587:**Startup** **[tested: this shape, on the starter's one scene, passed the harness at 2, 3 (host leaving) and 4 players with the engine running in every frame]**:\nPLAN.md:596:const watchdog = info ? setTimeout(() => AIHub.ready(), 14000) : 0;   // the harness allows 20 s after hello\nPLAN.md:602:unknown query key as a setting and fails with `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, **and the harness still reports PASS**, because the client keeps\nPLAN.md:611:  `keydown` on `window`: the harness sends a synthetic one. The card has no menus or choices, and draws numbers only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\nPLAN.md:614:  `AIHub.progress({ score: 0, label: 'Breathing in' })` and one ghost message, so a slow copy still passes the harness.\nPLAN.md:621:  values short; awards at most three, title at most 24, detail at most 40 (\"Unnervingly Still\").\nPLAN.md:629:**Boot deadline, the one place performance matters.** The harness gives every copy 20 s to call `ready()`. **[tested on SwiftShader]** the starter\nPLAN.md:674:**Characters** (`node x new body`, `node x new build`): Guest (three builds, palette slots for tracksuit), Plumb (very tall, thin; closed-eye arcs; `components: { secondary: { hair: 'ponytail' } }` at spawn for the plait, which the view\nPLAN.md:737:**Music, original, tracker notation** (`defineSong`; `node x new song`; test with `node x audio song:<id>`): light, slightly over-pleasant lobby music with plucks and soft marimba, never a melody from the source.\nPLAN.md:750:**Music is 10% by default:** right after `createAudio()`, call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)`. The engine's default is 0.5 **[source]**. Settings shows it as 10%. Test `audio.volume('music') === 0.1` on a fresh save. Mix each song so it is fine at 100% and a whisper at 10%; nothing the player needs may live only in music.\nPLAN.md:754:- A **syllable bank** per speaker: 16 entries (`defineSfx`), each a short consonant noise then a saw through two bandpass filters at a vowel's formants. **[tested: this renders, and vowels differ measurably; nobody can listen here, so judge by numbers]**\nPLAN.md:758:    { wave: 'noise', dur: 0.015, vol: 0.12, attack: 0.001, filter: { type: 'bandpass', freq: 3200 } },\nPLAN.md:778:**Effects** (`defineSfx`, plus built-ins `sfx:select`, `sfx:confirm`, `sfx:cancel`, `sfx:coin`, `sfx:step*`): wobble creak with pitch by `r`; breath in and out (filtered noise); mat squeak; stamp thump; pebble clack; small and huge splashes; gull squawk; frog ribbit; rope creak; marble roll, a loop with level by speed; hoop whoosh; clap, kick, hat; whistle; ferry horn; thunder; the island's deep groan, pitched by tilt; polite crowd \"ooh\". **Ambience:** sea, birds, wind, rain, as loops with `loop` passes.\nPLAN.md:782:**Checks:** `node x qa audio`, and in the browser read levels with an `AnalyserNode` or render through an `OfflineAudioContext` (`createAudio({ context })`). Nobody can listen here, so prove each voice and song makes sound, and that music sits at 10%.\nPLAN.md:796:- \"Your Wobble Age is 61. Yesterday it was 64. You have become three years younger by standing still. Science.\"\nPLAN.md:833:**Stack:** my-3dge full workspace (TypeScript, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, Vitest, Playwright, HTML/CSS UI). No new npm dependencies. The engine stays read-only: `npm run check` compares every engine file with `engine-lock.json`. Workarounds go in the game; what you needed goes in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\nPLAN.md:860:- **Page to sim** goes three ways, all recorded in replays:\nPLAN.md:866:**Suggested layout** (each file under 400 lines, 600 is a hard error, each opening with a `@file` comment; no enums; no `any`):\nPLAN.md:887:// labs/game/tools/onefile.mjs  (add its @file comment). Usage: node labs/game/tools/onefile.mjs <output.html>\nPLAN.md:894:  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\nPLAN.md:926:| Hub's `?aihub=…` in the query | `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, engine dead, harness still passes | Strip them; assert `__engine.ready` in every frame |\nPLAN.md:935:| No public way into the three.js scene **[source]** | A page cannot add a mesh | Everything drawn is a sim entity: terrain, level, prop, actor, crowd body, telegraph, emitter, or a component with `x`, `z`. All else is HTML |\nPLAN.md:937:| Importing `three` or `rapier` **[source]** | Lint error | Public API only |\nPLAN.md:940:| Bus defaults **[source]** | Music 0.5 | `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` |\nPLAN.md:948:| Fast sway | Doing nothing beats a human thumb **[tested]** | Keep `game.wobble.noiseRate` slow; judge with the delayed-thumb bot |\nPLAN.md:952:## 16. Testing\nPLAN.md:977:- **Settings:** music 0.1 on a fresh save; volumes persist across reload; Erase asks in-game.\nPLAN.md:979:- **About:** every Source Information field and every feedback answer is on the screen.\nPLAN.md:981:- **Hub harness:** serve the built file beside `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` (Node `http` server or `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is your game, stop only that PID: never `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`). Run `harness.html?game=<file>&players=N&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000` for N = 2, 3, 4, then `players=3&…&scenario=host-leave`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass`, with `body[data-complete=\"true\"]` at the end. **Also assert in each frame** `__engine.ready === true`, zero engine errors, a `ghost` entity at 2 players; no console line starting `[AIHub]`; and that the pasted client's SHA-256 from banner to last line matches `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0; compare what you fetched first, the hub may have moved on).\nPLAN.md:982:- **By hand in the harness:** run it once without `auto` at 2 players: its frames are your players on this computer, and clicking a frame gives it the keyboard. New round, Time up, Remove player. Drive it by script and read the state to see the card, ghosts and results; one screenshot.\nPLAN.md:984:**Screenshots, at the end, by eye, 1920 × 1080:** title, island, Pose Class HUD, Still Pond with a lure, The Line, Great Tilt wide shot, results, pause, Dev Mode, About. `node x shot labs/game --png` or a Playwright screenshot: both worked here.\nPLAN.md:992:1. **Skeleton (first hour's job).** Workspace, one-file build, hub client and tags, `game:round` with one mat, harness passing with the engine truly running, `verify.mjs` skeleton.\nPLAN.md:1001:10. **The shell.** Attract, full Dev Mode, Settings, Controls, About, touch-only, no-WebGPU page.\nPLAN.md:1005:**Cut line, if and only if you run out of budget.** Cut whole things and re-flow `days.ts`, leaving no trace (no greyed-out rows, no mentions), in this order: Great Tilt step 3 → Expert variants and outfits → Hoop Patrol → Reps Hall → Island Jog's race (keep the walk) → Cliff Plunge → Step Class. Never cut: Morning Check, Pose Class, Still Pond, The Line, Sand Garden, Paddle Glide, Great Tilt steps 1, 2, 4 and 5, Group Class, hub ghost round, attract, Dev Mode, About.\nPLAN.md:1021:Your TASK.md defines the chat reply, the About / Credits content and the exit interview, in its exact shape. Keep all the answers in one data file (`labs/game/ui/about-data.ts`), so the screen, the reply and the interview agree. They go in the bundle, so write them before the final build, then rerun `verify`.\nPLAN.md:1025:Answers already decided: Plan: the name this file has in your folder. Genre and Perspective as in section 1. Tech: my-3dge at its pinned commit, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, TypeScript. Art: the engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets. Animation: the engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim. Audio: tracker songs, `defineSfx` effects, gibberish syllable voices, all code, music at 10%. Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost; same-screen Group Class on its own. Environment and Model as your TASK.md gives them. Usage: \"added on import\".\nPLAN.md:1029:**Credits must include:** my-3dge (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), @stdlib (Apache-2.0); the AI Hub session client. Animation clips by what you actually copied: Mesh2Motion and Quaternius Universal Animation Library (CC0; credit anyway); **100STYLE dataset, Mason, Starke and Komura, 2022, CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), converted to key poses: required credit with a link and a note of changes** if you use any `STYLE100*` clip; CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database if you use any `CMU` clip (terms in `data/anim/LICENSES/CMU.txt`).\nPLAN.md:1040:| Title: playful riff, picked by a real RNG from 50 | Yours, per TASK.md. This plan just says \"the game's title\": on the title screen, hub card, attract banner, About |\nPLAN.md:1046:| Audio: all code, no files; gibberish voices; music 10% default | 12 |\nPLAN.md:1050:| Testing: headless scripts, full playthrough, one command, failures only, sparing screenshots, no review subagents | 16 |\nPLAN.md:1059:| Source Information, feedback, About screen, chat reply, exit interview | 8, 19 |\nTASK.md:19:Audio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\nTASK.md:24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\nTASK.md:28:Testing: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\nTASK.md:93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\nTASK.md:101:- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\nTASK.md:103:- Testing: testing parameters allowed\nTASK.md:107:- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\nTASK.md:109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\nTASK.md:112:  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\nTASK.md:130:Testing Feedback\n--- package ---\n{\n  \"name\": \"wee-fit-retreat\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"description\": \"A game made with the my-3dge engine.\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=24.10 <25\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc -b tsconfig.check.json\",\n    \"lint\": \"eslint --cache --cache-location node_modules/.cache/eslint/ .\",\n    \"format\": \"prettier --write --cache .\",\n    \"check\": \"node tools/checkAll.ts\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\": \"0.21.0\",\n    \"@stdlib/math-base-special-cos\": \"0.3.1\",\n    \"@stdlib/math-base-special-pow\": \"0.3.1\",\n    \"@stdlib/math-base-special-sin\": \"0.3.1\",\n    \"three\": \"0.182.0\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"1.32.2\",\n    \"@playwright/test\": \"1.64.1\",\n    \"@stryker-mutator/core\": \"9.6.1\",\n    \"@stryker-mutator/vitest-runner\": \"9.6.1\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"24.19.2\",\n    \"@types/three\": \"0.182.0\",\n    \"eslint\": \"9.39.5\",\n    \"eslint-plugin-jsdoc\": \"61.7.1\",\n    \"globals\": \"16.5.0\",\n    \"prettier\": \"3.9.10\",\n    \"tsx\": \"4.23.15\",\n    \"typescript\": \"5.9.3\",\n    \"typescript-eslint\": \"8.72.1\",\n    \"vite\": \"7.3.7\",\n    \"vitest\": \"4.1.12\"\n  },\n  \"allowScripts\": {\n    \"esbuild\": false\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
