{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_612","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- root ---'; ls -la; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- requirements ---'; rg -n -C 2 'AIHub|session\\\\.js|hub:|AI Hub|three|3D|noise|music|About|exit.interview|harness|Testing|testing|last.input' PLAN.md TASK.md | head -n 420; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- game files ---'; wc -l Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/*.{ts,css}\"","aggregated_output":"--- root ---\ntotal 156\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 micha micha  4096 Nov  5 03:54 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 micha micha  4096 Nov  4 22:40 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha 81516 Nov  4 22:40 PLAN.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha   936 Nov  5 04:15 PROGRESS.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha 12560 Nov  4 22:40 TASK.md\ndrwxr-xr-x 11 micha micha  4096 Nov  4 22:55 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha 43976 Nov  5 03:54 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055.html\n--- requirements ---\nTASK.md-17-Animation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\nTASK.md-18-\nTASK.md:19:Audio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\nTASK.md-20-\nTASK.md-21-Online: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub\nTASK.md-22-\nTASK.md-23-Working Environment and deliverable:\nTASK.md:24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\nTASK.md-25-\nTASK.md-26-Performance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\nTASK.md-27-\nTASK.md:28:Testing: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\nTASK.md-29-\nTASK.md-30-Effort: Spend effort however you see fit.\n--\nTASK.md-72-Create a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\nTASK.md-73-\nTASK.md:74:Include a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\nTASK.md-75-\nTASK.md-76-Attract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\n--\nTASK.md-91-\nTASK.md-92-## Source Information\nTASK.md:93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\nTASK.md-94-- Date: 2026-11-04 22:40:55\nTASK.md-95-- Source: the work it's based on\n--\nTASK.md-99-- Art Direction: style used\nTASK.md-100-- Animation: system used\nTASK.md:101:- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\nTASK.md-102-- Online: network features used, or none\nTASK.md:103:- Testing: testing parameters allowed\nTASK.md-104-- Research: research done, or none\nTASK.md-105-- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\nTASK.md-106-- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\nTASK.md:107:- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\nTASK.md-108-\nTASK.md:109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\nTASK.md-110-{\nTASK.md:111:  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\nTASK.md:112:  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\nTASK.md-113-  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\nTASK.md-114-  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n--\nTASK.md-128-The catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\nTASK.md-129-\nTASK.md:130:Testing Feedback\nTASK.md-131-\nTASK.md:132:- How many issues did testing catch?\nTASK.md-133-- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\nTASK.md-134-- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n--\nPLAN.md-6-\nPLAN.md-7-**[tested]** marks what was actually run on this machine on 2026-11-04, against my-3dge at commit e7a1243. **[source]**\nPLAN.md:8:marks what was read in that commit's code but not run. Trust both over your memory of three.js or the engine. Anything\nPLAN.md-9-unmarked is design: yours to tune.\nPLAN.md-10-\nPLAN.md-11-Contents: 1 The game · 2 World and cast · 3 The one verb · 4 Controls · 5 Structure · 6 Activities · 7 The finale ·\nPLAN.md:12:8 Screens · 9 Multiplayer · 10 Art · 11 Animation · 12 Audio · 13 Writing · 14 Tech · 15 Engine traps · 16 Testing ·\nPLAN.md-13-17 Build order · 18 Done · 19 Reports · 20 Brief-to-plan map\nPLAN.md-14-\n--\nPLAN.md-24-rock. On the last night the storm comes, the island tips, and in the finale your thumb's balance *is* the island's.\nPLAN.md-25-\nPLAN.md:26:**Genre:** a 3D sports and wellness anthology of balance activities around a small walkable island, with a daily-ritual\nPLAN.md-27-meta game and a comedy story. **Perspective:** third person throughout: a chase camera on the island, and a purpose-built\nPLAN.md-28-camera for each activity (the table in section 6). **Hub genre:** Sports.\n--\nPLAN.md-45-with personal questions; a serene instructor; earning time-based currency in a plaza; passive-aggressive encouragement.\nPLAN.md-46-\nPLAN.md:47:**Never take (this is an original game, not a recreation):** the word \"Wii\" anywhere in the game except the About\nPLAN.md-48-screen's Source line and the hub's source field; \"Fit Age\", \"Fit Credits\", \"Fit Piggy Bank\", \"Body Test\"; the source's\nPLAN.md-49-trainer look; the Balance Board's shape or lines; Mii-like avatars; Wuhu Island; the source's minigame names, course\n--\nPLAN.md-91-- **Old Nan** (she): 91, Wobble Age 19. Stands where you left her. Nobody has seen her arrive.\nPLAN.md-92-- **The Gull** and **the Frog** (it): recurring menaces. The Gull lands on you at the worst moment. The Frog just looks.\nPLAN.md:93:- **You**: \"Guest\". Pick one of three looks and a tracksuit colour at the pier. No name entry.\nPLAN.md-94-\nPLAN.md-95-**The five-day story** (delivered in one-liners, never in walls of text):\n--\nPLAN.md-118-```\nPLAN.md-119-target  = slew(stick + mouse, 4 units/s) × (gentle ? 0.4 : 1) × reach      // clamped to the disc\nPLAN.md:120:accel   = gain × (target − cob) + instability × cob + noise(t) × (1 − calmEffect × calm) + disturbance\nPLAN.md-121-vel    += accel × dt;   vel *= exp(−damping × dt);   cob += vel × dt\nPLAN.md-122-```\n--\nPLAN.md-127-| `game.wobble.instability` | 3 /s² | 0–10 | How hard you fall away from the centre |\nPLAN.md-128-| `game.wobble.damping` | 5 /s | 1–12 | How heavy the body feels |\nPLAN.md:129:| `game.wobble.noise` | 3.5 /s² | 0–8 | Sway strength |\nPLAN.md:130:| `game.wobble.noiseRate` | 0.15 Hz | 0.05–0.4 | Sway speed: a slow push you lean against |\nPLAN.md-131-| `game.wobble.reach` | 0.9 | 0.5–1 | Full stick's target; a held full stick topples, on purpose |\nPLAN.md-132-| `game.breath.period` | 8 s | 4–14 | One breath, half in, half out |\n--\nPLAN.md-137-\nPLAN.md-138-```\nPLAN.md:139:noise(t) = ( sin(2π·rate·m1·t + p1) + 0.6·sin(2π·rate·1.7·m2·t + p2) + 0.3·sin(2π·rate·3.1·m3·t + p3) ) / 1.3      // mi in 0.8–1.25\nPLAN.md-140-```\nPLAN.md-141-\n--\nPLAN.md-247-## 5. Structure\nPLAN.md-248-\nPLAN.md:249:**The Programme.** A five-day residency: a first full play takes about 45 minutes. Each day is a Morning Check plus three\nPLAN.md-250-activities, from a data table in `labs/game/scenes/data/days.ts`:\nPLAN.md-251-\n--\nPLAN.md-300-| Morning Check | Plaza | Front, low, slow push-in | Lean, a foot |\nPLAN.md-301-| Pose Class | Pavilion | Three-quarter, drifting orbit round your mat | Lean, foot or both |\nPLAN.md:302:| Reps Hall | Annex | Side three-quarter, mirror behind | Lean scrubs the body |\nPLAN.md-303-| Step Class | Annex | Behind and above, class in view | Feet, both, some lean |\nPLAN.md-304-| Still Pond | Pond | Fixed portrait, front | Both, and nothing else |\n--\nPLAN.md-312-### Morning Check (about 75 s)\nPLAN.md-313-\nPLAN.md:314:Tare's Platform. Tare asks one yes/no question for the day (it changes only the remark). Then three tests:\nPLAN.md-315-\nPLAN.md-316-1. **Still Ring**, 12 s: stay inside a ring of r = 0.22, narrowing to 0.16 for the last 4 s. `A` = share of steps inside.\n--\nPLAN.md-321-overshoots, and settles. The Day 1 version introduces each verb with one line at a time.\nPLAN.md-322-\nPLAN.md:323:### Pose Class (about 2.5 min, three poses)\nPLAN.md-324-\nPLAN.md-325-Plumb demonstrates on the front mat (4 s, skippable). \"Now you.\"\n--\nPLAN.md-343-| The Lighthouse (`lighthouse`) | Tiptoe, arms straight up | 0, 0 | Ring 0.14; sway × 1.2 |\nPLAN.md-344-\nPLAN.md:345:### Reps Hall (about 90 s, three exercises)\nPLAN.md-346-\nPLAN.md-347-The signature \"thumb is the exercise\" activity. A tall gauge on the HUD shows a band moving at the tempo\n--\nPLAN.md-358-### Step Class (about 100 s)\nPLAN.md-359-\nPLAN.md:360:Rhythm on a step platform in the Annex, three phrases at 104, 112 and 120 BPM (`game.step.bpm` scales them), charts as\nPLAN.md-361-strings in `labs/game/scenes/data/charts.ts`: `\"L . R . L . R . | L L R . B . . .\"`. Footprints scroll to a hit line on the\nPLAN.md-362-HUD, floor tiles light in the world. Notes: L, R, B (both, a jump) and side steps (lean plus foot).\n--\nPLAN.md-365-follow your combo: lose it and they fall out of time, one by one, politely.\nPLAN.md-366-\nPLAN.md:367:**Beat audio goes on the effects bus, not the music bus.** Music defaults to 10%, so the song is only a bed. Sim `beat`\nPLAN.md-368-events fire claps and kicks at full level. The bed has no drums, so nothing flams against it. Timing is in sim steps,\nPLAN.md-369-never audio time.\n--\nPLAN.md-394-### The Line (about 75 s)\nPLAN.md-395-\nPLAN.md:396:A 40 m slackline across the lagoon with three flags. Alternate feet to step: each step moves 0.75 m and kicks you sideways\nPLAN.md-397-(`game.line.stepKick`, 0.35); the same foot twice is a stumble. Lean x fights it. Gusts every 6–10 s, telegraphed 1.5 s ahead\nPLAN.md-398-by ripples and a flag on Tare's little boat (`game.line.gust`). At 15 m the Gull lands on your arm, adding a steady bias\n--\nPLAN.md-413-the tray does the same. Marbles obey your own 2D integrator in the sim (slope × `game.garden.gravity`, friction, ridge\nPLAN.md-414-segments, holes that catch below `game.garden.sink` speed). Trays are data, 1–3 marbles each, rising to moving rakes and a\nPLAN.md:415:gap in the rim. Score: share sunk × 800, plus time left. No Wobble noise here: this one is about touch.\nPLAN.md-416-\nPLAN.md:417:### Cliff Plunge (three dives)\nPLAN.md-418-\nPLAN.md-419-A 14 m cliff. **Compose:** hold ring and breath for 4 s to fill power. **Go:** release both feet as a swinging gauge peaks.\n--\nPLAN.md-500-Load → Title ─┬─ Begin/Continue → Pier or the day's morning → Island ⇄ Activity → Results → … → Evening → next day\nPLAN.md-501-              ├─ Free Play (Noticeboard, after Day 1)\nPLAN.md:502:              ├─ Group Class → join on mats → three classes → podium\nPLAN.md-503-              ├─ Settings\nPLAN.md:504:              └─ About / Credits\nPLAN.md-505-      (10 s idle on any front-end menu) ⇄ Attract\nPLAN.md-506-```\n--\nPLAN.md-514-- **Evening:** calendar stamp, the age graph, a closing remark, \"Sleep\".\nPLAN.md-515-- **Pause** (Options or Esc, in play and on the island; pauses the sim with `inspector.pause()`, `modal` keeps keys out of play):\nPLAN.md:516:  Resume, Restart Activity, Back to the Island, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About / Credits, Quit to Title.\nPLAN.md-517-- **Settings:** Music (**10% by default**), Effects, Voices, Button icons, Mouse sensitivity, Invert look, Rumble, Steadier Hands (an\nPLAN.md-518-  assist: halves the sway), Reduced Motion (no camera roll or shake), Fullscreen, Erase Save.\nPLAN.md-519-- **Controls:** shows the bindings per scheme; keyboard rebinding through `input.bindingsFor`, `rebind`, `listen`.\nPLAN.md:520:- **About / Credits:** paged, from one data file: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, credits\nPLAN.md-521-  (section 19).\nPLAN.md-522-\n--\nPLAN.md-549-The game has two kinds, both up to four players. They share one module: `labs/game/scenes/round.ts`.\nPLAN.md-550-\nPLAN.md:551:**A Round** is three classes dealt from `w.rng('deal')` (same seed, same deal): Still Ring, then one of Heron, Hoop or Step, then Still\nPLAN.md:552:Pond, each in its `short` 45 s form with a 6 s lead-in. About 2.7 minutes. Score: the sum, 0–3000. They all play on mats, so they need\nPLAN.md-553-nothing but the pavilion.\nPLAN.md-554-\n--\nPLAN.md-562-each seat's input with `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:seats', […])`.\nPLAN.md-563-\nPLAN.md:564:### In AI Hub: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, mode **ghost**\nPLAN.md-565-\nPLAN.md-566-Read the protocol once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Fetch by raw URL, into\nPLAN.md:567:`labs/game/hub/`: `session.js` (save it as `session-client.txt`), and for tests `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same\nPLAN.md-568-folder. **Do not clone the ai-hub repository: it is 5.3 GB.**\nPLAN.md-569-\n--\nPLAN.md-574-\nPLAN.md-575-```html\nPLAN.md:576:<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\nPLAN.md:577:<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\nPLAN.md:578:<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\nPLAN.md:579:<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\nPLAN.md:580:<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Stay the steadiest across three classes\">\nPLAN.md:581:<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: stick or WASD · Feet: L2 R2 or Q E · Breathe: both or Space\">\nPLAN.md:582:<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\nPLAN.md-583-```\nPLAN.md-584-\nPLAN.md:585:Goal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80. Also `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit.\nPLAN.md-586-\nPLAN.md:587:**Startup** **[tested: this shape, on the starter's one scene, passed the harness at 2, 3 (host leaving) and 4 players with the engine running in every frame]**:\nPLAN.md-588-\nPLAN.md-589-```ts\n--\nPLAN.md-591-for (const key of [...search.keys()]) if (key.startsWith('aihub')) search.delete(key); // see the trap below\nPLAN.md-592-search.set('touch', 'off');\nPLAN.md:593:const AIHub = window.AIHub;\nPLAN.md:594:const info = AIHub?.active ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\nPLAN.md-595-if (info) { search.set('scene', 'game:round'); search.set('seed', String(info.seed)); }\nPLAN.md:596:const watchdog = info ? setTimeout(() => AIHub.ready(), 14000) : 0;   // the harness allows 20 s after hello\nPLAN.md-597-engine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['game:island', 'game:round'], search: `?${search}`, /* … */ });\nPLAN.md:598:if (info) { clearTimeout(watchdog); AIHub.ready(); }\nPLAN.md-599-```\nPLAN.md-600-\nPLAN.md-601-**The biggest trap in this whole plan [tested]:** the hub opens the page with `?aihub=1&aihub-seed=N`. `createEngine` treats every\nPLAN.md:602:unknown query key as a setting and fails with `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, **and the harness still reports PASS**, because the client keeps\nPLAN.md-603-answering while the game is dead. Strip those keys, and make your test assert, inside every frame, `__engine.ready === true` and\nPLAN.md-604-`__engine.errors.length === 0`.\n--\nPLAN.md-608-- No title, menus or attract. Straight to the game's own card: the four mats in the pavilion, Plumb in front, each player standing on their\nPLAN.md-609-  mat. It shows the game's title, players in colour with who is ready, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left (from the `card` event).\nPLAN.md:610:  Keys: Enter or Cross answers `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T answers `'more'`, a tap or click works too. Listen for Enter with your own\nPLAN.md:611:  `keydown` on `window`: the harness sends a synthetic one. The card has no menus or choices, and draws numbers only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\nPLAN.md-612-  Make it HTML over whatever is drawn, because the watchdog may call `ready()` while the view is still warming up.\nPLAN.md:613:- `start` arrives; play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`. Send the sim `round.go` then (scene action). On `start` also send one\nPLAN.md:614:  `AIHub.progress({ score: 0, label: 'Breathing in' })` and one ghost message, so a slow copy still passes the harness.\nPLAN.md:615:- During play: `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` whenever it changes (label at most 24 characters, \"Class 2 · 640\"), and every 100 ms\nPLAN.md:616:  `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', e: classIndex, x, y, p: poseId, s: score }, { reliable: false })`. Never above 20 a second.\nPLAN.md-617-- Ghosts are sim entities, because only sim entities can be drawn: incoming messages go through\nPLAN.md-618-  `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:ghosts', […])` to actors on the other mats, tinted with `info.players[i].color`, leans scrubbed by their CoB,\nPLAN.md-619-  name labels from the hub as text (never as HTML), shown only while `e` matches. On `leave`, they walk off politely.\nPLAN.md:620:- Finished: `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once. Stats at most six, names at most 16 characters (\"Wobble Age\", \"Best hold\", \"Breath\"),\nPLAN.md:621:  values short; awards at most three, title at most 24, detail at most 40 (\"Unnervingly Still\").\nPLAN.md-622-- `time-up`: report the current score at once if you have not. `end`: `engine.stop()`, stop all sound, take no input, send nothing.\nPLAN.md:623:- If `engine.ready` is false (no WebGPU): `AIHub.fail('WebGPU required')`.\nPLAN.md-624-- **Rules in a session:** network only through the hub; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation; restart\nPLAN.md:625:  and quit do nothing. Pause is an overlay that never pauses the sim: Resume, volume, button icons. No dev mode. **Create + Options belongs to the hub:**\nPLAN.md-626-  while pad button 8 is held, ignore the engine's `pause`. Storage is a fresh memory copy, handled by the client, so write nothing special for it.\nPLAN.md-627-- Outside a session (`connect` gives `null`, or no client at all in the dev server) the game must behave exactly as it does alone.\nPLAN.md-628-\nPLAN.md:629:**Boot deadline, the one place performance matters.** The harness gives every copy 20 s to call `ready()`. **[tested on SwiftShader]** the starter\nPLAN.md-630-game alone needed 8–16 s per copy at four copies; the engine's playground needed 52–73 s. So `game:round` is a small separate scene with just the\nPLAN.md-631-pavilion, the mats and the cast. The island's cost never reaches a session, and the watchdog covers the rest. Performance is out of scope everywhere else.\n--\nPLAN.md-672-Anything that moves goes on a kinematic body: `body: { type: 'kinematic', shape, size }` in the prop, then `driveBody(physicsOf(w), entity.sceneProp.body, position, rotation, w.dt)` each step, with full rotation **[tested]**. So the tray, hoops, board and sea pose freely. Physically simulated things are dynamic bodies. Anything else is drawn by HTML.\nPLAN.md-673-\nPLAN.md:674:**Characters** (`node x new body`, `node x new build`): Guest (three builds, palette slots for tracksuit), Plumb (very tall, thin; closed-eye arcs; `components: { secondary: { hair: 'ponytail' } }` at spawn for the plait, which the view\nPLAN.md-675-swings by itself when the body moves **[source]**), Gerald (`build:bulky`-like with huge calves), Bex, Nan (small, stooped), Tare (a very short build; torso a flat drum, a dial on the front, two stubby legs, no arms). On a results\nPLAN.md-676-screen Tare's dial is a large CSS dial with a live needle. The Gull and the Frog are engine **blob rigs** (with wings for the Gull) as crowd bodies: `addAgent`, `crowdBody`, cheap and very funny; `labs/box/cast/` has worked examples.\n--\nPLAN.md-735-All sound is code and data. No audio files. Test: the built HTML holds no `data:audio`, `.mp3`, `.wav` or `.ogg`.\nPLAN.md-736-\nPLAN.md:737:**Music, original, tracker notation** (`defineSong`; `node x new song`; test with `node x audio song:<id>`): light, slightly over-pleasant lobby music with plucks and soft marimba, never a melody from the source.\nPLAN.md-738-\nPLAN.md-739-| Song | Use | Character |\n--\nPLAN.md-748-| `song:stamp` | Results | A short jingle, played once |\nPLAN.md-749-\nPLAN.md:750:**Music is 10% by default:** right after `createAudio()`, call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)`. The engine's default is 0.5 **[source]**. Settings shows it as 10%. Test `audio.volume('music') === 0.1` on a fresh save. Mix each song so it is fine at 100% and a whisper at 10%; nothing the player needs may live only in music.\nPLAN.md-751-\nPLAN.md-752-**Voices: Animalese-style gibberish, written in code.** The engine has no speech. Build it from sound data:\nPLAN.md-753-\nPLAN.md:754:- A **syllable bank** per speaker: 16 entries (`defineSfx`), each a short consonant noise then a saw through two bandpass filters at a vowel's formants. **[tested: this renders, and vowels differ measurably; nobody can listen here, so judge by numbers]**\nPLAN.md-755-\nPLAN.md-756-  ```ts\nPLAN.md-757-  const syllable = (f0: number, f1: number, f2: number) => ({ bus: 'ui', voices: [\nPLAN.md:758:    { wave: 'noise', dur: 0.015, vol: 0.12, attack: 0.001, filter: { type: 'bandpass', freq: 3200 } },\nPLAN.md-759-    { wave: 'saw', freq: f0, to: f0 * 0.92, at: 0.012, dur: 0.07, vol: 0.5, attack: 0.006, filter: { type: 'bandpass', freq: f1 }, q: 7 },\nPLAN.md-760-    { wave: 'saw', freq: f0, to: f0 * 0.92, at: 0.012, dur: 0.07, vol: 0.35, attack: 0.006, filter: { type: 'bandpass', freq: f2 }, q: 9 },\n--\nPLAN.md-776-- **`say(speaker, text)`** in `labs/game/audio/voice.ts`: one syllable per two letters, hashed from the letters so the same line always babbles the same way; `audio.play(id, { pitch, when, vol, bus: 'ui', duck: true })`; pitch contour rises on \"?\" and falls on \".\"; text types in sync. Voices slider scales `vol`. Silence on spaces, longer on punctuation.\nPLAN.md-777-\nPLAN.md:778:**Effects** (`defineSfx`, plus built-ins `sfx:select`, `sfx:confirm`, `sfx:cancel`, `sfx:coin`, `sfx:step*`): wobble creak with pitch by `r`; breath in and out (filtered noise); mat squeak; stamp thump; pebble clack; small and huge splashes; gull squawk; frog ribbit; rope creak; marble roll, a loop with level by speed; hoop whoosh; clap, kick, hat; whistle; ferry horn; thunder; the island's deep groan, pitched by tilt; polite crowd \"ooh\". **Ambience:** sea, birds, wind, rain, as loops with `loop` passes.\nPLAN.md-779-\nPLAN.md-780-In `onFrame`: `audio.update(frame.camera, frame.queries ?? undefined)`, then play each new sim event by `seq` from `frame.world.events.trace()`. Reset your `seq` when `frame.world` changes (after a restart).\nPLAN.md-781-\nPLAN.md:782:**Checks:** `node x qa audio`, and in the browser read levels with an `AnalyserNode` or render through an `OfflineAudioContext` (`createAudio({ context })`). Nobody can listen here, so prove each voice and song makes sound, and that music sits at 10%.\nPLAN.md-783-\nPLAN.md-784----\n--\nPLAN.md-794-- \"I no longer measure weight. It made people sad, and it made me sad. Now I only measure how much you wobble.\"\nPLAN.md-795-- \"Please step on me. Not like that. Actually, like that is fine.\"\nPLAN.md:796:- \"Your Wobble Age is 61. Yesterday it was 64. You have become three years younger by standing still. Science.\"\nPLAN.md-797-- \"That was your best score so far. It is also your only score so far. Well done on both.\"\nPLAN.md-798-- \"You came back. A lot of people say they will.\"\n--\nPLAN.md-831-## 14. Tech\nPLAN.md-832-\nPLAN.md:833:**Stack:** my-3dge full workspace (TypeScript, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, Vitest, Playwright, HTML/CSS UI). No new npm dependencies. The engine stays read-only: `npm run check` compares every engine file with `engine-lock.json`. Workarounds go in the game; what you needed goes in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\nPLAN.md-834-\nPLAN.md-835-**Setup [tested], in the empty dev folder:**\n--\nPLAN.md-858-- **Sim-side** (lint enforces it only under `labs/game/scenes/` and `labs/game/cast/`, so keep all sim code there; imports only `engine/sim-api.ts`): flow, wobble, events, bot, director, round, data tables.\nPLAN.md-859-- **Page** (imports `engine/index.ts`): `labs/game/main.ts`, `ui/`, `audio/`, `hub/`. It reads the sim and never writes it.\nPLAN.md:860:- **Page to sim** goes three ways, all recorded in replays:\nPLAN.md-861-  1. Scene `actions` **[tested]**: `defineScene(id, { actions: { 'game.start': (w, args) => … } })`, called with `inspector.actions.run('game.start', { event: 'pond' })`. Runs between steps, recorded in replays. **Use this for every menu pick:** `game.begin` (with the save's state, since the sim cannot read the store), `game.start`, `game.leave`, `game.sleep`, `round.go`.\nPLAN.md-862-  2. Custom intents: `input.virtual.axis('game:mouse', [dx, dy])`. Held until changed, and dropped while `modal()` is true.\n--\nPLAN.md-892-const result = await build({\nPLAN.md-893-  root, configFile: false, logLevel: 'warn', base: './',\nPLAN.md:894:  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\nPLAN.md-895-  build: { write: false, modulePreload: false, cssCodeSplit: false, assetsInlineLimit: () => true, chunkSizeWarningLimit: Infinity,\nPLAN.md-896-    rollupOptions: { input: { game: join(root, 'labs/game/index.html') }, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } } },\n--\nPLAN.md-924-| Trap | What happens | Do this |\nPLAN.md-925-|---|---|---|\nPLAN.md:926:| Hub's `?aihub=…` in the query | `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, engine dead, harness still passes | Strip them; assert `__engine.ready` in every frame |\nPLAN.md-927-| No `CHROMIUM_PATH` | `x shot` and friends crash on `/opt/pw-browsers/chromium` | Export the headless shell path (section 14) |\nPLAN.md-928-| A crashed `x` browser launch | The process hangs after printing the crash | Wrap browser commands in `timeout` |\n--\nPLAN.md-933-| `playClip` in `setup` | `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT` | `clips.play` at spawn, or from the first step |\nPLAN.md-934-| `seekClip` **[source]** | Moves only the top clip | Write `clips.state.slots[i].t` |\nPLAN.md:935:| No public way into the three.js scene **[source]** | A page cannot add a mesh | Everything drawn is a sim entity: terrain, level, prop, actor, crowd body, telegraph, emitter, or a component with `x`, `z`. All else is HTML |\nPLAN.md-936-| `modal()` true **[source]** | Intents dropped, virtual device too | Menu picks go through scene actions |\nPLAN.md:937:| Importing `three` or `rapier` **[source]** | Lint error | Public API only |\nPLAN.md-938-| `input.prompt()` **[source]** | Xbox labels for unknown pads | Own glyph table (section 4) |\nPLAN.md-939-| Engine touch stick **[source]** | Appears on touch screens | `touch=off` in the query |\nPLAN.md:940:| Bus defaults **[source]** | Music 0.5 | `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` |\nPLAN.md-941-| Hub client through a formatter **[source]** | Hub rejects it | Keep it as `.txt`, inject at build |\nPLAN.md-942-| `git` in the dev folder | It belongs to the larger repository around it | Do not `git init`, commit or restore there, despite `AGENTS.md`'s \"commit as you go\", unless your TASK.md asks |\n--\nPLAN.md-946-| `npm run dev` | Binds port 5173 strictly, on a machine other agents share; `PORT=0` falls back to 5173 **[source]** | Prefer the built file on `file://` and `node x shot`, which picks a free port. If you must, pick a free port for `PORT` |\nPLAN.md-947-| A map with `lock: true` on a menu **[source]** | A click behind the menu takes the pointer | `lock: false` on front-end screens |\nPLAN.md:948:| Fast sway | Doing nothing beats a human thumb **[tested]** | Keep `game.wobble.noiseRate` slow; judge with the delayed-thumb bot |\nPLAN.md-949-\nPLAN.md-950----\nPLAN.md-951-\nPLAN.md:952:## 16. Testing\nPLAN.md-953-\nPLAN.md-954-**One command:** `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` prints only failures and one final count line. `--quick` stops after the Node stages. Rerun it only after changing code it covers. Prefer scripts: screenshots only for what a script cannot check. Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n--\nPLAN.md-975-- **Attract:** starts at 10–11 s idle on the title, shows several activities across a loop, exits on a key, a click and a pad press; the save is untouched.\nPLAN.md-976-- **Pause and dev:** pause menu reaches Dev Mode; a slider changes behaviour; Reset restores defaults; jumps work; not present in a session.\nPLAN.md:977:- **Settings:** music 0.1 on a fresh save; volumes persist across reload; Erase asks in-game.\nPLAN.md-978-- **Touch-only:** Playwright's iPhone and tablet profiles in Chromium: \"Controller or keyboard required\", a Settings button that opens by `page.touchscreen.tap`, attract runs, no touch controls in the DOM.\nPLAN.md:979:- **About:** every Source Information field and every feedback answer is on the screen.\nPLAN.md-980-- **Standalone hub checks, as the hub's own test does:** press Enter, Space, Enter, Space; the client is there and inactive; `Math.random` is untouched; the screen is drawn; no errors.\nPLAN.md:981:- **Hub harness:** serve the built file beside `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` (Node `http` server or `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is your game, stop only that PID: never `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`). Run `harness.html?game=<file>&players=N&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000` for N = 2, 3, 4, then `players=3&…&scenario=host-leave`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass`, with `body[data-complete=\"true\"]` at the end. **Also assert in each frame** `__engine.ready === true`, zero engine errors, a `ghost` entity at 2 players; no console line starting `[AIHub]`; and that the pasted client's SHA-256 from banner to last line matches `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0; compare what you fetched first, the hub may have moved on).\nPLAN.md:982:- **By hand in the harness:** run it once without `auto` at 2 players: its frames are your players on this computer, and clicking a frame gives it the keyboard. New round, Time up, Remove player. Drive it by script and read the state to see the card, ghosts and results; one screenshot.\nPLAN.md-983-\nPLAN.md:984:**Screenshots, at the end, by eye, 1920 × 1080:** title, island, Pose Class HUD, Still Pond with a lure, The Line, Great Tilt wide shot, results, pause, Dev Mode, About. `node x shot labs/game --png` or a Playwright screenshot: both worked here.\nPLAN.md-985-\nPLAN.md-986----\n--\nPLAN.md-990-Do the risky integration first. The game should be shippable, in a smaller form, at every milestone.\nPLAN.md-991-\nPLAN.md:992:1. **Skeleton (first hour's job).** Workspace, one-file build, hub client and tags, `game:round` with one mat, harness passing with the engine truly running, `verify.mjs` skeleton.\nPLAN.md-993-2. **The verb.** Wobble Model, action maps, mouse lean, Balance Disc, glyphs, one activity (Still Ring), its bot, tests, dev sliders. Tune until holding still is fun by itself. The bot tells you it is winnable; numbers tell you it isn't trivial.\nPLAN.md-994-3. **The body.** Clip set, scrubbing, Guest and Plumb, Pose Class. Voice system early: it carries the tone.\n--\nPLAN.md-999-8. **The finale.** Great Tilt, ending, credits.\nPLAN.md-1000-9. **Together.** Group Class; hub ghosts, own card, full round.\nPLAN.md:1001:10. **The shell.** Attract, full Dev Mode, Settings, Controls, About, touch-only, no-WebGPU page.\nPLAN.md-1002-11. **Polish.** All 200+ lines, songs, ambience, effects, camera moves, rumble, Expert variants, outfits.\nPLAN.md-1003-12. **Finish.** Section 18 and 19.\nPLAN.md-1004-\nPLAN.md:1005:**Cut line, if and only if you run out of budget.** Cut whole things and re-flow `days.ts`, leaving no trace (no greyed-out rows, no mentions), in this order: Great Tilt step 3 → Expert variants and outfits → Hoop Patrol → Reps Hall → Island Jog's race (keep the walk) → Cliff Plunge → Step Class. Never cut: Morning Check, Pose Class, Still Pond, The Line, Sand Garden, Paddle Glide, Great Tilt steps 1, 2, 4 and 5, Group Class, hub ghost round, attract, Dev Mode, About.\nPLAN.md-1006-\nPLAN.md-1007----\n--\nPLAN.md-1019-## 19. Reports\nPLAN.md-1020-\nPLAN.md:1021:Your TASK.md defines the chat reply, the About / Credits content and the exit interview, in its exact shape. Keep all the answers in one data file (`labs/game/ui/about-data.ts`), so the screen, the reply and the interview agree. They go in the bundle, so write them before the final build, then rerun `verify`.\nPLAN.md-1022-\nPLAN.md:1023:**Keep a running tally as you go** of the issues testing catches, and which were critical: you will be asked for both, and for your most and least helpful test. Note engine surprises in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` when they happen.\nPLAN.md-1024-\nPLAN.md:1025:Answers already decided: Plan: the name this file has in your folder. Genre and Perspective as in section 1. Tech: my-3dge at its pinned commit, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, TypeScript. Art: the engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets. Animation: the engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim. Audio: tracker songs, `defineSfx` effects, gibberish syllable voices, all code, music at 10%. Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost; same-screen Group Class on its own. Environment and Model as your TASK.md gives them. Usage: \"added on import\".\nPLAN.md-1026-\nPLAN.md-1027-Hub catalogue suggestions: type `Game`; genre `Sports`; source `Wii Fit`; series empty (the source is its own franchise); players `1–4`; controls \"Lean: left stick, WASD or mouse · Feet: L2 R2, Q E or mouse buttons · Breathe: both\"; tags from `3d`, `third-person`, `comedy`, `arcade`, `sports`, `story`. Tagline idea: \"Stand still. It is harder than it looks.\"\nPLAN.md-1028-\nPLAN.md:1029:**Credits must include:** my-3dge (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), @stdlib (Apache-2.0); the AI Hub session client. Animation clips by what you actually copied: Mesh2Motion and Quaternius Universal Animation Library (CC0; credit anyway); **100STYLE dataset, Mason, Starke and Komura, 2022, CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), converted to key poses: required credit with a link and a note of changes** if you use any `STYLE100*` clip; CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database if you use any `CMU` clip (terms in `data/anim/LICENSES/CMU.txt`).\nPLAN.md-1030-\nPLAN.md-1031----\n--\nPLAN.md-1038-|---|---|\nPLAN.md-1039-| Genre and perspective chosen to fit | 1, 6 |\nPLAN.md:1040:| Title: playful riff, picked by a real RNG from 50 | Yours, per TASK.md. This plan just says \"the game's title\": on the title screen, hub card, attract banner, About |\nPLAN.md-1041-| Research: your choice | Not needed beyond this plan; report what you did |\nPLAN.md-1042-| Single HTML; downloads optional | 14 (everything inlined) |\n--\nPLAN.md-1044-| Art: engine's native style base; new assets for the source's feel | 10 |\nPLAN.md-1045-| Animation: engine's system base; new animations | 11 |\nPLAN.md:1046:| Audio: all code, no files; gibberish voices; music 10% default | 12 |\nPLAN.md-1047-| Online and multiplayer: hub integration and on its own | 9 |\nPLAN.md-1048-| Dev folder, separate modules, bundle; shared machine rules | 14, 16 |\nPLAN.md-1049-| Performance out of scope | 9 (one protocol deadline only) |\nPLAN.md:1050:| Testing: headless scripts, full playthrough, one command, failures only, sparing screenshots, no review subagents | 16 |\nPLAN.md-1051-| Original game; distinctive world, characters, themes, tone in mechanics, pacing, UX | 1, 2, 3, 13 |\nPLAN.md-1052-| Feature-complete demo showing all mechanics; vertical slice; infrastructure to grow | 5, 6, 7, data tables in 5 and 14 |\n--\nPLAN.md-1054-| Attract: 10 s idle, looping, AI may cheat, any input exits | 8 |\nPLAN.md-1055-| Narrative tone like the source | 13 |\nPLAN.md:1056:| 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard and mouse; hover focus; prompts by last input; PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option; no dense screens | 4, 8 |\nPLAN.md-1057-| Touch-only: no touch controls, the message, Settings, attract runs | 8 |\nPLAN.md-1058-| Done: no TODOs or stubs | 18 |\nPLAN.md:1059:| Source Information, feedback, About screen, chat reply, exit interview | 8, 19 |\n--- game files ---\n   35 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/art.ts\n   20 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/audio.ts\n   22 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/best.test.ts\n   33 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/best.ts\n   90 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/bot.ts\n  201 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts\n   49 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/programme.ts\n   43 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts\n   95 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/wobble.ts\n    2 Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/styles.css\n  590 total\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
