{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_680","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- guide sections ---'; rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} |attract|noise:|noise |hub|probe|About|animation|Dev Mode|Music|music'\"' PLAN.md | head -200; printf '\\\\n%s\\\\n' '--- engine structure ---'; ls Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine; rg -n 'export (class|function|interface|type).*([Pp]uppet|[Aa]nim|[Cc]amera|[Mm]esh|[Gg]eometry)' Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine | head -80; printf '\\\\n%s\\\\n' '--- npm config ---'; cat Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/package.json; printf '\\\\n%s\\\\n' '--- local instructions ---'; find Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs -name AGENTS.md -print\"","aggregated_output":"--- guide sections ---\n1:# Game plan: a balance-and-wellness game inspired by Wii Fit\n17:## 1. The game\n34:2. **Your thumb is the exercise.** The character's limbs follow the input directly, by scrubbing animation (section 11).\n47:**Never take (this is an original game, not a recreation):** the word \"Wii\" anywhere in the game except the About\n48:screen's Source line and the hub's source field; \"Fit Age\", \"Fit Credits\", \"Fit Piggy Bank\", \"Body Test\"; the source's\n57:## 2. World and cast\n108:## 3. The one verb: the Wobble Model\n176:## 4. Controls\n247:## 5. Structure\n291:## 6. Activities\n294:bot, attract, short? }` in `labs/game/scenes/events/`. `step` emits sim events; the page turns them into text, sound and\n295:HUD. `bot` writes the same seat input a player does, and is used by tests, attract mode and dev auto-play. `short` is the\n312:### Morning Check (about 75 s)\n323:### Pose Class (about 2.5 min, three poses)\n345:### Reps Hall (about 90 s, three exercises)\n358:### Step Class (about 100 s)\n367:**Beat audio goes on the effects bus, not the music bus.** Music defaults to 10%, so the song is only a bed. Sim `beat`\n371:### Still Pond (75 s; 45 s in rounds)\n394:### The Line (about 75 s)\n403:### Paddle Glide (75 s)\n410:### Sand Garden (90 s, five trays)\n415:gap in the rim. Score: share sunk × 800, plus time left. No Wobble noise here: this one is about touch.\n417:### Cliff Plunge (three dives)\n422:always scores 4. Wait too long at the lip and you slip off anyway, a small splash, low cards. This is the attract mode's best shot.\n424:### Hoop Patrol (60 s)\n432:### Island Jog (about 150 s)\n439:### Group Class\n445:## 7. The finale: The Great Tilt (about 4 minutes)\n480:## 8. Screens and UX\n504:              └─ About / Credits\n516:  Resume, Restart Activity, Back to the Island, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, About / Credits, Quit to Title.\n517:- **Settings:** Music (**10% by default**), Effects, Voices, Button icons, Mouse sensitivity, Invert look, Rumble, Steadier Hands (an\n520:- **About / Credits:** paged, from one data file: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, credits\n523:**Dev Mode** (from the pause menu; absent in hub sessions; a clear panel that works with pad, keyboard and mouse):\n547:## 9. Multiplayer\n552:Pond, each in its `short` 45 s form with a 6 s lead-in. About 2.7 minutes. Score: the sum, 0–3000. They all play on mats, so they need\n555:### On its own: Group Class\n564:### In AI Hub: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, mode **ghost**\n566:Read the protocol once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Fetch by raw URL, into\n567:`labs/game/hub/`: `session.js` (save it as `session-client.txt`), and for tests `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same\n568:folder. **Do not clone the ai-hub repository: it is 5.3 GB.**\n576:<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n577:<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n578:<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n579:<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n580:<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Stay the steadiest across three classes\">\n581:<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: stick or WASD · Feet: L2 R2 or Q E · Breathe: both or Space\">\n582:<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n585:Goal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80. Also `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit.\n591:for (const key of [...search.keys()]) if (key.startsWith('aihub')) search.delete(key); // see the trap below\n601:**The biggest trap in this whole plan [tested]:** the hub opens the page with `?aihub=1&aihub-seed=N`. `createEngine` treats every\n608:- No title, menus or attract. Straight to the game's own card: the four mats in the pavilion, Plumb in front, each player standing on their\n619:  name labels from the hub as text (never as HTML), shown only while `e` matches. On `leave`, they walk off politely.\n624:- **Rules in a session:** network only through the hub; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation; restart\n625:  and quit do nothing. Pause is an overlay that never pauses the sim: Resume, volume, button icons. No dev mode. **Create + Options belongs to the hub:**\n635:## 10. Art direction\n683:## 11. Animation\n723:**New animations to write:** the eight poses; lean strips; `DeepKnee`, `SideLunge`; `StepUpL`, `StepUpR`, `SideStep`, `Jump`; `HipCircle` (a looped key ring scrubbed by angle); `Somersault` (`body` lean running to 720°, since values keep counting past 360°) and\n733:## 12. Audio\n737:**Music, original, tracker notation** (`defineSong`; `node x new song`; test with `node x audio song:<id>`): light, slightly over-pleasant lobby music with plucks and soft marimba, never a melody from the source.\n750:**Music is 10% by default:** right after `createAudio()`, call `audio.volume('music', 0.1)`. The engine's default is 0.5 **[source]**. Settings shows it as 10%. Test `audio.volume('music') === 0.1` on a fresh save. Mix each song so it is fine at 100% and a whisper at 10%; nothing the player needs may live only in music.\n754:- A **syllable bank** per speaker: 16 entries (`defineSfx`), each a short consonant noise then a saw through two bandpass filters at a vowel's formants. **[tested: this renders, and vowels differ measurably; nobody can listen here, so judge by numbers]**\n782:**Checks:** `node x qa audio`, and in the browser read levels with an `AnalyserNode` or render through an `OfflineAudioContext` (`createAudio({ context })`). Nobody can listen here, so prove each voice and song makes sound, and that music sits at 10%.\n786:## 13. Writing\n831:## 14. Tech\n838:src=$(mktemp -d) && git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge \"$src\" && node \"$src/tools/game/new-game.mjs\" . --name <short-lowercase-name>\n852:**The pilot.** Keep every character, the Guest included, at `player: false`, and let one sim system, `pilot`, write `actor.intents` each step: the step's `move` on the island, nothing in an activity, the bot's in attract, the slope added in the finale. This one rule makes roam, activities, attract and the Great Tilt the same code. Cameras follow only a `player: true` actor by themselves, so give them the Guest's feet with `createEngine({ cameraInput: () => ({ follow: feet }) })` **[tested: walks and the chase camera follows]**.\n859:- **Page** (imports `engine/index.ts`): `labs/game/main.ts`, `ui/`, `audio/`, `hub/`. It reads the sim and never writes it.\n877:  hub/      session.ts  session-client.txt  tags.html\n884:**The single HTML [tested: 6.7 MB, 4 s, opens from file://, client stays byte-identical].** `node x html` is engine-only, so the game carries this. The session client goes in as text, so no formatter ever touches it: the hub rejects an edited copy by SHA-256.\n911:const client = readFileSync('labs/game/hub/session-client.txt', 'utf8');\n912:const tags = readFileSync('labs/game/hub/tags.html', 'utf8');\n918:**`window.__game`**, a small read-only state handle the page publishes for tests: screen, attract, last device, glyph set, volumes, day, event, focus.\n922:## 15. Engine traps (hit on this machine unless marked **[source]**)\n926:| Hub's `?aihub=…` in the query | `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, engine dead, harness still passes | Strip them; assert `__engine.ready` in every frame |\n940:| Bus defaults **[source]** | Music 0.5 | `audio.volume('music', 0.1)` |\n952:## 16. Testing\n976:- **Pause and dev:** pause menu reaches Dev Mode; a slider changes behaviour; Reset restores defaults; jumps work; not present in a session.\n977:- **Settings:** music 0.1 on a fresh save; volumes persist across reload; Erase asks in-game.\n978:- **Touch-only:** Playwright's iPhone and tablet profiles in Chromium: \"Controller or keyboard required\", a Settings button that opens by `page.touchscreen.tap`, attract runs, no touch controls in the DOM.\n979:- **About:** every Source Information field and every feedback answer is on the screen.\n980:- **Standalone hub checks, as the hub's own test does:** press Enter, Space, Enter, Space; the client is there and inactive; `Math.random` is untouched; the screen is drawn; no errors.\n981:- **Hub harness:** serve the built file beside `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` (Node `http` server or `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is your game, stop only that PID: never `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`). Run `harness.html?game=<file>&players=N&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000` for N = 2, 3, 4, then `players=3&…&scenario=host-leave`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass`, with `body[data-complete=\"true\"]` at the end. **Also assert in each frame** `__engine.ready === true`, zero engine errors, a `ghost` entity at 2 players; no console line starting `[AIHub]`; and that the pasted client's SHA-256 from banner to last line matches `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (client 1.4.0; compare what you fetched first, the hub may have moved on).\n984:**Screenshots, at the end, by eye, 1920 × 1080:** title, island, Pose Class HUD, Still Pond with a lure, The Line, Great Tilt wide shot, results, pause, Dev Mode, About. `node x shot labs/game --png` or a Playwright screenshot: both worked here.\n988:## 17. Build order\n992:1. **Skeleton (first hour's job).** Workspace, one-file build, hub client and tags, `game:round` with one mat, harness passing with the engine truly running, `verify.mjs` skeleton.\n1000:9. **Together.** Group Class; hub ghosts, own card, full round.\n1001:10. **The shell.** Attract, full Dev Mode, Settings, Controls, About, touch-only, no-WebGPU page.\n1005:**Cut line, if and only if you run out of budget.** Cut whole things and re-flow `days.ts`, leaving no trace (no greyed-out rows, no mentions), in this order: Great Tilt step 3 → Expert variants and outfits → Hoop Patrol → Reps Hall → Island Jog's race (keep the walk) → Cliff Plunge → Step Class. Never cut: Morning Check, Pose Class, Still Pond, The Line, Sand Garden, Paddle Glide, Great Tilt steps 1, 2, 4 and 5, Group Class, hub ghost round, attract, Dev Mode, About.\n1009:## 18. Done\n1019:## 19. Reports\n1021:Your TASK.md defines the chat reply, the About / Credits content and the exit interview, in its exact shape. Keep all the answers in one data file (`labs/game/ui/about-data.ts`), so the screen, the reply and the interview agree. They go in the bundle, so write them before the final build, then rerun `verify`.\n1025:Answers already decided: Plan: the name this file has in your folder. Genre and Perspective as in section 1. Tech: my-3dge at its pinned commit, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, TypeScript. Art: the engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets. Animation: the engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim. Audio: tracker songs, `defineSfx` effects, gibberish syllable voices, all code, music at 10%. Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost; same-screen Group Class on its own. Environment and Model as your TASK.md gives them. Usage: \"added on import\".\n1033:## 20. Brief-to-plan map\n1040:| Title: playful riff, picked by a real RNG from 50 | Yours, per TASK.md. This plan just says \"the game's title\": on the title screen, hub card, attract banner, About |\n1045:| Animation: engine's system base; new animations | 11 |\n1046:| Audio: all code, no files; gibberish voices; music 10% default | 12 |\n1047:| Online and multiplayer: hub integration and on its own | 9 |\n1057:| Touch-only: no touch controls, the message, Settings, attract runs | 8 |\n1059:| Source Information, feedback, About screen, chat reply, exit interview | 8, 19 |\n\n--- engine structure ---\nLICENSE\nanim\napp\naudio\ncore\ndev\ngfx\nindex.ts\ninput\nphysics\nsim\nsim-api.ts\nui\nworld\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/index.ts:62:export type { BoxOptions } from './gfx/geometry/box';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/index.ts:64:export type { RoundedBoxOptions } from './gfx/geometry/roundedBox';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/index.ts:66:export type { LimbOptions } from './gfx/geometry/limb';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/index.ts:68:export type { RampOptions } from './gfx/geometry/ramp';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/index.ts:70:export type { FrustumOptions } from './gfx/geometry/frustum';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/index.ts:73:export type { PillarOptions } from './gfx/geometry/pillar';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/index.ts:74:export type { PillarPart } from './gfx/geometry/pillar';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/index.ts:76:export type { RingOptions } from './gfx/geometry/ring';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/engine/index.ts:82:export type { GeometryEntry } from '