the engine?\n142:- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n144:- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n146:Prompt Feedback\n148:- What did you like most about this prompt?\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts:34:export function modalView(modal: string, preferences: Preferences): string {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:7:import { welcomeView, hubView, gameView, resultView, modalView } from './view';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:10:type Modal = 'settings' | 'about' | 'pause' | 'touch' | null;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:58:function render(): void {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:62:  root.innerHTML = content + (modal ? modalView(modal, save.preferences) : '');\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:66:function openGame(preview = false): void {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:72:function finish(): void {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:162:function frame(now: number): void {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_856","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '88,170p' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- GAME INTEGRATION ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,220p' Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts; printf '\\\\n--- MODAL ---\\\\n'; rg -n -C 6 'modalView|data-action=\\\"close|modal-overlay|modal-card' Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/{view.ts,styles.css}; printf '\\\\n--- HUB PLAN ---\\\\n'; sed -n '565,635p' PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_856","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '88,170p' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- GAME INTEGRATION ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,220p' Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts; printf '\\\\n--- MODAL ---\\\\n'; rg -n -C 6 'modalView|data-action=\\\"close|modal-overlay|modal-card' Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/{view.ts,styles.css}; printf '\\\\n--- HUB PLAN ---\\\\n'; sed -n '565,635p' PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"\n## Done\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n\n## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:40:55\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n  }\n}\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n\nTesting Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch?\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n\nEngine Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about the engine?\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n\nPrompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n- What would you change in this prompt?\n\n--- GAME INTEGRATION ---\n/** @file Runs the retreat's menus, input, and balance sessions. */\nimport './styles.css';\nimport './extras.css';\nimport { DAYS, rankFor, type Activity } from './programme';\nimport { DEFAULT_BALANCE, action, createSession, stepSession, targetFor, type Session } from './wobble';\nimport { Soundscape } from './audio';\nimport { welcomeView, hubView, gameView, resultView, modalView } from './view';\n\ntype Screen = 'welcome' | 'hub' | 'playing' | 'result';\ntype Modal = 'settings' | 'about' | 'pause' | 'touch' | null;\ntype Preferences = { sound: boolean; motion: boolean; contrast: boolean; assist: boolean };\ntype Save = { unlocked: number; scores: Record<string, number>; preferences: Preferences };\n\nconst root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#app')!;\nconst storageKey = 'wee-fit-retreat-save-v1';\nconst defaults: Save = { unlocked: 0, scores: {}, preferences: { sound: true, motion: false, contrast: false, assist: false } };\nfunction load(): Save {\n  try {\n    const saved = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(storageKey) || '{}') as Partial<Save>;\n    return { ...defaults, ...saved, scores: saved.scores || {}, preferences: { ...defaults.preferences, ...saved.preferences } };\n  } catch { return structuredClone(defaults); }\n}\nlet save = load();\nlet screen: Screen = 'welcome';\nlet modal: Modal = null;\nlet dayIndex = 0;\nlet activityIndex = 0;\nlet session: Session | null = null;\nlet attract = false;\nlet lastInput = performance.now();\nlet lastFrame = 0;\nlet accumulator = 0;\nlet lastPadButtons: boolean[] = [];\nlet lastInputType: 'keyboard' | 'controller' = 'keyboard';\nconst keys = new Set<string>();\nconst sounds = new Soundscape();\nsounds.enabled = save.preferences.sound;\n\nfunction persist(): void {\n  try { localStorage.setItem(storageKey, JSON.stringify(save)); } catch { /* storage can be unavailable */ }\n}\nfunction flatIndex(day: number, activity: number): number {\n  return DAYS.slice(0, day).reduce((total, item) => total + item.activities.length, 0) + activity;\n}\nfunction selected(): Activity { return DAYS[dayIndex].activities[activityIndex]; }\nfunction selectFlat(index: number): void {\n  let remaining = index;\n  for (let day = 0; day < DAYS.length; day++) {\n    if (remaining < DAYS[day].activities.length) { dayIndex = day; activityIndex = remaining; return; }\n    remaining -= DAYS[day].activities.length;\n  }\n}\nfunction totalActivities(): number { return DAYS.reduce((total, day) => total + day.activities.length, 0); }\nfunction playSound(name: 'click' | 'hit' | 'finish' | 'miss'): void { try { sounds.play(name); } catch { /* audio is optional */ } }\nfunction isTouchOnly(): boolean {\n  return matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)').matches && !Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.() || []).some(Boolean);\n}\nfunction render(): void {\n  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('reduced-motion', save.preferences.motion);\n  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('high-contrast', save.preferences.contrast);\n  const content = screen === 'welcome' ? welcomeView(isTouchOnly()) : screen === 'hub' ? hubView(dayIndex, activityIndex, save.unlocked, save.scores) : screen === 'playing' && session ? gameView(session, attract, lastInputType) : session ? resultView(session) : '';\n  root.innerHTML = content + (modal ? modalView(modal, save.preferences) : '');\n  if (screen === 'playing') updateGame();\n  if (modal) root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.modal button, .modal input')?.focus();\n}\nfunction openGame(preview = false): void {\n  if (!preview && isTouchOnly()) { modal = 'touch'; render(); return; }\n  session = createSession(selected(), 13 + flatIndex(dayIndex, activityIndex));\n  attract = preview; screen = 'playing'; modal = null; lastFrame = 0; accumulator = 0;\n  keys.clear(); render();\n}\nfunction finish(): void {\n  if (!session) return;\n  if (attract) { screen = 'welcome'; attract = false; session = null; lastInput = performance.now(); render(); return; }\n  const index = flatIndex(dayIndex, activityIndex);\n  save.scores[session.activity.id] = Math.max(save.scores[session.activity.id] || 0, session.score);\n  save.unlocked = Math.min(totalActivities() - 1, Math.max(save.unlocked, index + 1));\n  persist(); playSound('finish'); screen = 'result'; render();\n}\nfunction updateGame(): void {\n  if (!session) return;\n  const balance = session.balance;\n  const target = targetFor(session);\n  const ball = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#balance-ball');\n  const marker = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#balance-target');\n  if (ball) { ball.style.left = `${50 + balance.x * 40}%`; ball.style.top = `${50 + balance.y * 40}%`; }\n  if (marker) { marker.style.left = `${50 + target.x * 40}%`; marker.style.top = `${50 + target.y * 40}%`; }\n  const timer = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-time');\n  if (timer) { const remaining = Math.max(0, Math.ceil(session.activity.duration - session.time)); timer.textContent = `${Math.floor(remaining / 60)}:${String(remaining % 60).padStart(2, '0')}`; }\n  const cue = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-cue');\n  if (cue) cue.textContent = balance.recovering > 0 ? 'Take a breath. Find your footing.' : target.label || session.cue || 'Find your centre';\n  const score = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-score');\n  if (score) score.textContent = `${Math.round(session.samples ? session.scoreSum / session.samples : 0)}`;\n  const falls = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-falls');\n  if (falls) falls.textContent = String(balance.falls);\n  const progress = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#session-progress');\n  if (progress) progress.style.width = `${Math.min(100, session.time / session.activity.duration * 100)}%`;\n  const person = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.guest-art');\n  if (person) person.style.setProperty('--lean', `${Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, balance.x)) * 11}deg`);\n}\nfunction moveFocus(direction: number): void {\n  const scope = modal ? root.querySelector('.modal') : root;\n  const focusables = Array.from(scope?.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('button:not(:disabled), input:not(:disabled)') || []);\n  if (!focusables.length) return;\n  const current = focusables.indexOf(document.activeElement as HTMLElement);\n  focusables[(current + direction + focusables.length) % focusables.length].focus();\n}\nfunction doFoot(foot: 'left' | 'right' | 'both'): void {\n  if (!session || screen !== 'playing' || modal || attract) return;\n  playSound(action(session, foot) ? 'hit' : 'miss');\n}\nfunction wake(): void {\n  lastInput = performance.now();\n  if (attract) { attract = false; session = null; screen = 'welcome'; render(); }\n}\nroot.addEventListener('click', (event) => {\n  const button = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLElement>('[data-action]');\n  if (!button) return;\n  if (attract) { wake(); return; }\n  wake(); const command = button.dataset.action; playSound('click');\n  if (command === 'begin') { screen = 'hub'; selectFlat(save.unlocked); }\n  else if (command === 'home') { screen = 'welcome'; session = null; }\n  else if (command === 'settings' || command === 'about') modal = command;\n  else if (command === 'close') modal = null;\n  else if (command === 'pause') modal = 'pause';\n  else if (command === 'resume') { modal = null; lastFrame = 0; }\n  else if (command === 'quit') { modal = null; session = null; screen = 'hub'; }\n  else if (command === 'reset') {\n    if (window.confirm('Reset all retreat progress and scores?')) { save = structuredClone(defaults); sounds.enabled = save.preferences.sound; persist(); dayIndex = 0; activityIndex = 0; }\n  } else if (command === 'day') { dayIndex = Number(button.dataset.day); activityIndex = 0; }\n  else if (command === 'activity') activityIndex = Number(button.dataset.index);\n  else if (command === 'start' || command === 'retry') { openGame(); return; }\n  else if (command === 'continue') { screen = 'hub'; session = null; selectFlat(save.unlocked); }\n  render();\n});\nroot.addEventListener('change', (event) => {\n  const input = event.target as HTMLInputElement;\n  const key = input.dataset.preference as keyof Preferences | undefined;\n  if (!key) return;\n  save.preferences[key] = input.checked; sounds.enabled = save.preferences.sound; persist(); render();\n});\nwindow.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n  const key = event.key.toLowerCase();\n  if (attract) { event.preventDefault(); wake(); return; }\n  lastInput = performance.now(); lastInputType = 'keyboard';\n  if (key === 'escape') { event.preventDefault(); if (modal) modal = null; else if (screen === 'playing') modal = 'pause'; render(); return; }\n  if (screen === 'playing' && !modal) {\n    if (['arrowup','arrowdown','arrowleft','arrowright',' ','q','e'].includes(key)) event.preventDefault();\n    keys.add(key);\n    if (!event.repeat && key === 'q') doFoot('left');\n    if (!event.repeat && key === 'e') doFoot('right');\n    if (!event.repeat && key === ' ') doFoot('both');\n  } else if (['arrowup','arrowdown','arrowleft','arrowright'].includes(key)) {\n    event.preventDefault(); moveFocus(key === 'arrowup' || key === 'arrowleft' ? -1 : 1);\n  }\n});\nwindow.addEventListener('keyup', (event) => keys.delete(event.key.toLowerCase()));\nwindow.addEventListener('blur', () => keys.clear());\ndocument.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => { lastFrame = 0; });\nwindow.addEventListener('pointerdown', () => { if (attract) wake(); else lastInput = performance.now(); });\n\nfunction frame(now: number): void {\n  const pad = Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.() || []).find(Boolean);\n  let stickX = 0; let stickY = 0; let gentle = false;\n  if (pad) {\n    stickX = Math.abs(pad.axes[0] || 0) > .13 ? pad.axes[0] : 0;\n    stickY = Math.abs(pad.axes[1] || 0) > .13 ? pad.axes[1] : 0;\n    gentle = !!pad.buttons[7]?.pressed;\n    const buttons = pad.buttons.map((button) => button.pressed);\n    const pressed = (index: number) => buttons[index] && !lastPadButtons[index];\n    if (buttons.some((button, index) => button && !lastPadButtons[index]) || stickX || stickY) {\n      if (attract) wake();\n      lastInput = now; lastInputType = 'controller';\n    }\n    if (pressed(9) || pressed(3)) { if (screen === 'playing') { modal = modal ? null : 'pause'; render(); } }\n    if (screen === 'playing' && !modal) {\n      if (pressed(4)) doFoot('left'); if (pressed(5)) doFoot('right'); if (pressed(0)) doFoot('both');\n    } else {\n      if (pressed(12) || pressed(14)) moveFocus(-1);\n      if (pressed(13) || pressed(15)) moveFocus(1);\n      if (pressed(0)) (document.activeElement as HTMLElement | null)?.click();\n      if (pressed(1) && modal) { modal = null; render(); }\n    }\n    lastPadButtons = buttons;\n  } else lastPadButtons = [];\n  if (screen === 'welcome' && !modal && now - lastInput > 60000) { dayIndex = 0; activityIndex = 0; openGame(true); }\n  if (screen === 'playing' && session && !modal && !document.hidden) {\n    const elapsed = lastFrame ? Math.min((now - lastFrame) / 1000, .1) : 0;\n    accumulator += elapsed;\n    const input = attract ? { x: Math.sin(now / 1800) * .25, y: Math.cos(now / 2400) * .2, gentle: true } : {\n      x: Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, stickX + Number(keys.has('d') || keys.has('arrowright')) - Number(keys.has('a') || keys.has('arrowleft')))),\n      y: Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, stickY + Number(keys.has('s') || keys.has('arrowdown')) - Number(keys.has('w') || keys.has('arrowup')))),\n      gentle: gentle || keys.has('shift'),\n    };\n    const settings = save.preferences.assist ? { ...DEFAULT_BALANCE, gain: DEFAULT_BALANCE.gain * .7, instability: DEFAULT_BALANCE.instability * .7, damping: DEFAULT_BALANCE.damping * 1.3 } : DEFAULT_BALANCE;\n    while (accumulator >= 1 / 60 && !session.finished) { stepSession(session, input, settings, 1 / 60); accumulator -= 1 / 60; }\n    updateGame();\n    if (session.finished) finish();\n  }\n  lastFrame = now; requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\nrender(); requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n\n--- MODAL ---\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-28-  return `<div class=\"site game-site\">${header(attract ? 'A LITTLE PREVIEW' : activity.location.toUpperCase())}<main class=\"game-main\"><div class=\"game-title\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> ${attract ? 'IDLE PREVIEW · ANY INPUT TO RETURN' : 'A MOMENT FOR YOURSELF'}</div><h1>${activity.title}</h1><p>${activity.instruction}</p></div><button class=\"outline-button\" data-action=\"pause\">Ⅱ <span>Pause</span></button></div><div class=\"game-layout\"><section class=\"balance-panel\"><div class=\"panel-label\"><span>YOUR BALANCE</span><span>STAY WITH THE CIRCLE</span></div><div class=\"balance-board\"><div class=\"board-ring ring-outer\"></div><div class=\"board-ring ring-middle\"></div><div class=\"board-ring ring-inner\"></div><div class=\"board-line horizontal\"></div><div class=\"board-line vertical\"></div><div id=\"balance-target\" class=\"balance-target\"></div><div id=\"balance-ball\" class=\"balance-ball\"></div><span class=\"board-letter top\">N</span><span class=\"board-letter bottom\">S</span><span class=\"board-letter left\">W</span><span class=\"board-letter right\">E</span></div><div class=\"session-cue\" id=\"session-cue\">Find your centre</div><div class=\"game-progress\"><div id=\"session-progress\"></div></div><div class=\"board-bottom\"><span>GENTLE DOES IT</span><span>✳</span><span>EVERY WOBBLE COUNTS</span></div></section><aside class=\"session-side\"><div class=\"session-art\"><div class=\"session-sun\"></div><div class=\"guest-art\">${characterArt()}</div><div class=\"island-water\"></div></div><div class=\"session-stats\"><div><small>TIME REMAINING</small><b id=\"session-time\">0:00</b></div><div><small>BALANCE</small><b><span id=\"session-score\">0</span><i> / 100</i></b></div><div><small>STUMBLES</small><b id=\"session-falls\">0</b></div></div><div class=\"how-to\"><b>HOW TO MOVE</b><p>${input === 'controller' ? 'Left stick to lean · R2 for gentle movement · L1 / R1 for feet · ✕ for both' : 'WASD or arrow keys to lean · Shift for gentle movement · Q / E for feet · Space for both'}</p></div></aside></div></main></div>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-29-}\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-30-export function resultView(session: Session): string {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-31-  const rank = rankFor(session.score);\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-32-  return `<div class=\"site result-site\">${header('EXPERIENCE COMPLETE')}<main class=\"result-main\"><div class=\"result-art\">${characterArt()}<span>✳</span></div><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> YOU SHOWED UP. THAT COUNTS.</div><h1>Beautifully <em>done.</em></h1><p>You've completed ${session.activity.title}. Your body may have wandered, but your spirit stayed on the island.</p><div class=\"result-score\"><div><small>YOUR BALANCE SCORE</small><b>${session.score}<i> / 100</i></b></div><div><small>THE ISLAND CALLS YOU</small><b>${rank.name}</b></div><div><small>STUMBLES</small><b>${session.balance.falls}</b></div></div><div class=\"result-actions\"><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"continue\">Continue your stay <span>→</span></button><button class=\"text-button\" data-action=\"retry\">Try this again ↻</button></div></main></div>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-33-}\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts:34:export function modalView(modal: string, preferences: Preferences): string {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-35-  let body = '';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-36-  if (modal === 'settings') {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-37-    const toggle = (key: keyof Preferences, title: string, description: string) => `<label class=\"setting-row\"><span><b>${title}</b><small>${description}</small></span><input type=\"checkbox\" data-preference=\"${key}\" ${preferences[key] ? 'checked' : ''}><span class=\"switch\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></label>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-38-    body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">MAKE YOURSELF COMFORTABLE</div><h2>Retreat settings</h2>${toggle('sound','Sound effects','Little sounds for island moments')}${toggle('motion','Reduce motion','Keep the interface calm and still')}${toggle('contrast','Higher contrast','Make text and controls easier to see')}${toggle('assist','Balance assist','A gentler, more forgiving wobble')}<button class=\"text-button reset\" data-action=\"reset\">Reset saved progress ↺</button>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-39-  } else if (modal === 'pause') body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">TAKE ALL THE TIME YOU NEED</div><h2>Pause for a breath.</h2><p>Your experience will be right here when you're ready.</p><div class=\"modal-actions\"><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"resume\">Resume experience →</button><button class=\"text-button\" data-action=\"quit\">Return to itinerary</button></div>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts:40:  else if (modal === 'touch') body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">ONE SMALL THING</div><h2>Controller or keyboard required.</h2><p>Connect a controller or use a keyboard to take part. The settings and idle preview are still available here.</p><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"close\">Got it →</button>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-41-  else body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">A NOTE FROM THE ISLAND</div><h2>About this retreat</h2><p>Wee Fit Retreat is an original, gentle balance game inspired by the reassuring oddness of fitness games. All illustrations and sound effects were made for this project.</p><p>Explore five days of small activities. Lean towards the target and use your feet when the activity calls for them. Stumbles are invitations to begin again.</p><h3>Controls</h3><p><b>Keyboard:</b> WASD or arrows to lean, Shift for gentle movement, Q / E for left / right foot, Space for both, Esc to pause.<br><b>Controller:</b> left stick to lean, R2 for gentle movement, L1 / R1 for feet, Cross for both, Options to pause. D-pad and Cross navigate menus.</p><h3>Credits &amp; project notes</h3><p>Original code, illustration and synthesized audio created for this game. Built in the provided my-3dge workspace; this edition uses a custom 2D presentation and does not include online multiplayer. Progress is stored locally in your browser.</p><p>Built with Vite and TypeScript. The engine source and project feedback are included with the hand-in.</p>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts:42:  return `<div class=\"modal-backdrop\"><section class=\"modal\" role=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"true\" aria-label=\"${modal === 'about' ? 'About and credits' : modal}\" tabindex=\"-1\"><button class=\"modal-close\" data-action=\"close\" aria-label=\"Close\">×</button>${body}</section></div>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-43-}\n\n--- HUB PLAN ---\n\nRead the protocol once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Fetch by raw URL, into\n`labs/game/hub/`: `session.js` (save it as `session-client.txt`), and for tests `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same\nfolder. **Do not clone the ai-hub repository: it is 5.3 GB.**\n\nWhy ghost: every copy runs its own seeded round, nothing depends on a host, and each player sees the others on the neighbouring mats,\nwobbling in their seat colour. It is the source's solo ritual made social without any interference.\n\n**Tags** in the head, right after the client (the build injects them, section 14):\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Stay the steadiest across three classes\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Lean: stick or WASD · Feet: L2 R2 or Q E · Breathe: both or Space\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n```\n\nGoal at most 60 characters, how-to at most 80. Also `hub:type` Game, `hub:players` 1-4, `hub:source` Wii Fit.\n\n**Startup** **[tested: this shape, on the starter's one scene, passed the harness at 2, 3 (host leaving) and 4 players with the engine running in every frame]**:\n\n```ts\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\nfor (const key of [...search.keys()]) if (key.startsWith('aihub')) search.delete(key); // see the trap below\nsearch.set('touch', 'off');\nconst AIHub = window.AIHub;\nconst info = AIHub?.active ? await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\nif (info) { search.set('scene', 'game:round'); search.set('seed', String(info.seed)); }\nconst watchdog = info ? setTimeout(() => AIHub.ready(), 14000) : 0;   // the harness allows 20 s after hello\nengine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['game:island', 'game:round'], search: `?${search}`, /* … */ });\nif (info) { clearTimeout(watchdog); AIHub.ready(); }\n```\n\n**The biggest trap in this whole plan [tested]:** the hub opens the page with `?aihub=1&aihub-seed=N`. `createEngine` treats every\nunknown query key as a setting and fails with `CORE_BAD_SETTING`, **and the harness still reports PASS**, because the client keeps\nanswering while the game is dead. Strip those keys, and make your test assert, inside every frame, `__engine.ready === true` and\n`__engine.errors.length === 0`.\n\n**The round in a session:**\n\n- No title, menus or attract. Straight to the game's own card: the four mats in the pavilion, Plumb in front, each player standing on their\n  mat. It shows the game's title, players in colour with who is ready, how to win, this player's controls, seconds left (from the `card` event).\n  Keys: Enter or Cross answers `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T answers `'more'`, a tap or click works too. Listen for Enter with your own\n  `keydown` on `window`: the harness sends a synthetic one. The card has no menus or choices, and draws numbers only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n  Make it HTML over whatever is drawn, because the watchdog may call `ready()` while the view is still warming up.\n- `start` arrives; play begins at `AIHub.time() >= 0`. Send the sim `round.go` then (scene action). On `start` also send one\n  `AIHub.progress({ score: 0, label: 'Breathing in' })` and one ghost message, so a slow copy still passes the harness.\n- During play: `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` whenever it changes (label at most 24 characters, \"Class 2 · 640\"), and every 100 ms\n  `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', e: classIndex, x, y, p: poseId, s: score }, { reliable: false })`. Never above 20 a second.\n- Ghosts are sim entities, because only sim entities can be drawn: incoming messages go through\n  `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:ghosts', […])` to actors on the other mats, tinted with `info.players[i].color`, leans scrubbed by their CoB,\n  name labels from the hub as text (never as HTML), shown only while `e` matches. On `leave`, they walk off politely.\n- Finished: `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once. Stats at most six, names at most 16 characters (\"Wobble Age\", \"Best hold\", \"Breath\"),\n  values short; awards at most three, title at most 24, detail at most 40 (\"Unnervingly Still\").\n- `time-up`: report the current score at once if you have not. `end`: `engine.stop()`, stop all sound, take no input, send nothing.\n- If `engine.ready` is false (no WebGPU): `AIHub.fail('WebGPU required')`.\n- **Rules in a session:** network only through the hub; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation; restart\n  and quit do nothing. Pause is an overlay that never pauses the sim: Resume, volume, button icons. No dev mode. **Create + Options belongs to the hub:**\n  while pad button 8 is held, ignore the engine's `pause`. Storage is a fresh memory copy, handled by the client, so write nothing special for it.\n- Outside a session (`connect` gives `null`, or no client at all in the dev server) the game must behave exactly as it does alone.\n\n**Boot deadline, the one place performance matters.** The harness gives every copy 20 s to call `ready()`. **[tested on SwiftShader]** the starter\ngame alone needed 8–16 s per copy at four copies; the engine's playground needed 52–73 s. So `game:round` is a small separate scene with just the\npavilion, the mats and the cast. The island's cost never reaches a session, and the watchdog covers the rest. Performance is out of scope everywhere else.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Art direction\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
