{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_879","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '55,240p' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- PROGRESS ---\\\\n'; cat PROGRESS.md; printf '\\\\n--- ABOUT WIRES ---\\\\n'; rg -n -C 2 'about|About' Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/{main.ts,view.ts,about.ts}\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_879","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '55,240p' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- PROGRESS ---\\\\n'; cat PROGRESS.md; printf '\\\\n--- ABOUT WIRES ---\\\\n'; rg -n -C 2 'about|About' Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/{main.ts,view.ts,about.ts}\"","aggregated_output":"- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n\n### Sharing this computer\n\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\n\n## Goal\n\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\n\nScope\n\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\n\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\n\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\n\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\n\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\n\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\n\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\n\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\n\n## Done\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n\n## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:40:55\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n  }\n}\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n\nTesting Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch?\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n\nEngine Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about the engine?\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n\nPrompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n- What would you change in this prompt?\n\n--- PROGRESS ---\n# Wee Fit Retreat — progress\n\n## Current phase\n\n- The required my-3dge workspace is checked out at `2dbd829`.\n- The standalone `Wee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055.html` builds successfully from `labs/game`.\n- Credits and handoff are drafted; verify the final build and browser behavior.\n\n## Implementation checklist\n\n- [x] Build activity progression, wobble simulation, controls, and local persistence.\n- [x] Add an original 2D island presentation, synthesized effects, and settings.\n- [ ] Investigate 3D engine and AI Hub ghost integration; the current build has neither.\n- [x] Add presentation, synthesized music, accessibility, and developer tools.\n- [ ] Run final headless and cross-viewport/browser checks.\n- [x] Complete the About/credits information and `exit-interview.json`.\n\n## Testing notes\n\n- Initial viewport matrix: 24 screenshots across phone, tablet, desktop, Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit completed without reported overflow or JavaScript errors.\n- Visual inspection found that the welcome action fell below the fold on a landscape phone; responsive layout fix added, pending final verification.\n- Issues caught: at least one. Critical issues: not yet measured.\n\n--- ABOUT WIRES ---\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/about.ts:1:/** @file About, credits and project feedback for the standalone game. */\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/about.ts:2:export function aboutView(): string {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/about.ts:3:  return `<div class=\"modal-backdrop\"><section class=\"modal\" role=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"true\" aria-label=\"About and credits\" tabindex=\"-1\"><button class=\"modal-close\" data-action=\"close\" aria-label=\"Close\">×</button>\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/about.ts:4:    <div class=\"eyebrow\">A NOTE FROM THE ISLAND</div><h2>About this retreat</h2>\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/about.ts-5-    <p>Wee Fit Retreat is an original, gentle balance game inspired by the reassuring oddness of Wii Fit. Explore five days of small activities; stumbles are invitations to begin again.</p>\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/about.ts-6-    <h3>Controls</h3><p><b>Keyboard:</b> WASD or arrows to lean, Shift for gentle movement, Q / E for left / right foot, Space for both, Esc to pause.<br><b>Controller:</b> left stick to lean, R2 for gentle movement, L1 / R1 for feet, Cross for both, Options to pause. D-pad and Cross navigate menus.</p>\n--\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-6-import { Soundscape } from './audio';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-7-import { welcomeView, hubView, gameView, resultView, modalView } from './view';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:8:import { aboutView } from './about';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-9-\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-10-type Screen = 'welcome' | 'hub' | 'playing' | 'result';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:11:type Modal = 'settings' | 'about' | 'pause' | 'touch' | null;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-12-type Preferences = { sound: boolean; motion: boolean; contrast: boolean; assist: boolean };\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-13-type Save = { unlocked: number; scores: Record<string, number>; preferences: Preferences };\n--\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-61-  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('high-contrast', save.preferences.contrast);\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-62-  const content = screen === 'welcome' ? welcomeView(isTouchOnly()) : screen === 'hub' ? hubView(dayIndex, activityIndex, save.unlocked, save.scores) : screen === 'playing' && session ? gameView(session, attract, lastInputType) : session ? resultView(session) : '';\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:63:  root.innerHTML = content + (modal ? (modal === 'about' ? aboutView() : modalView(modal, save.preferences)) : '');\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-64-  if (screen === 'playing') updateGame();\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-65-  if (modal) root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.modal button, .modal input')?.focus();\n--\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-122-  if (command === 'begin') { screen = 'hub'; selectFlat(save.unlocked); }\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-123-  else if (command === 'home') { screen = 'welcome'; session = null; }\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts:124:  else if (command === 'settings' || command === 'about') modal = command;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-125-  else if (command === 'close') modal = null;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/main.ts-126-  else if (command === 'pause') modal = 'pause';\n--\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-10-function duration(seconds: number): string { return `${Math.ceil(seconds / 60)} MIN`; }\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-11-export function welcomeView(touch: boolean): string {\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts:12:  return `<div class=\"site welcome\">${header()}<main class=\"welcome-main\"><div class=\"hero-copy\"><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> A MOST GENTLE ESCAPE</div><h1>Find your<br><em>almost</em> balance.</h1><p>Welcome to a little island where the air is fresh, the hosts are encouraging, and standing still is surprisingly ambitious.</p><div class=\"hero-actions\"><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"begin\">Begin your stay <span>→</span></button><button class=\"text-button\" data-action=\"about\">What is this place? <span>↗</span></button></div>${touch ? '<p class=\"touch-notice\">Controller or keyboard required to play. Settings and the idle preview are available.</p>' : '<div class=\"control-note\"><span class=\"keycap\">↵</span> KEYBOARD &nbsp; OR &nbsp; CONTROLLER FRIENDLY</div>'}</div><div class=\"hero-art\"><div class=\"sun-halo\"></div>${islandArt()}<div class=\"postcard\"><span class=\"postcard-mark\">✳</span><div><b>A slower kind of holiday</b><small>YOUR RETREAT AWAITS</small></div></div><div class=\"art-caption\">EST. SOMEWHERE PEACEFUL &nbsp; · &nbsp; 01 / 05</div></div></main><footer class=\"welcome-footer\"><span>TAKE YOUR TIME. YOU'RE ON ISLAND TIME.</span><button class=\"footer-link\" data-action=\"about\">ABOUT &amp; CREDITS</button></footer></div>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-13-}\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-14-export function hubView(dayIndex: number, activityIndex: number, unlocked: number, scores: Record<string, number>): string {\n--\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-22-    return `<button class=\"activity-row ${index === activityIndex ? 'selected' : ''} ${isLocked ? 'locked' : ''}\" data-action=\"activity\" data-index=\"${index}\" aria-pressed=\"${index === activityIndex}\"><span class=\"activity-number\">${isLocked ? '·' : String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><span class=\"activity-name\"><b>${item.title}</b><small>${item.location} &nbsp; · &nbsp; ${duration(item.duration)}</small></span><span class=\"row-status\">${score !== undefined ? '✓' : isLocked ? 'LOCKED' : '→'}</span></button>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-23-  }).join('');\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts:24:  return `<div class=\"site hub\">${header('YOUR RETREAT PROGRAMME')}<main class=\"hub-main\"><div class=\"hub-heading\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"sun-dot\"></span> MAKE YOURSELF AT HOME</div><h1>Your island <em>itinerary.</em></h1><p>One small wobble at a time. There is no rush.</p></div><div class=\"stay-progress\"><span>YOUR STAY SO FAR</span><b>${String(complete).padStart(2, '0')} <small>experiences enjoyed</small></b></div></div><nav class=\"days\" aria-label=\"Retreat days\">${tabs}</nav><div class=\"hub-grid\"><section class=\"programme\"><div class=\"section-kicker\">DAY ${String(dayIndex + 1).padStart(2, '0')} <span>✳</span> ${day.subtitle}</div><h2>${day.title}</h2><p class=\"day-story\">${day.story}</p><div class=\"activity-list\">${items}</div></section><aside class=\"brief-card\"><div class=\"brief-top\"><span>YOUR NEXT EXPERIENCE</span><span>✳</span></div><div class=\"brief-illustration\">${characterArt()}<span class=\"illustration-sun\"></span></div><div class=\"brief-content\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">${chosen.location} &nbsp; / &nbsp; ${duration(chosen.duration)}</div><h2>${chosen.title}</h2><p>${chosen.description}</p><div class=\"host-quote\">“${chosen.quote}”<small>— ${chosen.host}, YOUR HOST</small></div><button class=\"primary full\" data-action=\"start\" ${locked ? 'disabled' : ''}>${locked ? 'Complete earlier experiences' : scores[chosen.id] !== undefined ? 'Enjoy again' : 'Start experience'} <span>→</span></button></div></aside></div></main><footer class=\"inner-footer\"><span>✳ &nbsp; THE ISLAND IS HAPPY YOU'RE HERE</span><button class=\"footer-link\" data-action=\"about\">ABOUT &amp; CREDITS</button></footer></div>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-25-}\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-26-export function gameView(session: Session, attract: boolean, input: 'keyboard' | 'controller'): string {\n--\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-39-  } else if (modal === 'pause') body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">TAKE ALL THE TIME YOU NEED</div><h2>Pause for a breath.</h2><p>Your experience will be right here when you're ready.</p><div class=\"modal-actions\"><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"resume\">Resume experience →</button><button class=\"text-button\" data-action=\"quit\">Return to itinerary</button></div>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-40-  else if (modal === 'touch') body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">ONE SMALL THING</div><h2>Controller or keyboard required.</h2><p>Connect a controller or use a keyboard to take part. The settings and idle preview are still available here.</p><button class=\"primary\" data-action=\"close\">Got it →</button>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts:41:  else body = `<div class=\"eyebrow\">A NOTE FROM THE ISLAND</div><h2>About this retreat</h2><p>Wee Fit Retreat is an original, gentle balance game inspired by the reassuring oddness of fitness games. All illustrations and sound effects were made for this project.</p><p>Explore five days of small activities. Lean towards the target and use your feet when the activity calls for them. Stumbles are invitations to begin again.</p><h3>Controls</h3><p><b>Keyboard:</b> WASD or arrows to lean, Shift for gentle movement, Q / E for left / right foot, Space for both, Esc to pause.<br><b>Controller:</b> left stick to lean, R2 for gentle movement, L1 / R1 for feet, Cross for both, Options to pause. D-pad and Cross navigate menus.</p><h3>Credits &amp; project notes</h3><p>Original code, illustration and synthesized audio created for this game. Built in the provided my-3dge workspace; this edition uses a custom 2D presentation and does not include online multiplayer. Progress is stored locally in your browser.</p><p>Built with Vite and TypeScript. The engine source and project feedback are included with the hand-in.</p>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts:42:  return `<div class=\"modal-backdrop\"><section class=\"modal\" role=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"true\" aria-label=\"${modal === 'about' ? 'About and credits' : modal}\" tabindex=\"-1\"><button class=\"modal-close\" data-action=\"close\" aria-label=\"Close\">×</button>${body}</section></div>`;\nWee-Fit-Retreat-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-224055/labs/game/view.ts-43-}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
